  <para style="h">Esikeel</para>
  <para style="toc1">Esikeel</para>
  <para style="toc2">Esikeel</para>
  <para style="toc3">Esi</para>
  <para style="mt1">Esikeel</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="EZK 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ntọọñọ Ñkukịd Esikeel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 1:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua edịb mme duob mmi, ke ayọhọ usen ition ke ayọhọ afiọñ inaañ, ke ini ami ñkebaaha ye mbon ekebịneke esio ke idʌñ Isrel ke mben Inyañ Keba, mme hefịn emaebeere ndin ami mmaakịt mme ñkukịd e-etooho Abasi.<verse eid="EZK 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 1:2" />Ke ayọhọ usen ition ke afiọñ ado, akedo ayọhọ isua ition tọọñọ nte ekeben Adidem Yehoiyakịn esio ke idʌñ, <verse eid="EZK 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 1:3" />uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadisịm aku Esikeel, ayịn Busi, ke mben Inyañ Keba ke isọñ Babilọn. Do ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadoro anye ke idem.<verse eid="EZK 1:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 1:4" />Ami mmaase, ndin ami mmaakịt ayobio naña ato adoro asọiyọ adi, ekandịk ntọñanyọñ ye amịneñmịneñ akebkeb, ñyayamma unwana anyʌñ akanna anye akʌk. Ufọọd ikañ ado akeba nte nsem-nsem ukwak, <verse eid="EZK 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 1:5" />ndin se ikiba nte aduuwem ñkpọ inaañ ekesịne ke esịd ikañ ado. Ke ndañkịd ammọ ekebit awo, <verse eid="EZK 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 1:6" />ado ammọ keedekeed emaenie iso inaañ ye mba inaañ. <verse eid="EZK 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 1:7" />Ukod ammọ ekedo nnen-nnen; ñkpad ammọ ekeba nte ake ñyịn enañ ndin ammọ emaesem nte brọns e-etʌkkọtʌk. <verse eid="EZK 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 1:8" />Ammọ emaenie ubọk awo ke idak mba ammọ ke naña ñkañ ammọ inaañ. Afịd ammọ inaañ emaenie iso ye mba, <verse eid="EZK 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 1:9" />ndin mba keed amaatuuk emọ-emọ mba. Ammọ keedekeed ekesaña nnen-nnen; ikiwọññọke iso ke ini ammọ esañake.<verse eid="EZK 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 1:10" />Iso ammọ ekeba ntom: Ammọ naña inaañ ekenie iso awo, ndin ke ñkañ ubọk nnasia ammọ keedekeed emaenie iso ekpe, ndin ke ufiin ammọ ekenie iso abaakenañ; ammọ keedekeed emaenyʌñ enie iso ntrukpuum. <verse eid="EZK 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 1:11" />Naña iso ammọ ekeba adodo. Ammọ keedekeed emaenie mba se ikitara ika anyọñ, etuuk mba emọ-emọ ke naña ñkañ iba; ndin ammọ keedekeed emaenie mba iba mfen se ikifʌk ammọ idem. <verse eid="EZK 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 1:12" />Ammọ keedekeed ekeneenen iso esaña. Itie akeedodo a-sịbidịd akpekekaaha, ammọ ekeka kpa do, iwọññọke iso ndomokeed. <verse eid="EZK 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 1:13" />Mme aduuwem ñkpọ ami ekeba nte mme ukañ e-esakka ikañ me nte mme ikañ emuum. Ikañ ado amaasak adọọk anyʌñ asak asọiyọ ke ufọọd mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado; anye amaayamma, ndin akebkeb amaakeppe awuọ ke esịd ikañ ado. <verse eid="EZK 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 1:14" />Mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado ekedo efeeñe eka iso efeeñe eka edem nte akebkeb amịneñ.<verse eid="EZK 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 1:15" />Naña ami ñkesʌkkọ nse mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado, ami mmaakịt wiil ke isọñ nte ana ke ñkañ mme aduuwem ñkpọ ami keedekeed, ammọ keedekeed emaenieñe iso inaañ. <verse eid="EZK 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 1:16" />Mme wiil ado ekeba ntom: Ammọ ekesem nte topas, ndin afịd ammọ inaañ ekeba ukem-ukem. Ammọ keedekeed ekeba nte wiil e-enamma esịn ke ufọọd wiil mfen. <verse eid="EZK 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 1:17" />Nte mme wiil ado ekesañake, ammọ ekekeene usʌñ keed ke atu mfọk inaañ se mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado ekesak iso ese; mme wiil ado ikikappake idʌk usʌñ mfen nte mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado ekesañake. <verse eid="EZK 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 1:18" />Mme rim ammọ emaekoñ enyʌñ enie uteeñe, ndin afịd rim inaañ ado emaenie anyen ekanna ekʌk.<verse eid="EZK 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 1:19" />Ke ini mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado ekesañake, mme wiil ado emaesaña ammọ ke ñkañ; ndin mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado emaedakka ekpọñ isọñ, mme wiil ado ñko emaenyʌñ edakka ekpọñ isọñ. <verse eid="EZK 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 1:20" />Itie keed akeedodo a-sịbidịd akekaha, ammọ emaekaa do, ndin mme wiil ado emaenyʌñ esaña edọọk ye ammọ, sia sịbidịd mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado mmọ akesịne ke mme wiil ado. <verse eid="EZK 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 1:21" />Ke ini mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado ekedakkake isañ, ammọ ñko emaenyʌñ edakka isañ; mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado emaeketuak eda, ammọ ñko emaenyʌñ etuak eda; ndin mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado emaedakka ke isọñ, mme wiil ado ñko emaenyʌñ edakka ke isọñ ye ammọ, sia sịbidịd mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado mmọdo akesịne ke mme wiil ado.<verse eid="EZK 1:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 1:22" />Ñkpọ a-abaaha nte ntotəño ñkpọ, asem nte kristal, amaatara akwe mme aduuwem ñkpọ ami, anyʌñ anie uteeñe. <verse eid="EZK 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 1:23" />Ke idak ntotəño abaitiad ado ammọ emaetat mba ammọ nọ enen eketuuk emọ-emọ, ndin ammọ keedekeed emaenie mba iba-iba e-ekefʌkkọ ammọ idem. <verse eid="EZK 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 1:24" />Ke ini mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado emaekedakka isañ, ami mmaakop uyom mba ammọ, afịt nte uyom mmọọñ a-afeghekefeghe, nte uyio Andikponñkan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ado </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Sadai</char></note>, nte aditịm udịmekọñ. Ke ammọ emaeketuak eda, ammọ emaesuuk mba ammọ ke isọñ.<verse eid="EZK 1:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 1:25" />Ndin uyio amaawuọ ato anyọñ ntotəño ñkpọ ado ke anyọñ iwuod ammọ naña ammọ edaaha esuuk mba ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 1:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 1:26" />Ke anyọñ akọm ado ke anyọñ iwuod ammọ, ñkpọ amaaba nte ebekpo e-ekedatta nsọñudua itiad a-asịneke bru ke esịd enam, ndin ke anyọñ ebekpo ado ñkpọ a-abaaha nte awo amaadoro. <verse eid="EZK 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 1:27" />Ami mmaakịt ke tọọñọ ke itie a-abaaha nte isịn amọ dọọk ke anye akeba nte ukwak e-efọppọ ke ikañ, nte akpedo ikañ ayọhọ ke esịd, ndin ke tọọñọ do suuhọ anye akeba nte ikañ; ñyayamma ikañ amaanyʌñ akanna anye akʌk. <verse eid="EZK 1:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 1:28" />Kpa naña adʌkabasi awuọ ada ke abubịd anyọñ ke usen edịm, kpa ntoro ke uyamma a-akekannake anye akʌk akeba.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 1:28">Ami akedo mbid ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ke ini ami ñkekịtte anye, ami mmaaduọ ñkʌp iso ke isọñ, ndin ami mmaakop uyio awo nte atañ ikọ.<verse eid="EZK 1:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="EZK 2" />
  <para style="s1">Ikood Esikeel nte Prọfed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 2:1" />Anye amambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, dakka da ke ukod mfo, ndin ami ñyaatañ ikọ unọ fiin.” <verse eid="EZK 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 2:2" />Nte anye akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ, Sịbidịd amandʌk miin idem anyʌñ andịppe adaaha ke ukod, ndin ami mmaakop naña anye atañ ikọ ye ami.<verse eid="EZK 2:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 2:3" />Anye amaabo ate: “Ayịn awo, ami ñyaudọñ fiin utom nnọ nditọ Isrel, nnọ idịd nsọñiwuod e-esọññọ iwuod ye ami; ammọ ye mme eteete ammọ emaedakka eda ikọ ye ami tutu awuọ idem usen mfịn ami. <verse eid="EZK 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 2:4" />Mbon se ami udọñ fiin utom nnọ esọñ iwuod enyʌñ etre utọñ. Bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ado ami.’ <verse eid="EZK 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 2:5" />Ndin me ammọ ekpañ utọñ me ikpañña, sia ammọ edo mbon nsọñiwuod, ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke prọfed mmọdo ke atu ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 2:6" />Ndin afo, ayịn awo, kuufeghe ammọ me ikọ ammọ. Kuukop ndịk, akpesʌkado akpab ye ñkukịm ebaaha ukanna fiin ekʌk ndin afo anyʌñ adʌñ ke atu mme ikpeyen. Kuukop ndịk ubaña se ammọ etañ, ñko kuunyʌñ udịkke ubaña ammọ, akpesʌkado ammọ edooho mbon nsọñiwuod. <verse eid="EZK 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 2:7" />Ana afo atañ ikọ mmi anọ ammọ, me ammọ ekpañ utọñ me ikpañña, sia ammọ e-esọñ iwuod. <verse eid="EZK 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 2:8" />Ado amaado afo, ayịn awo, kpañ utọñ kop se ami ntañ unọọ fiin. Kuusọñ iwuod nte mbon nsọñiwuod ado; kʌppọ inua mfo nyʌñ dia se ami unọọ fiin.”<verse eid="EZK 2:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 2:9" />Ndin ami mmaase, ñnyʌñ ñkịt ubọk keed nte anyanna anọ utịd mmi. Ubọk ado amaakama ikpañwed, <verse eid="EZK 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 2:10" />a-anye aketatta ke iso mmi. Emaewet mme ikọ aseeme ye ntuaña ye mfʌhọ ke naña edem ikpañwed iba.<verse eid="EZK 2:10" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="EZK 3" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 3:1" />Ndin anye amambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, ta se unaa fiin ke iso, ta ikpañwed ami; ndin kaa ketañ ikọ nọ nditọ Isrel.” <verse eid="EZK 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 3:2" />Ntom ke ami ñkekʌppọ inua mmi, ndin anye amannọ miin ikpañwed ado nọ nta.<verse eid="EZK 3:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 3:3" />Ndin anye amambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, ta ikpañwed a-ami unọọhọ fiin mi nọ uyọhọ fiin idịb.” Ndin ami mmaata anye, ndin anye amaanịññe nte adanakwọọk ke inua mmi.<verse eid="EZK 3:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 3:4" />Ndin anye amambo miin ate: “Ayịn awo, kaa ndin bịne nditọ Isrel idahami nyʌñ ketañ ikọ mmi nọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 3:5" />Awo udọññọ fiin nọ aka abịne mbon ndukpakka ikọ ye asen usem, ado udọñ nọ abịne nditọ Isrel; <verse eid="EZK 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 3:6" />awo udọññọ fiin ibo aka abịne uwak mbon ndukpakka ikọ ye asen usem, i-ikọ ammọ imuunwañake fiin, nọ afo umuukoppo se ammọ etañ. Ke akpanikọ akpedo ñkudọñ fiin utom nnọ ammọ, ammọ ekpaekekpañ utọñ unọ fiin. <verse eid="EZK 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 3:7" />Ado nditọ Isrel ibeeñeke idem adikpañ utọñ unọọ fiin sia ammọ ibeeñeke idem adikpañ utọñ innọọ miin, sia afịd nditọ Isrel esọñ esịd enyʌñ esọñ iwuod. <verse eid="EZK 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 3:8" />Ado ami ñyaanam afo asọñ ido anyʌñ asọñesịd nte ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 3:9" />Ami ñyaanam akpọiso mfo aba nte itiad se isọọñ ikan, asọọñ akan itiadikañ. Kuubaak ammọ, kuunyʌñ udịkke ke ntak ammọ, akpesʌkado a-ammọ edooho mbon nsọñiwuod.”<verse eid="EZK 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 3:10" />Ndin anye amambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, nekke kpañ utọñ nyʌñ ben afịd ikọ se ntañ unọ fiin sịn ke esịd mfo. <verse eid="EZK 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 3:11" />Kaa idahami bịne mbon mfo se eketañ efep ke abio nyʌñ ketañ ikọ nọ ammọ. Bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ado ami,’ me ammọ ekpañ utọñ me ikpañña.”<verse eid="EZK 3:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 3:12" />Akem Sịbidịd amambenne miin ke anyọñ, ndin ami mmaakop akpọsọñ uyom ke edem mmi nte ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akedakkake ke itie a-anye akedaaha. <verse eid="EZK 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 3:13" />Akedo uyom mme mba mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado ekedutuaiya ye uyom mme wiil ado ke ñkañ ammọ, ataa akpọsọñ uyom. <verse eid="EZK 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 3:14" />Sịbidịd ado ndin amambenne miin ke anyọñ anyʌñ aben adakka, ndin ami mmaadakka ñkaa ye idiọọkesịd ye iyadesịd sịbidịd mmi, akpọsọñ ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanyʌñ andoro miin ke idem. <verse eid="EZK 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 3:15" />Ami mmaadisịm mbon eketañña efep ke abio, e-ekedʌññọ ke Tel Afif akpere Inyañ Keba. Ndin do, ke itie a-ammọ ekedʌññọ, ami mmaatie ke atu ammọ usen itiaba ke ataa mbʌññọ esịd.<verse eid="EZK 3:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Utom Esikeel nte Awoukpeme</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 3:16" />Ke utịd usen itiaba ado, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 3:17" />“Ayịn awo, ami mmunịm fiin nte awoukpeme nnọ mbon Isrel; ke ntoro kop ikọ se ami ntañ nyʌñ dat ado dʌt ammọ utọñ. <verse eid="EZK 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 3:18" />Ke ini ami mbooho awo ibak, ‘Ke akpanikọ afo uduutreke adikpa,’ ndin afo udʌttọ ammọ utọñ, unyʌññọ usio uyio nọ ammọ esịññe idem ekpọñ idiọọk usʌñ ammọ, nọ ato do enịm uwem ammọ, idiọọk awo ado ayaakpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ amọ, ndin ami ñyaayem iyiib ammọ nto ubọk mfo. <verse eid="EZK 3:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 3:19" />Ado adieke afo adʌttọ awo ibak utọñ, ndin ammọ ikpọññọ ibak uwem me ndiọi usʌñ ammọ, ammọ eyaekpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ammọ; ado afo ayaanyaaña idem mfo.”<verse eid="EZK 3:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 3:20" />“Ñko, adinen awo amaawuọ akpọñ usʌñ eti ido ammọ anyʌñ anam idiọọk, ndin ami mben ñkpọ iduọ nnịm ammọ ke iso, ammọ eyaekpa. Sia afo umuunọọhọ ammọ item, ammọ eyaekpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ammọ. Awo idiitoiyoke ndinen ñkpọ a-awo ado akenamma, ndin ami ñyaayem iyiib ammọ nto ubọk mfo. <verse eid="EZK 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 3:21" />Ado adieke afo anọọhọ adinen awo item ate ke anam idiọọkñkpọ ndin anye inyʌññọ inam idiọọkñkpọ, ke akpanikọ ammọ eyaedu uwem sia ammọ emaekop item, ndin afo ayaanyʌñ anyaaña idem mfo.”<verse eid="EZK 3:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 3:22" />Ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amandoro miin ke idem do, ndin anye amambo miin ate, “Dakka da, wuọ kaa unaisọñ, ndin ami ñyaatañ ikọ unọ fiin do.” <verse eid="EZK 3:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 3:23" />Ndin ami mmaadakka nda ñnyʌñ ñwuọ ñka unaisọñ. Ndin ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmọdo akeda do, nte utọ ubọọñ ami ñkekịtte ke mben Inyañ Keba, ndin ami mmaaduọ ñkʌp iso ke isọñ.<verse eid="EZK 3:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 3:24" />Ndin Sịbidịd amandʌk miin idem anyʌñ ambenne miin adaaha ke ukod. Anye amaatañ ikọ ye ami ate: “Kaa, yịt usʌñ sịn idem mfo ke ufọk mfo. <verse eid="EZK 3:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 3:25" />Ndin afo, ayịn awo, eyaubọp ke udʌk; eyaubọp mbaak afo udukan uwuọ udʌk atu awo. <verse eid="EZK 3:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 3:26" />Ami ñyaanam edeme mfo adiana ke nsịñ mfo mbaak afo adop uyio, mbaak afo udunyʌñ unọọ ammọ ikpan sia ammọ edo mbon nsọñiwuod. <verse eid="EZK 3:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 3:27" />Ado ami mmaatañ ikọ ye afo, ami ñyaukʌppọ fiin inua ndin afo ayaabo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami.’ Awo akeedodo a-adiikpañ utọñ yak ammọ ekpañ utọñ, ñko awo akeedodo a-adiisịn adikpañ utọñ yak asịn; sia ammọ edo mbon nsọñiwuod.<verse eid="EZK 3:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="EZK 4" />
  <para style="s1">Naña Ukanna Yeruselem Ñkʌk Adiiba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 4:1" />“Idahami, ayịn awo, dat itiad aduañ keed, nịm anye ke iso mfo nyʌñ nam nduud abio Yeruselem ke idem amọ. <verse eid="EZK 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 4:2" />Ndin kanna anye kʌk: Daaha atañ kanna anye kʌk, bọp akọ nọ adọọk akesịm anye, wuuk mme nnaaekọñ kanna anye nyʌñ bon ñkpọ uwuut ndibene kanna anye. <verse eid="EZK 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 4:3" />Ndin dat ako ukwak ufrañ ñkpọ, nịm nte ndibene ukwak ke ufọọd mfo ye abio ado nyʌñ wọññọ iso mfo se anye. Eyaekanna abio ado ekʌk, ndin afo ñko ayaakanna anye akʌk. Ami adiido idiọọñọ inọ mbon Isrel.<verse eid="EZK 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 4:4" />“Umauma, naa ke ñkañ ubọk ufiin mfo nyʌñ ben idiọọkñkpọ ufọk Isrel dot ke idem mfo. Afo anie adibiom idiọọkñkpọ ammọ ke adaña ibad usen se afo anaa ke ñkañ mfo. <verse eid="EZK 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 4:5" />Ami mmunọ fiin ukem ibad usen asañake akekem ye ibad isua se ammọ ekenam idiọọkñkpọ. Ke ntoro afo ayaabiom idiọọkñkpọ ufọk Isrel ke usen ikie ita mme anaañ mme duob (390).<verse eid="EZK 4:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 4:6" />“Ke afo umaukweeñe ami, maana suuk naa, isañ anyem naa ke ñkañ ubọk nnasia, nyʌñ biom idiọọkñkpọ ufọk Yuda. Ami mmunọ fiin usen aba (40) adinam ntoro, usen keed ada anọ isua keed. <verse eid="EZK 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 4:7" />Kanna iso mfo wọt Yeruselem e-emaekekanna ekʌk nyʌñ tat ubọk mfo nyan tañ prọfesi baña anye. <verse eid="EZK 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 4:8" />Ami ñyaubọp fiin ke udʌk mbaak afo udukan ukanna idem tutu afo akweeñe mme usen ubiọọñọ mfo.<verse eid="EZK 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 4:9" />“Dat abakpa ye baali, akọti ye nsama, miled ye speel; dọñ ammọ ke ikịm keed nyʌñ kama ammọ nam uyo nọ idem mfo. Afo anie adita uyo ado ke usen ikie ita mme anaañ mme duob (390) a-afo anaaha ke ñkañ mfo. <verse eid="EZK 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 4:10" />Domo ndidia sekel edịb<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kram 230.</char></note> sio se afo uduudia ke usen ke usen nyʌñ dia anye ke akem ini. <verse eid="EZK 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 4:11" />Ñko domo mmọọñ mbaak hin keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte lita 0.6.</char></note> ke itie itiokeed nyʌñ nwọñ anye ke akem ini. <verse eid="EZK 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 4:12" />Dia ndidia ado nte akpediaha efiak uyo baali keed; sañ anye ke iso mbon awo, kama uduañ awo bara ikañ.” <verse eid="EZK 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 4:13" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo, “Ke utọ usʌñ ami ke nditọ Isrel ediidia ndedeghe ndidia ke atu mme idịd se ami ndiibịn ammọ ndọñ.”<verse eid="EZK 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 4:14" />Ndin ami mmaabo nte, “Idooho ntoro, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara! Akenam ami nsappake idem mmi. Tọọñọ ke uyịn mmi tutu idahami akenam ami ndiaha ñkpaikpa ñkpọ me se unam ikọd awot. Akenam ndedeghe unam ndomokeed idʌkkọ inua mmi.”<verse eid="EZK 4:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 4:15" />Anye amaabo ate, “Afọn, ami ñyaanam afo akama uduañ enañ asañ uyo mfo utu ke akama uduañ awo.”<verse eid="EZK 4:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 4:16" />Anye ndin amambo miin ate: “Ayịn awo, ami ñyem adisuuhọ ibad ndidia se iba ke Yeruselem. Mme awo ediidia udodomo ndidia ke ñnyeñidem enyʌñ enwọñ udodomo mmọọñ ke iduọesịd, <verse eid="EZK 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 4:17" />sia ndidia ye mmọọñ eyaenana. Idem ayaanekke akpa ammọ abaña keed ye aken enyʌñ etak eto ke idiọọkñkpọ ammọ.”<verse eid="EZK 4:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="EZK 5" />
  <para style="s1">Akadañ Ubiereikpe Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 5:1" />“Idahami, ayịn awo, dat akañkañ se isọp nyʌñ kama nte akadañ afadided fat ided iwuod mfo nyʌñ kwaat ñwaebek mfo. Umauma ado dat udomoñkpọ bakka ided ado. <verse eid="EZK 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 5:2" />Ini ubiọọñọ mfo amaakweeñe, fọp mbakka keed ke itie ita ided ado ke esịd abio. Ben mbakka keed ke itie ita mfen mia ke akañkañ kanna afịd abio. Ndin suan akpatre mbakka keed ke itie ita nọ afịm. Sia ami ñyaasio akañkañ mbịne ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 5:3" />Ado sio ñkpọ nte idem ided ifañ faak ke afọñidem mfo. <verse eid="EZK 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 5:4" />Ñko, dat usʌk ke atu ami top dọñ ke ikañ nyʌñ fọp ammọ. Ikañ ayaato do atara awuọ afịd Isrel.”<verse eid="EZK 5:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 5:5" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ado ami: Ami ado Yeruselem, a-ami nnịmme ke ufọọd mme idịd, ndin mme abio ekanna anye ekʌk. <verse eid="EZK 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 5:6" />Ado ke ido ibak amọ anye amaatre utọñ abaña mme mbed ye mme ewʌhọ mmi akan mme idịd ye mme abio e-ekannake anye ekʌk. Anye asịn mme mbed mmi inyʌññọ ikeene mme ewʌhọ mmi.<verse eid="EZK 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 5:7" />“Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Afo ameba mfịna-mfịna akan mme idịd u-ukannake fiin ekʌk unyʌññọ ukeene mme ewʌhọ mmi me adinịm mme mbed mmi. Afo udʌkkọdʌk uda ke ndaha mme idịd u-ukannake fiin ekʌk.”<verse eid="EZK 5:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 5:8" />“Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ado ami: Ami ke idem mmi mmenam ikọ ye afo, Yeruselem, ndin ami ñyaumia fiin ufen ke iso mme idịd. <verse eid="EZK 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 5:9" />Ke ntak afịd mme mbubiam ubobodñkpọ mfo, ami ñyaunam fiin se akenaanam ami nnamma, a-mme ndiinyʌññọ nnanam. <verse eid="EZK 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 5:10" />Ke ntoro, mme ete ye mme eka eyaeta nditọ ammọ ke ufọọd mfo, nditọ ñko eyaenyʌñ eta mme ete ye mme eka ammọ. Ami ñyaunọ fiin ufen ñnyʌñ nsuan afịd nsʌhọ mfo nsịn ke afịm. <verse eid="EZK 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 5:11" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ate, ke ntoro maama uwem mmi, sia afo ameben afịd ndedeghe mbid ñkpọ mfo ye mme mbubiam adinam mfo asappa adisana itieukpono mmi, ami ke idem mmi ñyaukpooño fiin; ami nduukoppo fiin udʌk ndiinyʌññọ usaana fiin ñyaak. <verse eid="EZK 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 5:12" />Mbakka keed ke itie ita mbon mfo eyaekpañña ke udọñọ nsobo me ke akañ ke esịd abio mfo; akañkañ ayaasobo mbakka keed ke itie ita mfen ke edem abio mfo; ñyaanyʌñ nsuan mbakka keed ke itie ita asʌhọke ndọñ ke afịm ñnyʌñ nsio akañkañ mbịne ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 5:13" />“Ndin iyadesịd mmi ayaatre, ifiobesịd a-ami ñkenieghe nnọ ammọ ayaanyʌñ asuuhọ, ndin ayaado ke ami mmesio ammọ usiene. Ndin ke ini ami mmaakenwañña ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk ammọ mma, ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ntañ ikọ ye akpọsọñ udọñ.<verse eid="EZK 5:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 5:14" />“Ami ñyaunam fiin ado ñkpọ nsobo ye ñkpọ asuenne ke atu mme idịd u-ukannake fiin ekʌk, ke anyen afịd mbon se isaña iboiyo. <verse eid="EZK 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 5:15" />Afo ayaado ñkpọ asuenne ye ñkpọ nsaha, ñkpọ nnọ item ye ñkpọ ndịk anọ mme idịd se ukanna fiin ikʌk ke ini ami mmaumia fiin ufen ke iyadesịd ye ifiobesịd ye akpọsọñ nduaiya. Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ntañ. <verse eid="EZK 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 5:16" />Ke ini ami mmautop fiin ke ndiọi idañ nsobo akañ mmi, ami ndiitop nọ ato do usobo fiin. Ami ñyaanam akañ anenekke aba ye afo ñnyʌñ ñkpịkke usʌñ ndidia mfo nsio. <verse eid="EZK 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 5:17" />Ami ñyaadọñ akañ ye ndiọi unam ikọd unọ fiin, ndin ammọ eyaenam afo anana nditọ. Idiọọk udọñọ nsobo ye uduọk iyiib eyaubeen fiin, ami ñyaanyʌñ usobo fiin ke akañkañ. Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ntañ.”<verse eid="EZK 5:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="EZK 6" />
  <para style="s1">Nsobo mme Ikpọabod Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 6:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 6:2" />“Ayịn awo, kappa iso mfo se mme ikpọabod Isrel; tañ prọfesi baña ammọ <verse eid="EZK 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 6:3" />nyʌñ bo ate: ‘Ndufo mme ikpọabod Isrel, ikop uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara. Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ anọ mme ikpọabod ye ntək abod, mme abedeñ ye itịkke ado ami: Ami ñyem adisio akañkañ ibịne ndufo, ñnyʌñ nsobo mme ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 6:4" />Eyaewuut mme akpokoro uwa ndufo enyʌñ enuak mme akpokoro uwa insensi ndufo; ndin ami ñyaawoot mbon mfo ke iso mme ubobodñkpọ ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 6:5" />Ami ñyaabon mme akpo nditọ Isrel ke iso ubobodñkpọ ammọ, ami ñyaanyʌñ nsuan mme akpọ ndufo ñkanna mme akpokoro uwa ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 6:6" />Nte ndufo edọdʌñ, eyaenam mme abio ado enaa ukpọk enyʌñ ewuut mme ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie ndufo, nọ ato do mme akpokoro uwa ndufo ena ukpọk, enuak enyʌñ ebiat mme ubobodñkpọ ndufo, ebom mme akpokoro uwa insensi ndufo, enyʌñ esọọk utom ndufo efep. <verse eid="EZK 6:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 6:7" />Mbon ndufo eyaekpañña afai ke atu ndufo, ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="EZK 6:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 6:8" />“ ‘Ado ami ñyaasʌhọ ubaak, sia ubaak ndufo eyaebọkkọ akañkañ ke ini emaisuan ndufo ke atu mme abio ye mme idịd. <verse eid="EZK 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 6:9" />Ndin ke mme idịd se eketañ ammọ ekebon nte mbon ñkpakọb, mbon se ikibọkkọ eyaentoiyo miin; naña mme esịd efịbe ammọ enam nọ ami mfʌhọ, e-emaekewọññọ eñkpọñ miin, anyen ammọ ñko, e-enamma use ye mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ enyʌñ ekeene enam ami mfʌhọ. Ammọ eyaesua idem ammọ ke ntak ibak se ammọ enam ye afịd mbubiam ido ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 6:10" />Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; idooho ke ikpu-ikpu ke ami ñkebo ke ñyaanam ammọ idiọọkñkpọ ami.<verse eid="EZK 6:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 6:11" />“ ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ben ubọk mfo iba mia nyʌñ tọ ukod mfo ke isọñ nyʌñ bọñ ñkpo bo “Sai!” ke ntak afịd ibak ye mbubiam ido nditọ Isrel, sia ammọ eyaekpañña ke akañkañ, ke akañ ye ke udọñọ nsobo. <verse eid="EZK 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 6:12" />Andiba ke anyan usʌñ ayaakpa ke udọñọ nsobo, akañkañ ayaanyʌñ asobo andiba ke ñkpere usʌñ, ndin awo akeedodo a-abọkkọke adiikpa ke akañ. Ntom ke ami ndiinwañña iyadesịd mmi mfʌk ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 6:13" />Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini mbon ammọ emaekpañña ena ke atu ubobodñkpọ ammọ e-enaaha ekanna mme akpokoro uwa ammọ ekʌk, ke afịd ñkoñ-ñkoñ abod ye ke afịd atịñe ikpọabod, ke idak afịd eto se itiañña ñkọk ye afịd eto afriyo se ibañña mfañ-mfañ, mme itie se ammọ ekesifọp anemufịk insensi enọ afịd mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 6:14" />Ndin ami ñyaanyanna ubọk mmi ntuuk ammọ ñnyʌñ nnam isọñ ado ado ndoon tọọñọ ke akpautatan tutu asịm Dibla<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ataa uwak mme ikpañwed Hibru ewet Dibla; ado ibad-ibad mme ikpañwed Hibru ewet Ribla</char></note>, itie akeedodo a-ammọ edʌññọ. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 6:14" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="EZK 7" />
  <para style="s1">Utịd Adisịm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 7:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 7:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 7:2" />“Ayịn awo, se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara adọkkọ isọñ Isrel ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:2">“ ‘Utịd! Utịd adisịm</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:2">naña mbeñ isọñ inaañ!<verse eid="EZK 7:2" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 7:3" />Utịd adusịm fiin ndin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:3">ami ñyaanyʌñ ñnwañña iyadesịd mmi ufʌk fiin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:3">Ami ñyaakpe ikpe mfo ñkeene adinam mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:3">ñnyʌñ ukpe fiin utịb afịd mme mbubiam ido mfo.<verse eid="EZK 7:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 7:4" />Ami nduuseeghe fiin ye mbọm;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:4">Ami nduuyaaha fiin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:4">Ke akpanikọ ñyaukpe fiin utịb adinam mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:4">ye utịb mme mbubiam ido ke atu ndufo.’ ”</para>
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 7:4">“ ‘Ndin afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 7:4" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 7:5" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:5">“ ‘Idiọọk unọmọ! Idiọọk unọmọ a-adooho akenam awo ikoppo!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:5">Se, anye adi!<verse eid="EZK 7:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 7:6" />Utịd adi!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:6">Utịd adi!</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:6">Anye adịppe idem amọ ukọp fiin.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:6">Se, anye adi<verse eid="EZK 7:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 7:7" />Nsobo adusịm fiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:7">afo a-adʌññọ ke isọñ ado.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:7">Ini adikem! Usen akpere!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:7">Ñnyeñidem aba ke mme ikpọabod, idooho idaara.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 7:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 7:8" />Ami ñyaanwañña ifiobesịd mmi ufʌk fiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:8">ñnyʌñ mben iyadesịd mmi ufʌk fiin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:8">Ami ñyaakpe ikpe mfo ñkeene adinam mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:8">ñnyʌñ ukpe fiin utịb ke afịd mme mbubiam ido mfo.<verse eid="EZK 7:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 7:9" />Ami nduuseeghe fiin ye mbọm;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:9">ami nduuyaaha fiin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:9">Ami ñyaukpe fiin utịb adinam mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:9">ye utịb mme mbubiam ido ke atu ndufo.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 7:9" />
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 7:9">“ ‘Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ado ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> imia ndufo.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 7:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 7:10" />“ ‘Se, usen ado!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:10">Se, usen ado adi!</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:10">Nsobo atop awuọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:10">esañ aseghe,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:10">ntañidem aseghe!<verse eid="EZK 7:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 7:11" />Afai asakka,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:11">esañ adimia awo ibak ufen.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:11">Awo ammọ ndomokeed idiisʌhọke,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:11">ndomokeed ke atu mme awo ado,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:11">inie ammọ ndomokeed,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:11">ñkpọ ndomokeed se ibaba ufọn.<verse eid="EZK 7:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 7:12" />Ini adi!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:12">Usen adikem!</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:12">Yak andideb akuudaara,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:12">andinyam ñko akuufʌhọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:12">sia ifiobesịd mmi adoro afịd atu awo ke idem.<verse eid="EZK 7:12" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 7:13" />Andinyam idiimaanake ibọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:13">ñkpọ se anye amaakenyam,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:13">adaña ini nte andideb ye andinyam ebaaha ke uwem.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:13">Sia ñkukịd a-abañake afịd atu awo ado</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:13">idiimaanake iwọññọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:13">Ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ammọ, awo ammọ ndomokeed</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:13">idiinieghe uwem amọ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 7:13" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 7:14" />“Ammọ efịt adukpoñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:14">ammọ ebeeñe afịd ñkpọ ebono,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:14">ado awo ndomokeed idiikaaha ekọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:14">sia ifiobesịd mmi adoro afịd atu awo ke idem.<verse eid="EZK 7:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 7:15" />Akañkañ mmọdo ke esiin;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:15">udọñọ nsobo ye akañ eba ke esịd abio.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:15">Mbon se iba ke abioinwañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:15">eyaekpa ke akañkañ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:15">mbon se iba ke esịd abio</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:15">akañ ye udọñọ nsobo eyaewot ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 7:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 7:16" />Mbon e-ebọkkọke</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:16">eyaefeghe ekaa mme ikpọabod.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:16">Nte mme ibiom e-edʌññọ ke abedeñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:16">afịd ammọ eyaekuun,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:16">ebaña mme idiọọkñkpọ ammọ keedekeed.<verse eid="EZK 7:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 7:17" />Afịd ubọk ayaatọ atekke;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:17">afịd ukod ayaadeññe enọ ikịm.<verse eid="EZK 7:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 7:18" />Ammọ eyaesiine afọñikpo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:18">ndịk anyʌñ ado afọñ a-afʌkkọ ammọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:18">Abuud ayaafʌk afịd iso awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:18">ndin eyaekwaat afịd iwuod awo.”<verse eid="EZK 7:18" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 7:19" />“Ammọ eyaetoomo silfa ammọ eduọñọ ke mme usʌñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">ediinyʌñ idat kold ammọ nte ndedeghe ñkpọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:19">Silfa ye kold ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">idiikanna inyaaña ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">ke usen ifiobesịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:19">Anye idiisuuho ammọ abiọọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">idiinyʌññọ iyọhọ ammọ idịb,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">sia anye anam nọ ammọ eduọ edʌk idiọọkñkpọ.<verse eid="EZK 7:19" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 7:20" />Ammọ emaenam iseri ebaña mfọọn ñkpọ mbanaidem ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:20">enyʌñ ekama enam mbubiam ubobodñkpọ ammọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:20">Ammọ emaeben enam mme ndiọi mbid ñkpọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:20">ke ntoro ami ñyaanam anye ado ndedeghe ñkpọ anọ ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 7:20" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 7:21" />Ami ñyaaben inie ammọ nnọ isenawo nte ndubịme,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:21">ñnyʌñ nnọ mbon ibak ederimbod nte ñkpọ mbịme,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:21">ammọ eyaesappa anye.<verse eid="EZK 7:21" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 7:22" />Ami ñyaawọññọ iso mmi ñkpọñ mbon awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:22">ndin mme amauke eyaesappa itie a-ami mmaaha.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:22">Ammọ eyaeboiyo edʌk</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:22">enyʌñ esappa anye.<verse eid="EZK 7:22" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 7:23" />“ ‘Ibeeñe ñkpọnọ ibono!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:23">Sia isọñ ayọhọ ye uduọkiyiib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:23">abio anyʌñ ayọhọ ye afai.<verse eid="EZK 7:23" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 7:24" />Ami ñyaaben idịd se ibak ibak ikan</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:24">nọ ediben mme ufọk ammọ enie.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:24">Ami ñyaatre ntañidem ñkpọsọñ awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:24">ndin eyaesappa mme ndisana itie ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 7:24" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 7:25" />Nsobo amaadi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:25">ammọ eyaeyem emem ado idiikịtte.<verse eid="EZK 7:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 7:26" />Idiọọk unọmọ ayaadi amaana adi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:26">ñko nsu-nsu etob ayaawuọ amaana awuọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:26">Ammọ eyaesaaña eyem ñkukịd eto prọfed,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:26">item mbed aku ayaanyʌñ atre,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:26">item mme ñkpisọñ ayaatre.<verse eid="EZK 7:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 7:27" />Adidem ayaafʌhọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:27">akpanabọọñ ayaasịne mfʌhọ nte afọñidem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:27">ndin ubọk mbon abio eyaenyeñ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:27">Ami ñyaanam ammọ naña asaña akekem ye ido ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:27">ñnyʌñ ñkpe ikpe ammọ ñkeene mme ndaha ammọ.’ ”</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 7:27" />
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 7:27">“Idaha ado ke ammọ ediidiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="EZK 7:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="EZK 8" />
  <para style="s1">Mbubiam ke Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 8:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua itiokeed, ke ayọhọ afiọñ itiokeed ke ayọhọ usen ition, ke ini ami ñketieghe ke ufọk mmi ndin mme ñkpisọñ ke Yuda enyʌñ etie ke iso mmi, ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara amandoro miin ke idem. <verse eid="EZK 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 8:2" />Ami mmaase, ñnyʌñ ñkịt ñkpọ keed nte mbid awo. Tọọñọ ke itie se ikiba nte isịn amọ sọiyọ anye akeba nte ikañ, ndin tọọñọ do dọọk mbid amọ amaayamma nte ukwak e-efọppọ ke ikañ. <verse eid="EZK 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 8:3" />Anye amaasio ñkpọ a-akebaaha nte ubọk anyan anyʌñ ammʌm miin ke ided iwuod mmi. Sịbidịd amambenne miin adaaha ufuum ke ufọọd isọñ ye anyọñ, ndin ke mme ñkukịd Abasi anye amamben miin akaa Yeruselem, ke ntondʌk inuaatob adoro esịd-esịd akwere, ke itie u-ubobodñkpọ a-anamma nọ Abasi afịbe ufịb akedaaha. <verse eid="EZK 8:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 8:4" />Ndin do ke iso mmi ke ubọọñ Abasi Isrel akeda, naña ami ñkekịt ke ñkukịd ke unaisọñ ado.<verse eid="EZK 8:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 8:5" />Akem anye amaambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, se ke ukañ adoro.” Ndin ami mmaase, ndin ke ntondʌk ukañ adoro inuaatob akpokoro uwa ami mmaakịt ubobodñkpọ a-anamma nọ Abasi afịbe ufịb.<verse eid="EZK 8:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 8:6" />Ndin anye amaambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, nte afo amekịt se ammọ enam, mme ataa mbubiam ñkpọ a-nditọ Isrel enamma mi, mme ñkpọ se idimbịn miin isio ke adisana itie mmi? Ado afo ayaakịt mme mbubiam ñkpọ se idọdiọọk ikan ado.”<verse eid="EZK 8:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 8:7" />Ndin anye amaamben miin adi inuaatob akwere. Ami mmaase, ñnyʌñ ñkịt adudu ke ndibene. <verse eid="EZK 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 8:8" />Anye amaambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, dọk ndibene ado idahami.” Ndin ami mmaadọk ndibene ñnyʌñ ñkịt usʌñ keed do.<verse eid="EZK 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 8:9" />Ndin anye amaambo miin ate, “Dʌk kaa kekịt mme ibak ye mbubiam ñkpọ se ammọ enañña mi.” <verse eid="EZK 8:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 8:10" />Ndin ami mmaadʌk ñnyʌñ ñkese, ndin ami mmaakịt naña ekap afịd utọ ñkpọ se inyọnyọọn ye mme ndedeghe unam ye afịd ubobodñkpọ Isrel ke afịd ndibene ado. <verse eid="EZK 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 8:11" />Ñkpisọñ Isrel ata mme duob (70) emaeda ammọ ke iso, ndin Yaasania ayịn Safan amaanyʌñ ada ke atu ammọ. Ammọ keedekeed emaekama sensa ke ubọk, ndin anem ufịk insensi amaadọọk ke anyọñ nte nsʌñikañ.<verse eid="EZK 8:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 8:12" />Anye amaambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, afo amekịt se mme ñkpisọñ Isrel enam ke akịm, awo keedekeed ke ñwommo ubobodñkpọ amọ? Ammọ ebo ete, ‘<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikịtte ñnyịn; <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adakka akpọñ isọñ ami.’ ” <verse eid="EZK 8:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 8:13" />Anye amaamaana abo, “Afo ayaakịt ammọ naña enam mme mbubiam ñkpọ se idọdiọọk ikan ado.”<verse eid="EZK 8:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 8:14" />Ndin anye amaamben miin akaa ntondʌk inuaatob ukañ adoro ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin ami mmañkịt ibaan naña etie do, esʌk efʌhọ ebaña abasi Tamuus. <verse eid="EZK 8:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 8:15" />Anye ambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, nte afo amekịt ami? Afo ayaakịt mme mbubiam ñkpọ se idọdiọọk ikan ami.”<verse eid="EZK 8:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 8:16" />Ndin anye amaamben miin adʌk ataa esịd-esịd akwere ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin do ke ntondʌk tembịd, ke ufọọd esa ye akpokoro uwa, ñkpọ nte ideen edịb mme ition emaeda. Ammọ emaekpaedem ewọt tembịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enyʌñ esak iso ese ukañ usakkautịn, etuak iwuod enọ ayio ke ukañ usakkautịn.<verse eid="EZK 8:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 8:17" />Anye amaambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, nte afo amekịt ami? Me ado etək ñkpọ ufọk Yuda adinam mme mbubiam ñkpọ a-ammọ enamma mi? Me ana ammọ eyọhọ isọñ ami ye afai enyʌñ ekaiso eñyat miin esịd? Se ammọ naña eben ñkọk edian ke iwuo ammọ! <verse eid="EZK 8:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 8:18" />Ke ntoro ami ñyaanam ammọ ñkpọ ke iyadesịd; ami ndiiseeghe ammọ ke mbọm, ndiinyʌññọ ñyaak ammọ. Akpekọm ammọ ebọñ ñkpo ke utọñ mmi, ami ndiikpañña utọñ nnọ ammọ.”<verse eid="EZK 8:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="EZK 9" />
  <para style="s1">Ubiereikpe Nnọọ Mme Akpono Ndem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 9:1" />Ndin ami mmaakop naña anye akoot ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, “Nam nọ mbon se emek ebo yak ekpe ikpe abio ado esaña ekpere, ammọ keedekeed ekama ñkpọ ekọñ ammọ ke ubọk.” <verse eid="EZK 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 9:2" />Ndin ami mmaakịt ideen itiokeed nte eto ñkañ adoro-adoro inuaatob, a-aseeghe adoro edi, afịd ammọ keedekeed ekaama aniendịk ñkpọekọñ ke ubọk. Awodeen keed a-akesịneke afọñidem linen anyʌñ akama ñkpọ uwedñkpọ ke ñkañ amọ amaasaña ye ammọ. Ammọ emaedʌk edida ke ñkañ akpokoro uwa brọns.<verse eid="EZK 9:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 9:3" />Ndin ubọọñ Abasi Isrel amaadọọk akpọñ serubim, itie a-anye akedoroke, akaa inuausʌñ tembịd. Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakoot awodeen a-akesịneke afọñidem linen anyʌñ akama ñkpọ uwedñkpọ ke ñkañ. <verse eid="EZK 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 9:4" />Abọọñ amaabo anye ate, “Saña dʌk afịd abio Yeruselem nyʌñ nịm idiọọñọ ke akpọiso mbon se ifʌhọ inyʌñ iseeme ibaña afịd mme mbubiam ñkpọ se enam ke esịd amọ.”<verse eid="EZK 9:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 9:5" />Nte ami ñkekpañña utọñ, anye amaabo mbon ako ate, “Ikeene anye isaña afịd abio inyʌñ iwot, ikiitua awo mbọm, ikiikop awo udʌk. <verse eid="EZK 9:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 9:6" />Iwot ñkaan ideen, ñkparawa ye ubọikpa, mme eka ye ntəkayịn, ado ikiituuk awo ndomokeed a-anieghe idiọọñọ ado. Itọọñọ ke adisana itie mmi.” Ndin ammọ emaetọọñọ ye ñkaan ideen e-ekebaaha ke iso tembịd.<verse eid="EZK 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 9:7" />Akem anye amaabo ammọ ate, “Isappa tembịd inyʌñ iwot awo iyọhọ akwere amọ. Ikaa!” Ndin ammọ emaewuọñọ eketọọñọ adiwoot mme awo ke afịd abio. <verse eid="EZK 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 9:8" />Idaha a-ammọ ekesʌkkọ ewot awo nọ ami mba ikpọọñ, ami mmaaduọ ñkʌp iso ke isọñ, ñnyʌñ ntua nte, “Sai, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara! Afo ayem adisobo afịd ñyọhọnsʌhọ ufọk Isrel ke adinwañña ifiobesịd mfo mfʌk Yeruselem?”<verse eid="EZK 9:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 9:9" />Anye amambọọrọ miin ate, “Idiọọkñkpọ mbon Isrel ye Yuda akpon abọhọ; iyiib ayọyọhọ isọñ ami ndin ukwañ ikpe ayọhọ abio. Ammọ ebo ete, ‘<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adakka akpọñ isọñ ami; <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikịtte.’ <verse eid="EZK 9:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 9:10" />Ke ntoro ami ndiituaha ammọ mbọm, ndiinyʌññọ ñyaak ammọ, ado ñyaaben se ammọ ekenam ndot ammọ ke iwuod.”<verse eid="EZK 9:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 9:11" />Ndin awo a-akesịneke afọñidem linen akama ñkpọ uwedñkpọ ke ñkañ amaaben etob anyọñ adi, ate, “Ami mmenam naña afo akenọọ uyio abo yak nnam.”<verse eid="EZK 9:11" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="EZK 10" />
  <para style="s1">Ubọọñ Abasi Akpọñ Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 10:1" />Ami mmaase, ndin mmaakịt mbid ebekpo nsọñudua itiad ke anyọñ a-akedoroke mme serubim ke iwuod. <verse eid="EZK 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 10:2" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo awodeen a-akesịneke afọñ linen ate, “Dʌk kaa ke ufọọd mme wiil a-asịneke ke idak mme serubim. Woppo eboho ikañ ke ufọọd mme serubim nọ uyọhọ ubọk nyʌñ ben ammọ ke suan ke abio.” Nte ami ñkesʌkkọ nse, anye amaadʌk akaa.<verse eid="EZK 10:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 10:3" />Idahami mme serubim ekeda ke edem usuuk tembịd ini a-awodeen ado akedʌkkọ aka, ndin ntọñanyọñ amaayọhọ ataa esịd-esịd akwere. <verse eid="EZK 10:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 10:4" />Akem ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadakka ke anyọñ serubim ado akaa inuausʌñ tembịd. Ntọñanyọñ amaayọhọ tembịd, ndin uyamma ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayọhọ akwere. <verse eid="EZK 10:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 10:5" />Ekeme aditie ke akwere esiin ekop uyio serubim ke anyan usʌñ, nte ekop uyio Abasi Andikponñkan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Hibru Abasi Andikponñkan ado El-Sadai</char></note> ke ini anye atañña ikọ.<verse eid="EZK 10:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 10:6" />Ke ini <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akenọọhọ awodeen a-akesịneke linen do ewʌhọ ate, “Dappa ikañ ke ufọọd mme wiil ado, ke atu mme serubim,” awodeen ado amaadʌk akeda ke ñkañ wiil keed. <verse eid="EZK 10:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 10:7" />Ndin keed ke atu mme serubim ado amaanyanna ubọk atuuk ikañ a-akebaaha ke atu ammọ. Anye amaasio ubaak ebok ikañ asịn ke ubọk awodeen a-akesịneke afọñ linen, ndin anye amaabọ aben awuọ. <verse eid="EZK 10:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 10:8" />(Emaekeme adikịt mbid ubọk awo ke idak mba mme serubim ado.)<verse eid="EZK 10:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 10:9" />Ami mmaase, ndin mmaakịt wiil inaañ ke ñkañ serubim, keed ke ñkañ serubim keedekeed; mme wiil ado ekesem nte itiad topas. <verse eid="EZK 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 10:10" />Amaado naña ammọ ekeba, naña ammọ inaañ ekeba ukem-ukem; ammọ keedekeed ekeba naña wiil akpeba ke ufọọd wiil. <verse eid="EZK 10:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 10:11" />Nte ammọ ekesañake eka, ammọ emaekeme edika ñkañ keed akeedodo a-mme serubim ado ekewọññọke iso ewọt; mme wiil ado ikiwọññọke naña mme serubim ado esañake eka. Mme serubim ado ekeka ubeñ nte iwuod ammọ akewọt, iwọññọke ke ini ammọ esañake. <verse eid="EZK 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 10:12" />Anyen akeyọọyọhọ afịd idem ammọ, ye edem ammọ, mme ubọk ye mme mba ammọ, kpa naña akeyọhọ wiil ammọ naña inaañ. <verse eid="EZK 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 10:13" />Ami mmaakop naña ekekoot mme wiil ado “mme ukakanna wiil.” <verse eid="EZK 10:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 10:14" />Mme serubim ado keedekeed ekenieñe iso inaañ: Iso keed akedo iso serub, ayọhọ iso iba akedo iso awo, ayọhọ iso ita ado iso ekpe, ndin ayọhọ iso inaañ ado iso ntrukpuum.<verse eid="EZK 10:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 10:15" />Akem mme serubim emaedakka edọọk anyọñ. Mbon ami edo mme aduuwem ñkpọ a-ami ñkekịtte ke mben Inyañ Keba. <verse eid="EZK 10:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 10:16" />Ke ini mme serubim ado ekedakkake isañ, mme wiil ado ke ñkañ ammọ emaenyʌñ edakka isañ; ndin mme serubim eketat mba ammọ adidakka ñkpọñ isọñ, mme wiil ado ikikpọññọ ñkañ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 10:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 10:17" />Ke ini mme serubim ado eketuakka eda, ammọ emaenyʌñ etuak eda; ndin ke ini mme serubim ekedakkake edọọk, ammọ emaedakka edọọk ñko ye ammọ, sia sịbidịd mme aduuwem ñkpọ ado mmọdo akeba ammọ ke idem.<verse eid="EZK 10:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 10:18" />Ndin ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadakka akpọñ inuausʌñ tembịd anyʌñ akeda ke anyọñ mme serubim. <verse eid="EZK 10:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 10:19" />Nte ami ñkesʌkkọ nse, mme serubim ado emaetat mba ammọ enyʌñ edakka ekpọñ isọñ, ndin nte ammọ ekaaha, mme wiil ado emaekaa ye ammọ. Ammọ emaekeda ke ntondʌk inuaatob ukañ edem usakkautịn ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin ubọọñ Abasi Isrel amaaba ke anyọñ ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 10:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 10:20" />Mbon ami ekedo mme aduuwem ñkpọ a-ami ñkekịtte ke idak Abasi Isrel ke mben Inyañ Keba, ndin ami mmaadiọọñọ mbo ke ammọ edo mme serubim. <verse eid="EZK 10:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 10:21" />Ammọ keedekeed ekenie iso inaañ ye mba inaañ, ndin mbid ubọk awo aba ke idak mba ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 10:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 10:22" />Iso ammọ ekeba ukem nte mbon a-ami ñkekịtte ke mben Inyañ Keba. Ammọ keedekeed emaenen iso ammọ esaña nnen-nnen.<verse eid="EZK 10:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="EZK 11" />
  <para style="s1">Ubiomikpe Abasi ke Abaña Yeruselem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 11:1" />Akem Sịbidịd amambenne miin ke anyọñ anyʌñ amben akewuọ inuaatob ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> a-asakkaiso ase usakkautịn. Do ke ntondʌk inuaatob ado ideen edịb mme ition emaeba, ndin ami mmaakịt Yaasania ayịn Asọọ ye Pelatia ayịn Benaiya, mme adadusʌñ ke abio, ke atu ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 11:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 11:2" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amambo miin ate, “Ayịn awo, mbon ado edo ideen e-eduakka idiọọk ye mbon se inọ idiọọk item ke abio ami. <verse eid="EZK 11:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 11:3" />Ammọ ebo ete, ‘Nte idooho mmi-mmi ke ekemaana ebọọp mme ufọk ñnyịn? Abio ami ado ako, ñnyịn inyʌñ ido unam ke esịd amọ.’ <verse eid="EZK 11:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 11:4" />Ke ntoro tañ prọfesi dian ammọ; tañ prọfesi, ayịn awo.”<verse eid="EZK 11:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 11:5" />Akem Sịbidịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaandoro miin ke idem, anyʌñ ambo miin yak mbo nte: “Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ ado ami: Se ndufo etañ ado ami, ndufo mme adadusʌñ ke Isrel, ado ami mmediọọñọ se isịne ndufo ke esịd. <verse eid="EZK 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 11:6" />Ndufo emewot uwak awo ke abio ami enyʌñ enam mme efaak eyọhọ ye akpo awo.<verse eid="EZK 11:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 11:7" />“Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Mme akpo awo a-ndufo etoomoke eduọñọ do edo unam ndin abio ami ado ako, ado ami ñyaibịn ndufo nsio ke esịd. <verse eid="EZK 11:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 11:8" />Ndufo ebaabaak akañkañ, ndin akañkañ ke ami ndiiben ikeene ndufo, ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 11:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 11:9" />Ami ñyaibịn ndufo nsio ke abio ami, ñnyʌñ iyaak ndufo nsịn ke ubọk mme isenawo, ñnyʌñ inọ ndufo ufen. <verse eid="EZK 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 11:10" />Ndufo eyaeduọññọ ke akañkañ, ndin ami ñyaakpe ikpe ndufo ke mme adaña Isrel. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 11:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 11:11" />Abio ami idiidooho ako inọ ndufo, ndufo ñko idiidooho unam ke esịd amọ; ami ñyaakpe ikpe ndufo ke mme adaña Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 11:12" />Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, sia ndufo ikeeneke mme ewʌhọ mmi inyʌññọ inịm mme mbed mmi, ado enam ñkpọ ekeene ido mme idịd i-ikannake ndufo ekʌk.”<verse eid="EZK 11:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 11:13" />Idaha a-ami ñkesʌkkọ ntañ prọfesi, Pelatia ayịn Benaiya amaakpa. Ndin ami mmanduọ ñkʌp iso ke isọñ ñnyʌñ ntua ke akpọsọñ uyio nte, “Sai, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara! Nte afo ayaasobo ñyọhọnsʌhọ ufọk Isrel?”<verse eid="EZK 11:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Enwọñọ Adiben Isrel Ntịmme Ñnyọñ Ndi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 11:14" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 11:15" />“Ayịn awo, mbon Yeruselem etañ ntom ebaña mme emọ-emọ mbon ekebịneke esio ke idʌñ ye afịd nditọ Isrel mfen, ‘Ammọ enyọọñ usʌñ ekpọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; ekinọ ñnyịn isọñ ami nte unen udeeme ñnyịn.’<verse eid="EZK 11:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 11:16" />“Ke ntoro bo ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Akpesʌkado a-ami ñkebịnne ammọ ñka anyan usʌñ ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ nsuan ammọ ke atu mme abio, ado ke etək ini ami mmedo itie udịbe nnọ ammọ ke mme abio a-ammọ ekaaha.’<verse eid="EZK 11:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 11:17" />“Ke ntoro bo ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaikoono ndufo ke mme idịd ñnyʌñ iben ndufo ñnyọñ ndi ke mme abio e-ekisuanna ndufo, ndin ami ñyaamaana ñkpọñ isọñ Isrel inọ ndufo.’<verse eid="EZK 11:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 11:18" />“Ammọ eyaetịmme enyọñ edi do edisịññe afịd ndedeghe mbid ñkpọ ye mme mbubiam ubobodñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 11:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 11:19" />Ami ñyaanọ ammọ esịd keed ñnyʌñ nsịn ammọ ufa sịbidịd ke idem; ami ñyaasio ammọ esịd itiad ñnyʌñ nsịn ammọ esịd abʌk. <verse eid="EZK 11:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 11:20" />Ndin ammọ eyaekeene mme ewʌhọ mmi enyʌñ ekpeme edinịm mme mbed mmi. Ammọ eyaedo ikọd mmi, ami ñyaanyʌñ ndo Abasi ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 11:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 11:21" />Ado amaado mbon esịnne esịd ammọ ke ndedeghe mbid ñkpọ ye mme mbubiam ubobodñkpọ ammọ, ami ñyaaben se ammọ enam ndot ammọ ke iwuod, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 11:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 11:22" />Ndin mme serubim, ye mme wiil ke ñkañ ammọ, emaetat mba ammọ, ndin ubọọñ Abasi Isrel amaadoro ke anyọñ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 11:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 11:23" />Ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadakka ke esịd abio aketuak ada ke anyọñ ekamba abod a-abaaha ke edem usakkautịn abio. <verse eid="EZK 11:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 11:24" />Sịbidịd amandịppe miin aben akesuuk anọ mbon eketañña esio ke idʌñ ekoono ekaa Babilọn ke ñkukịd a-Sịbidịd Abasi akenọọhọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 11:24">Akem ñkukịd a-ami ñkekịtte amañkpọñ miin, <verse eid="EZK 11:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 11:25" />ndin ami mmaadọkkọ mbon eketañña esio ke idʌñ afịd ñkpọ se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akeñwọt miin.<verse eid="EZK 11:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="EZK 12" />
  <para style="s1">Idiọọñọ Ubịne Awo Nsio ke Idʌñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 12:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 12:2" />“Ayịn awo, afo adʌñ ke atu mbon nsọñiwuod. Ammọ enie anyen adikịt ñkpọ ado ikịtte enyʌñ enie utọñ adikop ñkpọ ado ikoppo, sia ammọ edo mbon nsọñiwuod.<verse eid="EZK 12:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 12:3" />“Ke ntoro, ayịn awo, tañ ñkpoduoho mfo nyʌñ beeñe idem adiwuọ ke idʌñ ndin yak ado ke uweemeayio, naña ammọ esʌkkọ ese, wuọ ke idʌñ nte afo aba nyʌñ kaa itie mfen. Akemeido ayaanwaña ammọ, akpesʌkado ammọ edooho mbon nsọñiwuod. <verse eid="EZK 12:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 12:4" />Ke uweemeayio, nte ammọ esʌkkọ ese, sịññe ñkpoduoho mfo a-afo umaukubeeñe unịm adiwuọ ke idʌñ bon. Ndin amaado ndubiayio, naña ammọ esʌkkọ ese, wuọ nte mbon ebịneke esio ke idʌñ. <verse eid="EZK 12:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 12:5" />Idaha a-ammọ esʌkkọ ese, dọk adudu ke ndibene nyʌñ ben ñkpoduoho mfo saña do wuọ. <verse eid="EZK 12:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 12:6" />Dot ammọ ke afara idaha ammọ esʌkkọ ese do nyʌñ wuọ ke ayio amaatọọñọ idịp awo idem. Fʌk iso mfo mbaak udukịt isọñ, sia ami mmuunịm fiin nte ñkpọ idiọọñọ nnọ ufọk Isrel.”<verse eid="EZK 12:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 12:7" />Ndin ami mmaanam naña ekentemme. Akedo uweemeayio ami mmaasịññe ñkpoduoho mmi a-mmaakebọọp nnịm adiwuọ ke idʌñ. Ndin akedo ndubiayio ami mmaadat ubọk mmi ndọk ndibene. Ami mmaaben ñkpoduoho mmi nsio naña ayio atọọñọke adidịp awo idem, mbiom ammọ ke afara mmi idaha ammọ ekesʌkkọ ense.<verse eid="EZK 12:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 12:8" />Ke ubakusen ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin abo ate: <verse eid="EZK 12:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 12:9" />“Ayịn awo, nte nditọ Isrel, mbon nsọñiwuod ado, ikubịppe fiin ibo, ‘Nsoo ke afo anam?’<verse eid="EZK 12:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 12:10" />“Bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Prọfesi ami abaña akpanabọọñ ke Yeruselem ye afịd mbon Isrel e-ebaaha do.’ <verse eid="EZK 12:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 12:11" />Bo ammọ ate, ‘Ami ndo ñkpọ idiọọñọ inọ ndufo.’</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 12:11">“Kpa naña ami nnam, ntoro ke ediinam ye ammọ. Eyaetañ ammọ esio ke idʌñ nte mbon ñkpakọb.<verse eid="EZK 12:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 12:12" />“Andido akpanabọọñ ke atu ammọ ayaadot ñkpọ amọ ke afara ke ini ayio adịppe awo idem awuọ, ndin eyaetịppe adudu ke ndibene enọ anye nọ asaña awuọ. Anye ayaafʌk iso amọ mbaak anye adikịt isọñ. <verse eid="EZK 12:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 12:13" />Ami ñyaatat iyịre mmi nnịm nnọ anye, ndin afia mmi ayaamʌm anye; ami ñyaaben anye ndi Babilọn, isọñ mme Saaldiin, ado anye idiikịtte isọñ ado, ndin anye ayaakpa do. <verse eid="EZK 12:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 12:14" />Ami ñyaasuan afịd mbon se ikanna anye ikʌk ndọñ ke mme afịm, mbon utom amọ ye afịd mbon ekọñ amọ, ami ñyaanyʌñ nsio akañkañ mbịne ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 12:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 12:15" />“Ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini ami mmaasuan ammọ ndọñ ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ nsuan ammọ ñyọhọ afịd idịd. <verse eid="EZK 12:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 12:16" />Ado ñyaafak usʌk ammọ mfep ke akañkañ, akañ ye udọñọ nsobo, nọ ato do ke mme idịd se ammọ eka ammọ ebʌk ebaña afịd mbubiam adinam ammọ. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="EZK 12:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 12:17" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 12:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 12:18" />“Ayịn awo, yak idem unyeñ fiin idaha a-afo adiaha ndidia mfo, nyʌñ kop ndịk idaha a-afo anwọññọ mmọọñ. <verse eid="EZK 12:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 12:19" />Dọkkọ mbon idʌñ ado ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ abaña mbon se idʌñ ke Yeruselem ye ke isọñ Isrel ado ami: Ammọ ediidia ndidia ammọ ke iduọesịd enyʌñ enwọñ mmọọñ ammọ ke ayeemensia, sia eyaebọ ammọ afịd ñkpọ se iba ke isọñ ammọ ke ntak afai uwem afịd mbon e-edʌñọke do. <verse eid="EZK 12:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 12:20" />Eyaenam mme abio a-mme awo edʌñọke ekappa ndoon ndin isọñ ado ayaanaa ukpọk. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 12:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ubiadini Idiibaaha</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 12:21" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 12:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 12:22" />“Ayịn awo, nsoo ñke ke ndufo etop ami ke isọñ Isrel: ‘Usen asʌk aboiyo ndin mme ñkukịd iwuọhọ isu’? <verse eid="EZK 12:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 12:23" />Bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaanam nọ ñke ami atre, ndin ammọ idiitoppo anye aba ke Isrel.’ Bo ammọ ate, ‘Mme usen akpere a-afịd ñkukịd adiiwuọ isu. <verse eid="EZK 12:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 12:24" />Sia ndomo nsu-nsu ñkukịd me nneminua idiọñ ndomokeed idiibaaha aba ke atu ufọk Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 12:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 12:25" />Ado ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñyaatañ se ndiinam, ndin ayaawuọ asu ubiadini ibaaha. Sia ke ayio ndufo, ndufo mbon nsọñiwuod, ami ñyaanam se adodo a-ami ntañña yak asu, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 12:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 12:26" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 12:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 12:27" />“Ayịn awo, mbon Isrel esʌk ebo ete, ‘Ñkukịd se anye akịt ado se idiidat uwak isua adisu, ñko anye atañ prọfesi abaña anyan ini ke iso.’<verse eid="EZK 12:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 12:28" />“Ke ntoro bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ikọ mmi ndomokeed idiikpeeneke aba adiwuọ nsu; se adodo a-ami ntañña ayaawuọ asu, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 12:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="EZK 13" />
  <para style="s1">Esua Enọ mme Nsu-Nsu Prọfed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 13:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 13:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 13:2" />“Ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi baña mme prọfed Isrel e-esʌkkọ etañ prọfesi idahami. Dọkkọ mbon e-etañña prọfesi a-atooho udọñ esịd ammọ: ‘Ikop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>! <verse eid="EZK 13:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 13:3" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Adọdiọọk anọ mme ndisịme<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ibak</char></note> prọfed e-ekeeneke sịbidịd idem ammọ inyʌññọ ikịt ñkpọ ndomokeed! <verse eid="EZK 13:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 13:4" />Isrel, mme prọfed mfo eba nte mme ewaikọd ke atu mme mbiaña ñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 13:5" />Ndufo idọọhọ ika mme adudu ndibene ikidiọñ anye inọ ufọk Isrel mbaak ammọ esọọñọ eda ke ekọñ ke usen <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 13:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 13:6" />Mme ñkukịd ammọ edo abiaña, idiọñ ammọ enyʌñ edo nsu. Akpesʌkado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikiidọññọ ammọ, ammọ ete, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ,” ndin enie idodanyen ke akpena anye anam ikọ se ammọ etañ awuọ asu. <verse eid="EZK 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 13:7" />Nte ndufo ikịtte nsu-nsu ñkukịd inyʌññọ ibre abiaña-abiaña idiọñ ke ndufo emaebo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ,” akpesʌkado ami mmentañña?<verse eid="EZK 13:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 13:8" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke ntak mme ikọ abiaña ye nsu-nsu ñkukịd ndufo, ami mmenam ikọ ye ndufo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 13:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 13:9" />Ubọk mmi ayaadoro mme prọfed e-ekịtte nsu-nsu ñkukịd enyʌñ ebre abiaña-abiaña idiọñ. Ammọ idiisịneke ke esob ikọd mmi, awo idiinyʌññọ iwet anyịñ ammọ isịn ke ñwed ufọk Isrel, ammọ idiinyʌññọ idʌk isọñ Isrel. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara.<verse eid="EZK 13:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 13:10" />“ ‘Sia ammọ etịnne ikọd mmi usʌñ, ebo, “Emem,” ke ini emem imiibaaha, ñko sia adooho, emaebọp ndibene i-imiisọññọ idem, ammọ eben afia ndom edeppe efʌk anye, <verse eid="EZK 13:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 13:11" />ke ntoro dọkkọ mbon ebenne afia ndom edeppe efʌk anye bo ke anye ayaaduọ. Ekamba ukod edịm ayaadep, ami ñyaanyʌñ ndọñ edịm itiad eduọññọ, ndin afịm ayobio ayaafịme. <verse eid="EZK 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 13:12" />Ndibene ado amaaduọ, nte mme awo idiibịppe ndufo ibo, “Mmọ afia ndom ekebenne edeppe efʌk anye?”<verse eid="EZK 13:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 13:13" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke ifiobesịd mmi ami ñyaasio afịm ayobio, ndin ke iyadesịd mmi ami ñyaanam edịm itiad ye ikpọ ukod edịm edep akpọsọñ-akpọsọñ ebiat ñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 13:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 13:14" />Ami ñyaawuut ndibene a-ndufo ebenne afia ndom efʌk do ñnyʌñ mmia anye nnịm ke isọñ nọ itiad idakisọñ amọ ana ukpọk. Anye<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">abio ado</char></note> amaaduọ, ndufo eyaetak ke esịd; ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 13:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 13:15" />Ntom ke ami ndiinwañña ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk ndibene ado ye mbon se ikiben afia ndom ideppe ifʌk anye. Ami ñyaibo ndufo nte, “Ndibene ado ibaaha aba, ukem ye mbon e-ekekamake afia ndom edeppe anye, <verse eid="EZK 13:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 13:16" />mme prọfed Isrel ado eketañña ikọ prọfesi ebaña Yeruselem enyʌñ ekịt mme ñkukịd emem enọ anye ke ini emem imiikibaaha, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.” ’<verse eid="EZK 13:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 13:17" />“Idahami, ayịn awo, wuuk anyen mfo se nditọ ibaan mbon ndufo e-etañña prọfesi eto udọñ esịd ammọ. Tañ prọfesi baña ammọ <verse eid="EZK 13:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 13:18" />nyʌñ bo ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Adọdiọọk anọ ibaan e-ekịmme ibọk mmayịk ekọñọ ke afịd itọñubọk ammọ enyʌñ enam ñkpọ ufʌkiwuod ke utọ ke utọ unyọọñ enọ iwuod ammọ nọ ato do ammọ esịn mme awo ukad. Nte ndufo eyaesịn uwem mbon mmi ke ukad ado enịm a-ndufo ke nte afọn? <verse eid="EZK 13:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 13:19" />Ndufo emensappa miin ke atu ikọd mmi ato ke etək uyọhọ ubọk baali ifañ ye mbeñe uyo. Ke adisʌhọ nsu nnọọ ikọd mmi, e-ekpañña utọñ enọ nsu, ndufo emewot mbon imiikpikinaaha ekpa, enyʌñ esaana mbon imiikpikinaaha edu uwem eyaak.<verse eid="EZK 13:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 13:20" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami mmesua mme ibọk mmayịk a-ndufo ekamake esịn mme awo ukad nte inuen ndin ami ñyaakịppe ammọ nsio ke ubọk ndufo; ami ñyaanam mbon se ndufo esịn ke ukad ebọkkọ nte inuen. <verse eid="EZK 13:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 13:21" />Ami ñyaawai mme ñkpọ ufʌkiwuod ndufo ñnyʌñ ñnyaaña ikọd mmi nsio ke ubọk ndufo, ndin ammọ idiiduọhọ idʌk adudu ndufo aba. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 13:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 13:22" />Sia ndufo ekedatta nsu ndufo enam ndinen awo enie iduọesịd, ke ini ami mmeñkebenne ukuud nsọk ammọ, ñko sia ndufo emaesọọñọ mbon ibak idem anam ammọ ikpọññọ ibak usʌñ ammọ inyʌñ inyaaña uwem ammọ, <verse eid="EZK 13:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 13:23" />ke ntoro ndufo idiikịtte nsu-nsu ñkukịd idiinyʌññọ ibre idiọñ aba. Ami ñyaanyaaña ikọd mmi nsio ke ubọk ndufo. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 13:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="EZK 14" />
  <para style="s1">Esua Enọ mme Akpono Ndem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 14:1" />Usʌk mme ñkpisọñ ke Isrel emaedi embịne miin enyʌñ editie ke iso mmi. <verse eid="EZK 14:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 14:2" />Ndin ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 14:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 14:3" />“Ayịn awo, ideen ami eben mme ubobodñkpọ ewuuk ke esịd ammọ enyʌñ eben mme ibak ndiọiñkpọ iduọ enịm ke iso ammọ. Nte ami ñkpaayak ammọ edimbịp miin mbuume? <verse eid="EZK 14:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 14:4" />Ke ntoro tañ ikọ nọ ammọ nyʌñ bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Awo ufọk Isrel ndomokeed amaawuuk ndem ke esịd ammọ anyʌñ aben ibak idiọọkñkpọ iduọ anịm ke iso ammọ ndin edakka ebịne prọfed, ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñyaabọọrọ ammọ ke idem mmi naña asaña akekem ye akpọsọñ ukpono ubobodñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 14:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 14:5" />Ami ndiinam ami nọ ato do mmaana mben esịd mbon Isrel ntịmme ñnyọñ, e-emaekeñkpọñ miin ebịne mme ndem ammọ.’<verse eid="EZK 14:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 14:6" />“Ke ntoro bo mbon Isrel ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ikappa esịd! Isịññe idem ikpọñ mme ubobodñkpọ ndufo inyʌñ ikañ afịd mbubiam ido ndufo!<verse eid="EZK 14:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 14:7" />“ ‘Ke ini awo Isrel me asenawo ndomokeed a-adʌññọ ke Isrel amaadiañña idem amọ iñkpọñ miin inyʌñ ikiben ubobodñkpọ ammọ iwuuk ke esịd ammọ inyʌñ iben ibak idiọọkñkpọ iduọ inịm ke iso ammọ ndin edakka ebịne prọfed adidimbịp miin ñkpọ, ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñyaabọọrọ ammọ ke idem mmi. <verse eid="EZK 14:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 14:8" />Ami ñyaawuuk iso mmi nse ammọ ñnyʌñ mben ammọ nnam uwọdñkpọ ye se etañ ebaña. Ami ñyaasio ammọ mfep ke atu ikọd mmi. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="EZK 14:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 14:9" />“ ‘Ndin ekpekpek prọfed ado nọ atañ prọfesi, ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmekpek prọfed ado, ndin ami ñyaanyan ubọk mmi ntuuk anye ñnyʌñ nsobo anye nsio ke atu ikọd mmi Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 14:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 14:10" />Ammọ eyaebiom ndudue ammọ, prọfed ado ayaadue ukem nte awo a-akaaha akebịp anye ñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 14:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 14:11" />Ndin mbon Isrel idiitịnne usʌñ aba iñkpọñ miin, idiinyʌññọ isappa idem ammọ aba ye afịd ndiọiñkpọ ammọ. Ammọ eyaedo ikọd mmi, ami ñyaanyʌñ ndo Abasi ammọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 14:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yeruselem Idiibọkkọke Ubiomikpe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 14:12" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 14:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 14:13" />“Ayịn awo, adieke idʌñ ndomokeed endueghe miin ke aditre adinam akpanikọ ye ami ndin ami ñnyan ubọk mmi ndot anye nọ ntre ndidia adidʌk ñnyʌñ ndọñ akañ aka do anyʌñ akewot mme awo ye mme unam ammọ, <verse eid="EZK 14:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 14:14" />akpekọm ideen ita ami: Nua, Dandiel <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Danel, </char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọ etob awo ke mbʌk esed; se ñko ke Esi 14:20</char></note> ye Yoob, ekeba do, ammọ ekeme edinyaaña idem ammọ ikpọọñ ato ke adinenido ammọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 14:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 14:15" />“Me adieke ndọññọ ndiọi unam edʌk idʌñ ado enyʌñ ewoot awo tutu awo ndomokeed isʌhọke aba ndin idʌñ ado akappa ndoon nọ awo ndomokeed imiikanna isaña iboiyo ke ntak ndiọi unam ado, <verse eid="EZK 14:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 14:16" />maama uwem mmi, akpekọm ideen ita ami ekeba ke idʌñ ado, ammọ ikpikanna inyaaña nditọ ideen ye ibaan ammọ. Ammọ ikpọọñ ekpebọkkọ, ado isọñ ayaakappa ndoon, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 14:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 14:17" />“Me ami ñkpedat akañkañ ñkeene idʌñ ado ñnyʌñ mbo nte, ‘Yak akañkañ asaña isañ ke afịd isọñ,’ ndin ami ñwot mme andidʌñ ye mme unam ammọ, <verse eid="EZK 14:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 14:18" />maama uwem mmi, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ, akpekọm ideen ita ami ekeba ke esịd abio ado, ammọ ikpikanna inyaaña nditọ ideen ye ibaan ammọ. Ammọ ikpọọñ ekpebọkkọ.<verse eid="EZK 14:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 14:19" />“Me ami ñkpedọñ udọñọ nsobo utom ke isọñ ado ñnyʌñ ñnwañña ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk anye ato ke uduọk iyiib, ñwot mme andidʌñ ke esịd ye mme unam ammọ, <verse eid="EZK 14:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 14:20" />maama uwem mmi, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ, akpekọm Nua, Dandiel ye Yoob ekeba do, ammọ ikpikanna inyaaña nditọ ideen ye ibaan ammọ. Ammọ ekpenyaaña idem ammọ kpọd ato ke adinenido ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 14:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 14:21" />“Sia se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Adiidiọọk ikitre die ke ami mmaadọñ mme aniendịk ubiomikpe mmi inaañ: akañkañ ye akañ ye ndiọi unam ye udọñọ nsobo utom ke Yeruselem yak ekewot mme awo ye mme unam ammọ! <verse eid="EZK 14:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 14:22" />Kpayeado ayaaba mbon se idiibọkkọ, nditọ ideen ye ibaan se ediikoono isio do. Ammọ eyaedi ubịne fiin, ndin afo umaukịt ido ammọ ye mme adinam ammọ, afo ayaakop idọñesịd ke abaña idiọọk unọmọ a-ami ndatta ñkeene Yeruselem, afịd idiọọk unọmọ se ami ndat ñkeene anye. <verse eid="EZK 14:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 14:23" />Afo ayaakop idọñesịd ke umaukịt ido ammọ ye mme adinam ammọ, sia afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami nnamma ñkpọ ndomokeed ke unana ntak, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 14:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="EZK 15" />
  <para style="s1">Yeruselem nte Fain I-imiiwuọñọke Ñkpọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 15:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 15:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 15:2" />“Ayịn awo, eto fain anie die ukpʌhọde ye ñkọk mme eto mfen ke akai? <verse eid="EZK 15:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 15:3" />Akenam e-edat ñkọk eto amọ enam ñkpọ ndomokeed se ifọn? Nte ammọ esidat anye enam mboi se ekama ekọọñ ñkpọ? <verse eid="EZK 15:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 15:4" />Ndin emaeben anye ikọñ ke ikañ nte ifia nọ ikañ ata anye naña ñkañ iba anyʌñ afọp ufọọd ado, nte anye akeme adifọn ke ñkpọ ndomokeed? <verse eid="EZK 15:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 15:5" />Adieke anye imiikifọnnọ ke ñkpọ ndomokeed naña akedooho ifre, die ndin ke ekeme adiben anye nnam ñkpọ se ifọn ke ini ikañ amaata anye nọ akappa ukañ?<verse eid="EZK 15:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 15:6" />“Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Kpa naña ami mmaaben eto fain ke atu mme eto ke akai nnọ nte ifia ikañ, kpa ntoro ke ami ndiinam mbon se idʌñọ ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="EZK 15:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 15:7" />Ami ñyaawuuk iso mmi nse ammọ. Akpesʌkado ammọ emaewuọ ke ikañ, ikañ adiisʌk itata ammọ. Ndin ke ami mmaawuuk iso mmi nse ammọ, afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 15:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 15:8" />Ami ñyaanam isọn ado akappa ndoon sia ammọ imiinamma akpanikọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 15:8" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="EZK 16" />
  <para style="s1">Yeruselem nte Asịn Efịbe Anwaan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 16:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 16:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 16:2" />“Ayịn awo, deet mme mbubiam ido se Yeruselem anañña wọt anye <verse eid="EZK 16:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 16:3" />nyʌñ bo ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ abaña Yeruselem ado ami: Ntịppe mfo ye emana mfo eketo isọñ Kenan; ete mfo akedo awo Amọọ, eka mfo anyʌñ ado awo Hed. <verse eid="EZK 16:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 16:4" />Usen a-afo akemanake awo ikukpịkkeke fiin udʌkakob, awo ikinyʌññọ uyet fiin ke mmọọñ yak afo asana, ikinyʌññọ usọọk fiin ke inʌñ me adubọp fiin ke afọñ. <verse eid="EZK 16:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 16:5" />Awo ndomokeed ikuseeghe fiin ye mbọm, inyʌññọ ukop udʌk ikem se ekpenam mme ñkpọ ami unọọ fiin. Utu ke ndo, emautop fiin eduọọk ke akpa inwañ, sia usen a-afo akemanake emausọọn fiin.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 16:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 16:6" />“Ndin ami mmaasaña mboiyo ñnyʌñ ñkịt naña afo amiañña ke iyiib mfo, ndin nte afo asịneke do ke iyiib mfo ami mmaubo fiin nte, ‘Du uwem!’ <verse eid="EZK 16:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 16:7" />Ami mmaanam afo akọt nte ñkpọ se itịppe ke inwañ. Afo amaakọt anyʌñ akpon akappa abọikpa. Amaatịppe eba, ided mfo amaanyʌñ akọt, kpayeado afo akesaña ataa ifed.”<verse eid="EZK 16:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 16:8" />Akema ami mmaadisaña mboiyo, ndin ke ini ami mmaakuse fiin ñnyʌñ ñkịt mbo ke afo amekpon akem se ema, ami mmaatat mben afọñidem mmi udot fiin ke idem ñnyʌñ ufʌk ifed. Ami mmaanam enwọñọ ye afo ñnyʌñ ndʌk edioomo ye afo, ndin afo amaakappa ado ake mmi, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 16:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 16:9" />Ami mmauyet fiin ke mmọọñ ñnyʌñ usio iyiib ado ke idem mfep, ñnyʌñ ufiọññọ adan. <verse eid="EZK 16:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 16:10" />Ami mmausịn fiin awedeñwed afọñ ke idem ñnyʌñ usịn ikpaukod e-ekamake ataa eti uduud ikpa enam. Ami mmausịn fiin uyaiya afọñ linen ñnyʌñ ndat mme nsọñudua afọñ ufʌk fiin. <verse eid="EZK 16:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 16:11" />Ami mmaubana fiin idem ye ñkpọ mbanaidem: ami mmausịn fiin mme akpohoubọk ke ubọk ñnyʌñ ukọọñ ñkwaitọñ ke itọñ, <verse eid="EZK 16:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 16:12" />ñko ami mmausịn ñkpannuun ke iwuo mfo, ñkpahautọñ ke utọñ ye uyaiya anyanya ke iwuod mfo. <verse eid="EZK 16:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 16:13" />Ke ntoro emaubana fiin idem ke kold ye silfa; ekedat uyaiya linen ye nsọñudua afọñ ye awedeñwed afọñ ekịm mme nsiine mfo. Ndidia mfo akedo adanakwọọk, adan ọlif ye ataa eti ndomuyo. Uyai mfo amaademme eti-eti ndin afo amaanyʌñ adọọk akekappa abọọñanwaan. <verse eid="EZK 16:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 16:14" />Etob mfo amaatara ke mme idịd ke ntak uyai mfo, sia inie a-ami ñkunọọhọ fiin amaanam uyai mfo afọn ama, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 16:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 16:15" />Ado afo amaabuọt idem ke uyai mfo anyʌñ akama etob mfo asaña akpara. Afo amaafọn ido ye awo akeedodo akesañake aboiyo ndin uyai mfo amaakappa ado ake amọ. <verse eid="EZK 16:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 16:16" />Afo amaaben ubaak nsiine mfo anam mme ñyaayamma ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie a-afo asitieghe anam akpara mfo. Afo amaabịne anye, ndin anye amaaben uyai mfo anie. <verse eid="EZK 16:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 16:17" />Afo amaanyʌñ aben uyaiya ñkpọ mbanaidem a-ami ñkunọọhọ fiin, ñkpọ mbanaidem edatta kold ye silfa mmi enam, amaanyʌñ abot mme abasi ke mbid ideen anọ idem mfo anyʌñ anam akpara ye ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 16:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 16:18" />Afo amaanyʌñ aben mme awedeñwed afọñ mfo asịn ammọ, anyʌñ aben adan mmi ye insensi mmi anịm ammọ ke iso. <verse eid="EZK 16:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 16:19" />Ñko ndidia a-ami ñkunọọhọ fiin: ndomuyo, adan ọlif ye adanakwọọk a-ami ñkunọọhọ fiin mbo yak adia, afo amaaben anịm ammọ ke iso nte anemufịk insensi. Se ikitịppe ado ado, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 16:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 16:20" />Afo amaanyʌñ akoono nditọ ideen ye ibaan a-afo akemanna annọọ miin awa anọ mme ubobodñkpọ nte ndidia. Nte akpara mfo ikikemme? <verse eid="EZK 16:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 16:21" />Afo amaayọi nditọ mmi aben awa anọ mme ubobodñkpọ ado. <verse eid="EZK 16:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 16:22" />Ke afịd mme mbubiam adinam mfo ye akpara mfo afo ukutoiyoke mme usen uyịn mfo, a-afo akesañake ifed ye ukpọk, anyʌñ amiañña ke iyiib mfo.<verse eid="EZK 16:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 16:23" />Adọdiọọk! Adọdiọọk unọ fiin, ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. Ke adidian ke afịd mme ibak mfo mfen, <verse eid="EZK 16:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 16:24" />afo amaabọp abod anọ idem mfo anyʌñ anam uyaiya ñwommo ke afịd anwa abio. <verse eid="EZK 16:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 16:25" />Kwa ikọkkọ efaak afo amaabọọp mme mfọọn ñwommo mfo anyʌñ abiat uyai mfo, anyʌñ atat ukod akpara mfo anọ afịd awo se isaña iboiyo. <verse eid="EZK 16:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 16:26" />Afo amaanam akpara ye mbon Iyib, mme mbọhọidʌñ mfo e-enieghe ikpọ idemideen, a-anyʌñ anam iyadesịd mmi akpon ato ke edu usaña akpara mfo. <verse eid="EZK 16:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 16:27" />Anam ami mmaanyanna ubọk mmi udot fiin ke idem ñnyʌñ nsuuho adaña udeeme idʌñ mfo; ami mmauyaak fiin nnọ idiọọkitọñ mme asua mfo, kpa nditọ ibaan mbon Filistia, e-ekekoppo ñkpaidem ebaña abʌd-abʌd ido mfo. <verse eid="EZK 16:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 16:28" />Afo amaasaña akpara ye mbon Asiria ñko, sia ukukoppo uyʌkkọ; ndin ke umaukuma ado, afo ukusʌkkọ ukokop uyʌkkọ. <verse eid="EZK 16:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 16:29" />Ndin afo amaasaña akpara akewuọ Babilọn, isọñ mme anyam udua, ado kpayeado ukukoppo uyʌkkọ.<verse eid="EZK 16:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 16:30" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo, Ami mmeyọhọ ye iyadesịd ubaña fiin, ke ini afo umaunam afịd mme ñkpọ ami, nte akpara i-imiinieghe iso abuud! <verse eid="EZK 16:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 16:31" />Ke ini afo akebọppọ mme abod mfo ke afịd iwuod efaak anyʌñ anam mme mfọọn ñwommo mfo ke afịd anwa abio, afo ukubaaha nte akpara, sia amaasịn adibọ akʌk utom akpara.<verse eid="EZK 16:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 16:32" />Afo asịn efịbe anwaan! Afo amema isenawo akan ebe mfo! <verse eid="EZK 16:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 16:33" />Afịd mme akpara esida ke adibọbọ enọ, ado afo anọọnọ afịd mbon ima mfo enọ, anọ ammọ ubọkedem ate ammọ eto afịd itie edi ubịne fiin nọ edibọ ndiọi unwam uto fiin. <verse eid="EZK 16:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 16:34" />Ke ntoro, ke usaña akpara mfo afo unamma naña mbon mfen enam; awo ndomokeed idiighe ubịne fiin ke ntak adiyem mfọn mfo. Afo ado ataa isio-isio, sia afo amekpe akʌk, ado awo ukpeeghe fiin ñkpọ ndomokeed.<verse eid="EZK 16:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 16:35" />Ke ntoro, afo akpara, kop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>! <verse eid="EZK 16:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 16:36" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ado ami: Sia afo umaunwañña idiọọkitọñ mfo unyʌñ ufʌkkọ ifed mfo ato ke adinam use ye mme ama mfo, ñko ke ntak afịd mbubiam ibọk mfo, ye sia umaukunọ ammọ iyiib nditọ mfo, <verse eid="EZK 16:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 16:37" />ke ntak ado ami ñyaakoono afịd mme ama mfo, a-afo akesikoppo inem uwem ye ammọ, mbon a-afo akemaaha ye mbon a-afo akesuaha. Ami ñyaakoono ammọ ke afịd ñkanñkʌk mbon itie keed ñnyʌñ ufʌkkọ fiin ifed ke iso ammọ, ndin ammọ eyaekịt naña afo ada ataa ifed. <verse eid="EZK 16:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 16:38" />Ami ñyaabiide ukem ufen e-esinọọhọ ibaan e-esịnne efịbe ye mbon e-eduọkkọ iyiib unọ fiin; ke ifiobesịd ye ufịb mmi, ami ñyaanyʌñ mbiere ikpe usio usiene uduọk iyiib unọ fiin. <verse eid="EZK 16:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 16:39" />Ami ñyauyaak fiin nsịn ke ubọk mme ama mfo ndin ammọ eyaewuut mme abod mfo enyʌñ ebiat mme mfọọn ñwommo mfo. Ammọ eyausịññe fiin afọñ ke idem enyʌñ ekoono mfọọn ñkpọ mbanaidem mfo ndin uyaak fiin esuuk ataa ifed. <verse eid="EZK 16:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 16:40" />Ammọ eyaedat udịm awo ukeene fiin, ammọ eyautọọñ fiin ke itiad enyʌñ ukpok fiin mbai-mbai ke akañkañ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 16:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 16:41" />Ammọ eyaefọọmọ mme ufọk mfo enyʌñ unọ fiin ufen ke iso uwak ibaan. Ami ñyautre fiin usaña akpara, ndin afo uduukpeeghe mme ama mfo aba. <verse eid="EZK 16:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 16:42" />Ndin ifiobesịd mmi ye afo ayaasuuhọ, iyadesịd ufịb mmi ayaanyʌñ awọññọ ukpọñ fiin; ami ñyaasuuhọ esịd ñnyʌññọ ñyat esịd aba.<verse eid="EZK 16:42" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 16:43" />Sia afo umuukutoiyoke mme usen uyịn mfo ado anam afịd ñkpọ ami nọ esịd añyat miin, ke akpanikọ ami ñyaaben se afo anam udot fiin ke iwuod, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. Nte afo ukubenne ndedeghe ido mfo udian ye afịd mme mbubiam adinam mfo mfen?<verse eid="EZK 16:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 16:44" />Afịd mbon se isitop ufiid eyaetop ufiid ami ubaña fiin: “Ayịn mbid eka.” <verse eid="EZK 16:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 16:45" />Afo ado ataa mbid eka mfo, a-akesuaha ebe ye nditọ amọ; afo anyʌñ ado ataa mbid nditọeka mfo ibaan, e-ekesuaha mme ebe ye nditọ ammọ. Eka mfo akedo awo Hed, ete mfo anyʌñ ado awo Amọọ. <verse eid="EZK 16:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 16:46" />Ekamba ayịneka mfo awonwaan aketo Sameria, a-akedʌññọ ke ukañ adoro mfo ye nditọ ibaan amọ; ndin etək ayịneka mfo awonwaan, a-akedʌññọ ke usuuk mfo ye nditọ ibaan amọ, aketo Sọdọm. <verse eid="EZK 16:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 16:47" />Afo ukukeeneke usʌñ ammọ unyʌñ unam mbubiam ido ammọ kpọd, ado afo amaasappa idem mfo akan ammọ ke afịd usʌñ mfo. <verse eid="EZK 16:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 16:48" />Adaña ini a-nduuho uwem, ayịneka mfo andikito Sọdọm ye nditọ amọ ibaan akenam inamma se afo ye nditọ mfo ibaan enam, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 16:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 16:49" />Idiọọkñkpọ ayịneka mfo a-aketooho Sọdọm akedo ami: Anye ye nditọ amọ ibaan ekewọt idem, edia eyʌkkọ inyʌññọ idọñ anyen ibaña mbon mfen; ammọ ikinwamma mme uweene ye mbon unana. <verse eid="EZK 16:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="EZK 16:50" />Ammọ emaetañ idem enyʌñ enam mme mbubiam ñkpọ ke iso mmi. Ke ntoro, ami mmaabịn ammọ nsio nte afo akịtte. <verse eid="EZK 16:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="EZK 16:51" />Andikito Sameria ikinamma ukpọk mbakka iba ndiọiñkpọ se afo akenam. Afo amenam mbubiam ñkpọ nọ awak akan ake ammọ, ndin afịd se afo anam ami anam anye aba nte nditọeka mfo ibaan edo ndinen. <verse eid="EZK 16:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="EZK 16:52" />Biom asuenne mfo, sia afo amenam nọ nditọeka mfo ibaan enen. Sia ndiọiñkpọ mfo emaediọi ekan ake ammọ, anye adiba nte ammọ efọn ukan fiin. Ke ntoro, kop abuud nyʌñ biom asuenne mfo, sia afo amenam nọ aba nte nditọeka mfo ibaan edo ndinen.<verse eid="EZK 16:52" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" sid="EZK 16:53" />Ado ami ñyaayaak mfọnọñkpọ Sọdọm ye nditọ amọ ibaan ye ake Sameria ye nditọ amọ ibaan, ye ake mfo, etịmme ubịne fiin, <verse eid="EZK 16:53" /><verse number="54" style="v" sid="EZK 16:54" />nọ ato do afo abiom asuenne mfo anyʌñ akop abuud ke afịd se afo anam adinọ ammọ idọñesịd. <verse eid="EZK 16:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="EZK 16:55" />Ndin nditọeka mfo ibaan, Sọdọm ye nditọ amọ ibaan ye Sameria ye nditọ amọ ibaan, eyaemaana edido se ekedo; afo ye nditọ ibaan mfo eyaenyʌñ emaana edido se ekedo. <verse eid="EZK 16:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="EZK 16:56" />Afo ukpukusiaha anyịñ Sọdọm ayịneka mfo ke usen ntañidem mfo, <verse eid="EZK 16:56" /><verse number="57" style="v" sid="EZK 16:57" />mbemiso ekeyaara ibak mfo. Kpayeado, afo adiido ñkpọ nsaha anọ nditọ ibaan Edọm idahami ye afịd mbọhọidʌñ amọ ye nditọ ibaan Filistia, afịd mbon se ukanna fiin ikʌk u-useeghe fiin nte ñkpọ ndọk. <verse eid="EZK 16:57" /><verse number="58" style="v" sid="EZK 16:58" />Afo ayaabọ utịb ndedeghe ido mfo ye mme mbubiam adinam mfo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ.<verse eid="EZK 16:58" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" sid="EZK 16:59" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: “Ami ñyaanam naña adot ye afo, sia afo amaasịn unwọñọ mmi ke ndek ke adibiat edioomo mmi. <verse eid="EZK 16:59" /><verse number="60" style="v" sid="EZK 16:60" />Kpayeado ñyaatoiyo edioomo a-ami ñkenamma ye afo ke ini uyịn mfo, ndin ami ñyaawuuk nsi-nsi edioomo ye afo. <verse eid="EZK 16:60" /><verse number="61" style="v" sid="EZK 16:61" />Ndin afo ayaatoiyo usʌñ mfo anyʌñ akop abuud ke ini mmaayaak nditọeka mfo ibaan unọ, mbon se usọñ fiin ye mbon se isịp ukan fiin. Ami ñyaaben ammọ unọ fiin nte nditọ mfo ibaan, ado idiitooho ke edioomo mmi ye afo. <verse eid="EZK 16:61" /><verse number="62" style="v" sid="EZK 16:62" />Ke ntom ami ñyaanam edioomo mmi ye afo asọọñọ ada, ndin afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 16:62" /><verse number="63" style="v" sid="EZK 16:63" />Ndin, ami mmaadakka unọ fiin ke afịd se afo anam, afo ayaatoiyo anyʌñ akop abuud, ndin tutu amama uduukʌppọke inua aba akeene ntak asuenne mfo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 16:63" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 16" />
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="EZK 17" />
  <para style="s1">Ntrukpuum Iba ye Fain Keed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 17:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 17:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 17:2" />“Ayịn awo, nọ ndadñwọd ikọ a-awọttọ idiọọk ye eti edu nyʌñ ben anye tañ wọt nditọ Isrel nte ñke. <verse eid="EZK 17:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 17:3" />Bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ekamba ntrukpuum a-anieghe akpọsọñ mba, ñnyan ñwa a-adọọñọke nsio-nsio ñkem amaadi Lebanọn. Amaadidoro ke atịñe sida keed, <verse eid="EZK 17:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 17:4" />anye amaabuuñ ataa atịñe sida ado asio anyʌñ aben aketọ ke abio mme anyamudua.<verse eid="EZK 17:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 17:5" />“ ‘Anye amaaben mfịd keed ke isọñ ado aketọ ke eti isọñ. Anye aketọ anye nte eto wilo ke mben uwak mmọọñ, <verse eid="EZK 17:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 17:6" />ndin anye amaatịppe anyʌñ akappa fain a-asakkake ñkọk anyʌñ aməho idaha. Mme ñkọk amọ emaekappa ese anye, ado mme adʌñ amọ emaesʌhọ ke idak amọ. Ndin anye amaakappa ado fain anyʌñ asaiya ñkọk, anyʌñ asịññe mme mfañ.<verse eid="EZK 17:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 17:7" />“ ‘Ado ekamba ntrukpuum mfen amaaba se ikikop akpọsọñ adudu ke mme mba amọ, ñwa amọ anyʌñ awak. Fain ami ndin amaawọññọ adʌñ amọ awọt anye, ke itie e-eketọọhọ anye, anyʌñ anyanna mme ñkọk amọ anọ anye, ayem mmọọñ. <verse eid="EZK 17:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 17:8" />Eketọ anye ke eti isọñ ke mben isọñ se inekke inie mmọọñ nọ ato do anye asaiya ñkọk, anwịm mfịd anyʌñ akappa ado ataa uyaiya fain.’<verse eid="EZK 17:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 17:9" />“Bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Nte anye ayaaseghe? Nte awo idiiwịppeke anye isio inyʌñ ikịp mfịd amọ nọ anye ayeppe? Afịd ufa nseghe amọ ayaayeppe. Idooho ubọk se inie adudu me uwak awo ediida iwịppe anye isio ito adʌñ amọ. <verse eid="EZK 17:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 17:10" />Emaetọ anye, ado nte anye ayaaseghe? Nte anye idiiyeppeke afịd-afịd ke ini afịm ayobio edem usakkautịn atuuhọ anye, ayeppe ke itie isọñ eketọọhọ anye?’ ”<verse eid="EZK 17:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 17:11" />Ndin ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 17:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 17:12" />“Dọkkọ mbon nsọñiwuod ami ate, ‘Nte ndufo idiọọñọke se mme ñkpọ ami ewuọñọ?’ Bo ammọ ate: ‘Adidem Babilọn amaakaa Yeruselem akeben adidem amọ ye mme ñkpisọñ amọ, akoono ammọ anyọñ akaa Babilọn. <verse eid="EZK 17:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 17:13" />Ndin anye amaasio awo ufọk adidem keed anyʌñ anam edioomo ye anye, anyʌñ anam anye adat unwọñọ. Anye amaanyʌñ akoono mme awuọiso awo ke abio asio, <verse eid="EZK 17:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 17:14" />nọ ato do esuuhọ ubọọñ abio ado, mbaak anye akuukan abenne idem aba, adu uwem ato ke anye adinịm edioomo amọ kpọd. <verse eid="EZK 17:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 17:15" />Ado adidem amaasọñ iwuod ye anye anyʌñ adọñ mme isʌñutom eka Iyib ekebọ mme enañmbakara ye uwak mbon ekọñ esọk anye. Nte anye ayaakịt unen? Nte awo a-anamma utọ ñkpọ ado ayaabọkkọ? Nte anye ayaabiat edioomo ado ama ndin abọkkọ?<verse eid="EZK 17:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 17:16" />“ ‘<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ate, Adaña nte ami nduuho uwem, anye adiikpa ke Babilọn, ke isọñ adidem ado a-aketemme anye ke ebekpo, a-anye akesịnne unwọñọ amọ ke ndek, anyʌñ abiat edioomo amọ. <verse eid="EZK 17:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 17:17" />Fero ye ñkpọsọñ udịmekọñ amọ ye ikpọ uwak atu awo idiibaaha ufọn inọ anye ke ekọñ, ke emaebọp mme ufiọkñkpọ ye mme ufọk ekọñ nọ ato do esobo uwak uwem awo. <verse eid="EZK 17:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 17:18" />Anye amaasịn unwọñọ ke ndek ke adibiat edioomo. Sia adooho anye amaanam enwọñọ ama akem anye asʌk akenam afịd ñkpọ ami, anye idiibọkkọke.<verse eid="EZK 17:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 17:19" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Adaña nte ami nduuho ke uwem, ami ñyaanọ anye utịb ke abaña anye adisịn enwọñọ mmi ke ndek ye ke adibiat edioomo mmi. <verse eid="EZK 17:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 17:20" />Ami ñyaatat iyịre mmi nnịm nnọ anye, ndin afia mmi ayaamʌm anye. Ami ñyaaben anye ñkaa Babilọn ñnyʌñ ñkekpe ikpe amọ do sia anye ikinamma akpanikọ ye ami. <verse eid="EZK 17:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 17:21" />Eyaesobo afịd nti mbon ekọñ amọ ke akañkañ, ndin eyaesuan mbon se isʌhọ edọñ ke mme itʌñ ye inuuk. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ntañ.<verse eid="EZK 17:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 17:22" />“ ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ke idem mmi ñyaadat nseghe ke ataa atịñe sida ñnyʌñ ntọ; ami ñyaabuuñ nsek emịne ke ataa atịñe amọ ñnyʌñ ntọ ke anyọñ ñkoñ-ñkoñ abod. <verse eid="EZK 17:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 17:23" />Ami ndiitọ anye ke atịñe ñkoñ-ñkoñ ikpọabod Isrel; anye ayaasaiya ñkọk anyʌñ anwịm mfịd anyʌñ akappa uyaiya sida. Mme nsio-nsio utọ inuen eyaebọp efọk edʌñọ do; ammọ eyaenie mfuud ke idak ñkọk amọ <verse eid="EZK 17:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 17:24" />Afịd eto ke akai eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> nnam anyan eto aməho ñnyʌñ nnam ibio eto akọt anyọọñ. Ado ami nnam nọ awawa eto asaat ñnyʌñ nnam nsaad eto aseghe atara.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 17:24">“ ‘Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmetañ, ndin ñyaanyʌñ nnam.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 17:24" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 17" />
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="EZK 18" />
  <para style="s1">Anam Idiọọkñkpọ Ayaakpa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 18:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 18:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 18:2" />“Awuọñọ die ndufo editop utọ ntəño-ntəño ñke ami mbaña isọñ Isrel:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:2">“ ‘Mme ete ye eka edadia ñkpaiya kreb,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:2">ndin eded nditọ edidoro adiyịk’?<verse eid="EZK 18:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 18:3" />“<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ate, adaña nte ami mbaaha ke uwem, ndufo idiitoppo ntəño-ntəño ñke ami aba ke Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 18:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 18:4" />Sia afịd awo edo ake mmi, ete ye eka ukem nte ayịn, ammọ awo iba ukem-ukem edo ake mmi. Awo a-anamma idiọọkñkpọ ado anye adiikpa.<verse eid="EZK 18:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 18:5" />“Adieke adinen awo abaaha</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:5">a-anamma se ifọn inyʌñ inen.<verse eid="EZK 18:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 18:6" />Anye idiaha ñkpọ ke mme ñwommo ikpọabod</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:6">inyʌññọ ibenne anyen ise mme ubobodñkpọ Isrel.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:6">Anye isappake anwaan mbọhọidʌñ amọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:6">inyʌññọ inie ewuana ye awonwaan ke ini itieisọñ amọ.<verse eid="EZK 18:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 18:7" />Anye ifiighe awo ndomokeed,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:7">ado asaana se anye akebọọ awo ke ubiọñ ayaak.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:7">Anye iwooho ñwo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:7">ado aben ndidia amọ anọ mbon abiọọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:7">anyʌñ anọ mbon esañake ifed afọñ.<verse eid="EZK 18:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 18:8" />Anye iwuọdọ awo akʌk iyem udod</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:8">inyʌññọ ibọ ammọ udod.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:8">Anye isịnne ubọk ke idiọọkñkpọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:8">anyʌñ akpe ikpe ke ufọọd awo iba ke unen.<verse eid="EZK 18:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 18:9" />Anye asaña ke mme ewʌhọ mmi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:9">anyʌñ anịm mme mbed mmi ke afịd esịd.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:9">Awo ado ado adinen;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:9">ke akpanikọ anye ayaadu uwem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:9">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo.<verse eid="EZK 18:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 18:10" />“Akpedo anam anye anie afai-afai ayịn, a-aduọkkọ iyiib anyʌñ anam mme ñkpọ ami ndomokeed <verse eid="EZK 18:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 18:11" />(akpesʌkado ete amọ imiinamma ndomokeed):</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:11">“Anye adia ñkpọ ke mme ñwommo ikpọabod.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:11">Anye asappa anwaan mbọhọidʌñ amọ.<verse eid="EZK 18:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 18:12" />Anye afiik uweene ye mbon unana.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:12">Anye awo ñwo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:12">Anye isaanake se anye akebọọ ke ubiọñ iyaak.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:12">Anye abenne anyen ase mme ubobodñkpọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:12">Anye anam mme mbubiam ñkpọ.<verse eid="EZK 18:12" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 18:13" />Anye awuọt awo akʌk ke udod anyʌñ abọ akpọsọñ udod.</para>
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 18:13">Nte utọ awo ado ayaadu uwem? Anye idiiduuho! Sia anye anam afịd mbubiam ñkpọ ami, ana ewot anye; iyiib amọ adiidoro anye ke iwuod.<verse eid="EZK 18:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 18:14" />“Akpedo anam ayịn ami anie ayịn a-akịtte afịd ndiọiñkpọ se ete amọ anam, ndin akpesʌkado anye akịtte ammọ, anye inamma mme utọ ñkpọ ado:<verse eid="EZK 18:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 18:15" />“Anye idiaha ñkpọ ke mme ñwommo ikpọabod</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:15">inyʌññọ ibenne anyen ise mme ubobodñkpọ Isrel.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:15">Anye isappake anwaan mbọhọidʌñ amọ.<verse eid="EZK 18:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 18:16" />Anye ifiikke awo ndomokeed</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:16">inyʌññọ ibọ ubiọñ mbemiso anọ awo ewuọd.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:16">Anye iwooho ñwo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:16">ado anọ mbon abiọọñ ndidia amọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:16">anyʌñ anọ mbon se isaña ifed afọñ.<verse eid="EZK 18:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 18:17" />Anye inamma uweene idiọọk</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:17">inyʌññọ ibọ ammọ udod me usiene.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:17">Anye anịm mme mbed mmi anyʌñ asaña ke mme ewʌhọ mmi.</para>
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 18:17">Anye idiikpaaha ke iwuod idiọọkñkpọ ete amọ; ke akpanikọ anye ayaadu uwem. <verse eid="EZK 18:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 18:18" />Ado ete amọ ayaakpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ amọ, sia anye akefiighe mme awo abọ ñkpọ, awo ayịneka amọ anyʌñ anam se imiifọnnọ ke atu mbon amọ.<verse eid="EZK 18:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 18:19" />“Ado afo abịp ate, ‘Nsoo inam nọ ayịn imiiwanake ke ufen ndudue ete amọ?’ Sia ayịn amaanam se inen inyʌñ ifọn anyʌñ adat ini anịm afịd ewʌhọ mmi, anye idiitreke adidu uwem. <verse eid="EZK 18:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 18:20" />Awo a-anamma idiọọkñkpọ ado awo se idiikpa. Ayịn idiiwanake ke ufen ndudue ete, ete ñko idiiwanake ke ufen ndudue ayịn. Eyaebat adinenido mbon ndinen awo enọ ammọ, enyʌñ ebat ibak mbon ibak enọ mbon ibak.<verse eid="EZK 18:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 18:21" />“Ado idiọọk awo akpekpọñ afịd ndiọiñkpọ a-anye akenamma anyʌñ anịm afịd ewʌhọ mmi anyʌñ anam se inen inyʌñ ifọn, ke akpanikọ awo ado ayaadu uwem; anye idiikpaaha. <verse eid="EZK 18:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 18:22" />Awo idiitoiyoke ndudue ndomokeed a-ammọ ekenamma. Ammọ eyaedu uwem ato ke ntak ndinen ñkpọ a-ammọ ekenamma. <verse eid="EZK 18:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 18:23" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ate, Ado nte ami ñkop inemesịd ke ñkpa idiọọk awo? Utu ke ado, nte ami nnemme esịd ke ammọ emaekpọñ usʌñ ammọ inyʌñ idu uwem?<verse eid="EZK 18:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 18:24" />“Ado adinen awo akpekpọñ adinenido amọ anyʌñ anam idiọọkñkpọ ye ukem mbubiam ñkpọ ake anamidiọọk anamma, nte anye ayaadu uwem? Awo idiitoiyoke eti ñkpọ ndomokeed se awo ado akenam. Ke ntak unana akpanikọ ammọ ye ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ a-ammọ ekenamma, ammọ eyaekpa.<verse eid="EZK 18:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 18:25" />“Kpayeado ndufo ebo, ‘Usʌñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inenne.’ Ikpañ utọñ, ndufo mbon Isrel: Nte usʌñ mmi inenne? Nte idooho usʌñ ndufo akapado se imiinenne? <verse eid="EZK 18:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 18:26" />Adinen awo akpekpọñ adinenido amọ anyʌñ anam idiọọkñkpọ, ammọ eyaekpa ke abaña ado; ammọ eyaekpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 18:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 18:27" />Ado idiọọk awo akpekpọñ idiọọk usʌñ amọ anyʌñ anam se inen inyʌñ ifọn, ammọ eyaenyaaña uwem ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 18:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 18:28" />Sia ammọ ekereke ebaña afịd ndudue ammọ enyʌñ esịññe idem ekpọñ, awo ado idiitreke adidu uwem; ammọ idiikpaaha. <verse eid="EZK 18:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 18:29" />Kpayeado mbon Isrel ebo ete, ‘Usʌñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inenne.’ Mbon Isrel, nte usʌñ mmi inenne? Nte idooho usʌñ ndufo akapado se imiinenne?<verse eid="EZK 18:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 18:30" />“Ke ntoro, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ate, ndufo mbon Isrel, ami ñyaakpe ikpe ye ndufo keedekeed ñkeene naña mme usʌñ ndufo eba. Ikappa esịd! Ikpọñ afịd idiọọk ido ndufo; ndin idiọọkñkpọ idiidooho ñkpọ iduọ inọ ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 18:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 18:31" />Isịññe idem ikpọñ afịd ndiọi se ndufo enam, inyʌñ inie ufa esịd ye ufa sịbidịd. Nsoo ido ntak ake ndufo eyemme edikpa, O mbon Isrel? <verse eid="EZK 18:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 18:32" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ate, ami ñkoppo inemesịd mbaña ñkpa awo akeedodo. Ikappa esịd inyʌñ idu uwem!<verse eid="EZK 18:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 18" />
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="EZK 19" />
  <para style="s1">Aseeme A-abañake Nditọ Mme Akpanabọọñ Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 19:1" />“Seeme aseeme baña mme akpanabọọñ Isrel <verse eid="EZK 19:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 19:2" />nyʌñ bo ate:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:2">“ ‘Eka ndufo akedo uman ekpe</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:2">ke atu mme ekpe!</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:2">Anye akena ke atu ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:2">anyʌñ abọọk mme ñyịn amọ.<verse eid="EZK 19:2" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 19:3" />Anye amaabọọk keed ke atu ñyịn amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:3">ndin anye amaanyʌñ akappa ado anie adudu ekpe.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:3">Anye amaakpeep adiwai ñkpọ se anye amʌm,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:3">ndin anye amaanyʌñ akappa ado andita awo.<verse eid="EZK 19:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 19:4" />Mme idịd emaekop ebaña anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:4">ndin emaemʌm anye ke ukpe ammọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:4">Ammọ emaekọp anye ke akpọnọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:4">eben ekaa isọñ Iyib.<verse eid="EZK 19:4" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 19:5" />“ ‘Ke ini eka amọ amaakekịt ke idodanyen ibaaha,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:5">ke idodanyen imọ akpa mfʌhọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:5">anye amaasio ñyịn amọ keed mfen,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:5">anyʌñ anam anye ado anie adudu ekpe.<verse eid="EZK 19:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 19:6" />Anye amaasaña ke atu mme ekpe,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:6">sia anye akedido anie adudu ekpe.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:6">Anye amaakpeep adiwai ñkpọ se anye amʌm,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:6">ndin anye amaanyʌñ akappa ado andita awo.<verse eid="EZK 19:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 19:7" />Anye amaabiat mme ñkpọsọñ itie ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:7">anyʌñ anam abio ammọ anaa ukpọk.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:7">Isọñ ado ye afịd awo se ikidʌñọ do</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:7">emaekop ndịk enọ uyio ñkuun amọ.<verse eid="EZK 19:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 19:8" />Ndin mme idịd emaedaaña eda ebaña anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:8">eto ke mme ñkanñkʌk ado.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:8">Ammọ emaetat iyịre ammọ enịm enọ anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:8">enyʌñ emʌm anye ke ukpe ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 19:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 19:9" />Ammọ emaekọp anye ke akpọnọ edʌt esịn ke ikad,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:9">enyʌñ eben anye esọk adidem Babilọn.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:9">Ammọ emaesịn anye ke ufọk ñkpakọb,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:9">anam awo ikikoppo uyio ñkuun amọ aba</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:9">ke mme ikpọabod Isrel.<verse eid="EZK 19:9" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 19:10" />“ ‘Eka mfo akeba nte fain ke inwañ fain mfo;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:10">eketọ anye ke mben mmọọñ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:10">anye amaanwịm mfịd anyʌñ anie uwak ñkọk</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:10">ke ntak uwak mmọọñ.<verse eid="EZK 19:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 19:11" />Mme ñkọk amọ emaesọọñ idem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:11">edot se ekpekama enam esañubọọñ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:11">Idaha amọ amaakoñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:11">akan mme atu eto mfen,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:11">emaesọp ekịt anye ke ntak unyọọñ amọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:11">ye uwak ñkọk amọ.<verse eid="EZK 19:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 19:12" />Ado emaewịppe anye esio ke ifiobesịd</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:12">enyʌñ etop eduọk ke isọñ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:12">Afịm ayobio usakkautịn amaanyʌñ anam anye ayeppe,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:12">emaekịp mfịd amọ esịññe;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:12">mme nsọọñ ñkọk amọ emaebʌñọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:12">ikañ amaanyʌñ ata ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 19:12" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 19:13" />Idahami etọ anye ke akpautatan,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:13">ke isọñ a-Asatta eti-eti.<verse eid="EZK 19:13" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 19:14" />Ikañ amaato ñkọk amọ keed awuọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:14">anyʌñ ata mme mfịd amọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:14">Ñkọk se isọñ idem ndomokeed isʌhọke aba ke idem amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:14">akpedotto se ekama enam esañubọọñ.’</para>
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 19:14">Ami ado aseeme, anyʌñ ado se ekama eseeme aseeme.”<verse eid="EZK 19:14" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 19" />
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="EZK 20" />
  <para style="s1">E-esat mme Asọñiwuod Mbon Isrel Esịññe ke Atu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 20:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua itiaba, ke ayọhọ afiọñ ition, ke ayọhọ usen duob, usʌk mme ñkpisọñ ke Isrel emaeto edi adibịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñkpọ, ndin ammọ edisuuk etie ke iso mmi.<verse eid="EZK 20:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 20:2" />Ndin ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 20:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 20:3" />“Ayịn awo, tañ ikọ nọ mme ñkpisọñ Isrel nyʌñ bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ndufo edi adimbịp miin ñkpọ? Ke adaña ini ami nduuho uwem, ami ndiiyakka ndufo embịp miin ñkpọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’<verse eid="EZK 20:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 20:4" />“Afo ayaakpe ikpe anọ ammọ? Ayịn awo, afo ayaakpe ikpe anọ ammọ? Ado ntoro, nam nọ ammọ ediọọñọ mme mbubiam adinam mme eteete ammọ <verse eid="EZK 20:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 20:5" />nyʌñ bo ammọ ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Usen a-ami ñkemekke Isrel, ami mmaabenne ubọk ke anyọñ ñnwọñọ nnọ ubon Yekọb ñnyʌñ ñyaara idem mmi nnọ ammọ ke Iyib. Ami mmaabenne ubọk ke anyọñ mbo ammọ nte, “Ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ndufo.” <verse eid="EZK 20:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 20:6" />Ke usen ado ami mmaanwọñọ nnọ ammọ mbo ke ñyaasịññe ammọ ke isọñ Iyib mben ñka ke isọñ se ami ñkeyem nnịm nnọ ammọ, isọñ a-afiọọrọke ye mmọọñeba ye adanakwọọk, isọñ ayaiyake akan afịd isọñ. <verse eid="EZK 20:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 20:7" />Ndin ami mmaabo ammọ nte, “Ndufo keedekeed, isaana mme ñkpọ ndek a-ndufo edịppeke anyen ese do iyaak, ikiinyʌñ isappa idem ndufo ye mme ubobodñkpọ Iyib. Ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ndufo.”<verse eid="EZK 20:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 20:8" />“ ‘Ado ammọ emaesọñ iwuod ye ami inyʌññọ ikpañ utọñ innọ miin; ammọ ikisaanake mme ñkpọ ndek a-ammọ ekedịppeke anyen ese iyaak, ikinyʌññọ ikpọñ mme ubobodñkpọ Iyib. Anam ami mmaabo ke ñyaanwañña ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk ammọ ñnyʌñ nduọk ammọ iyadesịd mmi ke Iyib. <verse eid="EZK 20:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 20:9" />Ado ke ntak anyịñ mmi, ami mmaasio ammọ ke Iyib. Ami ñkenam ami mbaak edisappa anyịñ mmi ke anyen mme idịd a-ammọ ekedʌñọke keed, a-adooho ami mmaayaara idem mmi nnọ nditọ Isrel ke iso ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 20:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 20:10" />Ke ntoro ami mmaasio ammọ ke Iyib ñnyʌñ mben ammọ ndʌk anaan. <verse eid="EZK 20:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 20:11" />Ami mmaanọ ammọ mme ewʌhọ mmi ñnyʌñ nnam ammọ ediọọñọ mme mbed mmi, a-adooho awo ake anam ammọ ayaadu uwem. <verse eid="EZK 20:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 20:12" />Ñko ami mmaanọ ammọ mme Sabad mmi nte idiọọñọ ke ufọọd ñnyịn, nọ ammọ ediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñkenam ammọ esana.<verse eid="EZK 20:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 20:13" />“ ‘Kpayeado nditọ Isrel emaesọñ iwuod ye ami ke anaan. Ammọ ikisañake ke mme ewʌhọ mmi, ado emaesịn mme mbed mmi, a-akenaaha nte ado awo a-anamma ammọ adu uwem; ndin ammọ emaenyʌñ enekke esappa mme Sabad mmi. Ke ntoro ami mmaabo ke ñyaakọọrọ ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk ammọ ñnyʌñ nsobo ammọ ke anaan. <verse eid="EZK 20:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 20:14" />Ado ke ntak anyịñ mmi ami mmaanam ñkpọ adikịt mbo ke awo isappake anye ke anyen mme idịd a-ami ñkesịññeke ammọ mfep. <verse eid="EZK 20:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 20:15" />Ami mmaanyʌñ mbenne ubọk ñnwọñọ nnọ ammọ ke anaan mbo ke ndiibenne ammọ ndʌk ke isọñ a-ami ñkenọọhọ ammọ, isọñ a-afiọọrọke ye mmọọñeba ye adanakwọọk, isọñ ayaiyake akan ke afịd isọñ; <verse eid="EZK 20:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 20:16" />sia ammọ emaesịn mme mbed mmi inyʌññọ isaña ke mme ewʌhọ mmi, enyʌñ esappa mme Sabad mmi; sia esịd ammọ akebịne ubobodñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 20:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 20:17" />Kpayeado ami mmaase ammọ ye mbọm, nsoboke ammọ ñnyʌññọ ñkweeñe ye ammọ ke anaan. <verse eid="EZK 20:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 20:18" />Ami mmaabo nditọ ammọ ke anaan nte, “Ikiisaña ke mme ewʌhọ mme ete ndufo, ikiinyʌñ inịm mme mbed ammọ, ikiinyʌñ isappa idem ndufo ye mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 20:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 20:19" />Ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ndufo; isaña ke mme ewʌhọ mmi inyʌñ inịm mme mbed mmi. <verse eid="EZK 20:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 20:20" />Inịm mme Sabad mmi esana, nọ ato do ammọ edo idiọọñọ ke ufọọd ñnyịn. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ndufo.”<verse eid="EZK 20:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 20:21" />“ ‘Ado nditọ ado emaesọñ iwuod ye ami: Ammọ ikisañake ke mme ewʌhọ mmi, ikiinyʌññọ ikpeme adinịm mme mbed mmi, a-ami ñkebooho, “Awo a-anamma ammọ ayaadu uwem ato ke ammọ,” ndin ammọ emaenyʌñ esappa mme Sabad mmi. Ke ntoro ami mmaabo ke ñyaakọọrọ ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk ammọ ñnyʌñ ñwọt ammọ iyadesịd mmi ke anaan. <verse eid="EZK 20:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 20:22" />Ado ami mmaamʌm ubọk mmi ñkama, ndin ke ntak anyịñ mmi ami mmaanam ñkpọ adikịt mbo ke awo isappake anye ke anyen mme idịd a-ami ñkesioho ammọ ke iso ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 20:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 20:23" />Ami mmaanyʌñ mbenne ubọk ñnwọñọ nnọ ammọ ke anaan ke ñyaabịn ammọ ndọñ ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ nsuan ammọ ndọñ ke mme abio, <verse eid="EZK 20:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 20:24" />sia ammọ imiikinamma mme mbed mmi ado esịn mme ewʌhọ mmi enyʌñ esappa mme Sabad mmi, anyen ammọ enyʌñ ekappa ese ubobodñkpọ mme ete ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 20:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 20:25" />Ndin ami mmaanọ ammọ mme ewʌhọ i-imiikifọnnọ ye mme mbed a-ammọ imiikikanna ikama idu uwem; <verse eid="EZK 20:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 20:26" />Ami mmaasappa ammọ ke mme enọ ammọ, uwa afịd akpa ayịn, nọ ato do nsịn ammọ ndịk ke idem nọ ammọ ediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’<verse eid="EZK 20:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 20:27" />“Ke ntoro, ayịn awo, tañ ikọ nọ mbon Isrel nyʌñ bo ammọ ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ntom ñko ke mme eteete ndufo ekensappa miin ke editre edinam akpanikọ ye ami. <verse eid="EZK 20:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 20:28" />Ke ini ami mmaakeben ammọ ndisịn ke isọñ a-ami ñkenwọñọke adinọ ammọ nọ ammọ ekekịt ñkoñ-ñkoñ abod me mfuud idak eto ndomokeed, ammọ emaewa mme uwa ammọ do, enam mme uwa e-ekedịppeke iyadesịd mmi, enọ anemufịk insensi ammọ enyʌñ enam mme unwọnwọñ uwa ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 20:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 20:29" />Ndin ami mmaabo ammọ nte: Nsoo ido ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie a-ndufo ekaaha mi?’ ” (Ekoot itie ado Bama<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20:29 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Bama </char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọñọ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie.</char></note> tutu asịm mfịn ami.)<verse eid="EZK 20:29" /></para>
  <para style="s1">E-emaana Edemme Asọñiwuod Mbon Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 20:30" />“Ke ntoro dọkkọ nditọ Isrel ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Nte ndufo eyaesappa idem ndufo naña mme eteete ndufo ekenam enyʌñ ekeene mme ñkpọ ndek ammọ? <verse eid="EZK 20:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 20:31" />Ndufo emaenọ enọ ndufo, adiwa nditọ ndufo ke ikañ, ndufo esʌk eka iso esappa idem ndufo ye afịd ubobodñkpọ ndufo tutu usen mfịn ami. Nte ami ñyaayaak ndufo embịp miin ñkpọ, ndufo mbon Isrel? Ke adaña ini ami nduuho uwem, ami ndiiyakka ndufo embịp miin ñkpọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 20:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 20:32" />“ ‘Ndufo ebo ete, “Ñnyịn iyem adiba nte mme idịd, nte mbon ederimbod, e-enamma ñkpọ enọ eto ye itiad.” Ado se ndufo enie ke esịd idiitịppeke tutu amama. <verse eid="EZK 20:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 20:33" />Ke adaña ini ami nduuho uwem, ami ndiikara ndufo ke akpọsọñ ubọk ye ke adinyanna ubọk ye ifiobesịd, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 20:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 20:34" />Ami ñyaidat ndufo nto ke mme idịd ye mme abio se ndufo ekesuana ekaa, ke akpọsọñ ubọk ye adinyanna ubọk ye ifiobesịd. <verse eid="EZK 20:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 20:35" />Ami ñyaidat ndufo ndʌk anaan mme idịd, ñnyʌñ ñkpe ikpe do ye ndufo iso ye iso. <verse eid="EZK 20:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 20:36" />Kpa naña ami ñkekpe ikpe ye mme eteete ndufo ke anaan ke isọñ Iyib, kpa ntoro ke ndiikpe ikpe ye ndufo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 20:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 20:37" />Ami ñyaatịñ anyen nse naña ndufo ediisaña iboiyo ke idak esañ mmi, ñnyʌñ isịn ndufo ke ñwed edioomo. <verse eid="EZK 20:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 20:38" />Ami ñyaasịññe mbon nsọñiwuod ye mbon se inam ntịme ye ami ke atu ndufo mfep. Akpesʌkado adooho ami ñyaasio ammọ ke isọñ a-ammọ edʌññọ, ammọ idiidʌkkọ isọñ Isrel. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="EZK 20:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 20:39" />“ ‘Amaado ndufo, mbon Isrel, se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ikaa ikikpono mme ubobodñkpọ ndufo, afịd ndufo! Ado amaama ke akpanikọ ndufo eyaekpañ utọñ ennọ miin, idiinyʌññọ isappa adisana anyịñ mmi aba ke mme enọ ye mme ubobodñkpọ ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 20:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 20:40" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara anọ uyio, sia ke adisana ekamba abod mmi, ñkoñ-ñkoñ ekamba abod Isrel, do ke isọñ ado afịd mbon Isrel eyaenam ñkpọ ennọ miin, ndin ami ñyaanyịmme ammọ, nnem esịd ye ammọ. Do ñko ke ami ndiiyem mme uwa ndufo ye mme nti enọ ndufo, ye afịd ndisana uwa ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 20:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 20:41" />Ami ñyaidat ndufo nte anemufịk insensi ke ini mmaisio ndufo ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ itañ ndufo ke mme abio e-ekisuanna ndufo, ndin ñyaawọt idem mmi nte adisana ke atu ndufo ke anyen mme idịd. <verse eid="EZK 20:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 20:42" />Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke mmaiben ndufo ndʌk isọñ Isrel, isọñ a-ami ñkedịppeke ubọk ñnwọñọ adinọ mme eteete ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 20:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 20:43" />Do ke ndufo ediitoiyo usʌñ ndufo ye afịd se ekenam esappa idem ndufo, ndin eyaesua idem ndufo ebaña afịd ndiọi se ekenam. <verse eid="EZK 20:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 20:44" />Ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini mmainam ndufo nọ asaña akekem ye anyịñ mmi, isañake ye idiọọk usʌñ ndufo ye mbiara adinam ndufo, ndufo mbon Isrel, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 20:44" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi A-abañake Usuuk</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 20:45" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 20:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 20:46" />“Ayịn awo, wuuk iso mfo se ukañ usuuk; kwọrọ ikọ dian usuuk nyʌñ tañ prọfesi dian akai isọñ usuuk. <verse eid="EZK 20:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 20:47" />Bo akai isọñ usuuk ate: ‘Kop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaakịm ikañ usịn fiin, ndin anye ayaata afịd eto mfo, nseghe ye nsaad. Ikañ ado idiinịmeke, ndin ayaata afịd iso, tọọñọ ke usuuk tutu asịm adoro. <verse eid="EZK 20:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 20:48" />Afịd awo eyaekịt ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñkesịn ikañ ado; anye idiinịmeke.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 20:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 20:49" />Ndin ami mmaabo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Andikara ammọ e-etañ embaña miin ebo, ‘Nte idooho ntəño-ntəño ñkaña ñke ke anye atop?’ ”<verse eid="EZK 20:49" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 20" />
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="EZK 21" />
  <para style="s1">Babilọn nte Akañkañ Ubiereikpe Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">21: </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke mme ikpañwed Hibru ewet Esi 21:1-32 nte Esi 21:6-37. </char>
    </note> <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 21:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 21:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 21:2" />“Ayịn awo, wuuk iso mfo se Yeruselem nyʌñ kwọrọ ikọ dian adisana itie. Tañ prọfesi dian isọñ Isrel <verse eid="EZK 21:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 21:3" />nyʌñ bo isọñ Isrel ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ ado ami: Ami ndaaha ye afo. Ami ñyaadʌt akañkañ mmi nsio ke efọk ñnyʌñ ñkpok ndinen awo ye mbon ibak nsio ke ufọọd mfo. <verse eid="EZK 21:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 21:4" />Sia adooho ñyaakpok ndinen awo ye mbon ibak, akañkañ mmi ayaawuọ ke efọk adiana afịd awo tọọñọ ke usuuk tutu asịm adoro. <verse eid="EZK 21:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 21:5" />Ndin afịd awo eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmesio akañkañ mmi ke efọk; anye idiitịmmeke idʌk aba.’<verse eid="EZK 21:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 21:6" />“Ke ntoro, ayịn awo, mịm mmịm! Mịm ke iso ammọ ye ibʌññọ esịd ye adiyịk-adiyịk mfʌhọ. <verse eid="EZK 21:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 21:7" />Ndin ammọ emaubịp fiin ibo, ‘Nsoo ido nọ afo amịm mmịm?’ afo ayaabo ammọ ate, ‘Ke ntak etob a-adiighe. Afịd esịd ayaayeeme ye ndịk, afịd ubọk ayaanyʌñ atọ atekke, ikịm ayaanyʌñ awaaña awo adiaat ke afịd ukod.’ Asʌk adi! Ke akpanikọ ayaatịppe, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo.”<verse eid="EZK 21:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 21:8" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 21:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 21:9" />“Ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:9">“ ‘Akañkañ, akañkañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:9">emaeban, emaenyʌñ etʌk,<verse eid="EZK 21:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 21:10" />emaeban anye ebeeñe enịm enọ uwot awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:10">emaetʌk anye nọ asem nte akebkeb!</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 21:10">“ ‘Nte ana ñnyịn idaara ke esañubọọñ ayịn ubọọñ mmi? Akañkañ asasua afịd utọ eto ado.<verse eid="EZK 21:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 21:11" />“ ‘Akena nte etọtʌk akañkañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:11">nọ ato do emọmʌm anye ke ubọk;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:11">ebaban enyʌñ etọtʌk anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:11">nọ ato do eben anye esịn ke ubọk awodawo.<verse eid="EZK 21:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 21:12" />Ayịn awo tua, bọñ ñkpo nyʌñ seeme,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:12">sia adiidoro ikọd mmi ke idem;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:12">adiidoro afịd nditọ ideen abọọñ Isrel ke idem.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:12">Etop ammọ eyak enọ akañkañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:12">ye ikọd mmi ñko.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:12">Ke ntoro, mia esịd mfo.<verse eid="EZK 21:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 21:13" />“ ‘Idomo idiitreketre adidi. Ndin nsoo idiido adieke esañubọọñ a-akañkañ imiimaaha imiikaaha iso? <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’<verse eid="EZK 21:13" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 21:14" />“Ke ntoro, ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">nyʌñ mia ubọk mfo iba.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:14">Yak akañkañ asobo akañ iba,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">akpekọm akañ ita.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:14">Ado akañkañ uwot awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">akañkañ akwa uwot awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">anye akanna ammọ akʌk.<verse eid="EZK 21:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 21:15" />Nọ ato do esịd aduọ mme awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:15">ñkpañña enyʌñ ewak,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:15">ami mmenịm akañkañ nnọ uwodawo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:15">ke afịd inuaatob ammọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:15">Se! E-enam anye akeppe nte akebkeb,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:15">e-eben anye ekama nọ ewot awo.<verse eid="EZK 21:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 21:16" />Afo akañkañ, kpịkke nọ nnasia,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:16">ndin kpịkke nọ ufiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:16">nte adodo i-iso ikwa mfo awọññọke aka.<verse eid="EZK 21:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 21:17" />Ami ñko ñyaamia ubọk mmi iba,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:17">ndin ifiobesịd mmi ayaasuuhọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:17">Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ntañ.”<verse eid="EZK 21:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 21:18" />Uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 21:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 21:19" />“Ayịn awo, siak akpọusʌñ iba nọ akañkañ adidem Babilọn asaña, naña ammọ mba etọọñọ ke ukem idịd. Nam idiọọñọ nịm ke itie nte usʌñ ado awakka adʌk abio. <verse eid="EZK 21:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 21:20" />Siak usʌñ keed nọ akañkañ aka Raba mbon Amọn, ye keed mfen nọ aka Yuda ye Yeruselem akpọsọñ abio. <verse eid="EZK 21:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 21:21" />Sia adidem Babilọn ayaasọñọ ada ke ñwaaña usʌñ ado, ke iwuod akpọusʌñ iba ado, adibre idiọñ nọ adiọọñọ se idiitịppe ke ini iso. Anye ayaakama mme idañ asịn afia, anye ayaakaa nduuñọ ke atu mme ubobodñkpọ amọ, anye ayaaduuño ati. <verse eid="EZK 21:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 21:22" />Afia ayaasio Yeruselem ke ubọk nnasia amọ, do ke anye adiinịm ñkpọ uwuut ndibene, itie se ediinọ uyio ibo ewot awo, adisio ñkpo ekọñ, adinịm ñkpọ uwuut ndibene mbaha mme inuaatob, adibọp usʌñ ñnyʌñ ndaaha nnaekọñ. <verse eid="EZK 21:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 21:23" />Anye adiiba nte nsu-nsu idiọọñọ anọ mbon se ikikaaña akaaña ye anye, ado anye ayaatoiyo ammọ mme ndudue ammọ anyʌñ adat ado asịn ammọ ukad.<verse eid="EZK 21:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 21:24" />“Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: ‘Sia ndufo emenam awo atoiyo mme ndudue ndufo ato ke nsọñiwuod ndufo, ndufo eyaara mme idiọọkñkpọ ndufo ke afịd se ndufo enam; sia ndufo emenam ami, eyaisịn ndufo ukad.<verse eid="EZK 21:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 21:25" />“ ‘Afo idiọọk ye ibak akpanabọọñ Isrel, u-usen mfo amaadikem, i-ini ufen mfo amaadiyọhọ iduọiyọ, <verse eid="EZK 21:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 21:26" />se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Yaara tọban, yaara anyanya. Idiidooho naña akesido aba. Eyaebenne mbon usuuhọ itie enyʌñ esuuhọ mbon se ikiba ke ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie. <verse eid="EZK 21:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 21:27" />Nsobo! Nsobo! Ami ñyaanam anye ado nsobo! Anyanya idiibaaha aba tutu ataa andinie amọ adi; anye ke ndiiyaak nnọ.’<verse eid="EZK 21:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 21:28" />“Ndin afo, ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami ke abaña nditọ Amọn ye mme usọñanyen ammọ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:28">“ ‘Akañkañ, akañkañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:28">e-esiooho ebo awot awo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:28">e-etʌkkọ anye nọ adia awo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:28">anyʌñ amịneñ nte akebkeb!<verse eid="EZK 21:28" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 21:29" />Kpa ye nsu-nsu ñkukịd e-ekịtte ubaña fiin</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:29">ye abiaña idiọñ e-ebreke ubaña fiin,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:29">ediiben anye idot ke mme itọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:29">mbon ibak e-eyemme ediwot,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:29">a-adooho usen ammọ adikem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:29">a-adooho ini ufen ammọ amaayọhọ aduọi.<verse eid="EZK 21:29" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 21:30" />“ ‘Yak akañkañ atịmme anyọñ efọk amọ.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:30">Ke itie e-ekubotto fiin,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:30">ke isọñ emana mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:30">ami ñyaakpe ikpe mfo.<verse eid="EZK 21:30" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 21:31" />Ami ñyaanwañña ifiobesịd mmi ufʌk fiin</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:31">ñnyʌñ mfuud ikañ iyadesịd mmi uduọk fiin;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:31">ami ñyauyaak fiin nsịn ke ubọk mbon afai,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:31">mbon e-enieghe ifiọk ebaña nsobo.<verse eid="EZK 21:31" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 21:32" />Afo ayaado ifia anọ ikañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:32">eyaeduọk iyiib mfo ke isọñ emana mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:32">awo iduutoiyoke fiin aba;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:32">sia ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmetañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 21:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 21" />
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="EZK 22" />
  <para style="s1">Ubiereikpe ke Abaña Ndiọiñkpọ Yeruselem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 22:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate:<verse eid="EZK 22:1" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 22:2" />“Ayịn awo, afo ayaakpe ikpe amọ? Nte afo ayaakpe ikpe abio uduọk iyiib ami? Akpedo ntoro, ben afịd mbubiam adinam amọ wọt anye <verse eid="EZK 22:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 22:3" />nyʌñ bo ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Afo abio a-abenne nsobo anọọ idem mfo ke adiduọk iyiib ke esịd mfo ñnyʌñ nsappa idem ke adibot mme ubobodñkpọ, <verse eid="EZK 22:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 22:4" />afo amedue ke ntak iyiib a-afo aduọkkọ; ñko amenyʌñ akappa ado se emaesappa ke ntak mme ubobodñkpọ a-afo abotto. Afo amenam usen mfo aməho, ndin utịd mme isua mfo adiwuọ. Ke ntoro ami ñyaanam afo ado ñkpọ asuenne ke iso mme idịd anyʌñ ado ñkpọ nsaha ke iso afịd mme abio. <verse eid="EZK 22:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 22:5" />Mbon se ikpere ye mbon se iba ke anyan usʌñ eyauduọi fiin, afo idiọọk abio ami, a-ayọhọke ye ndutịme.<verse eid="EZK 22:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 22:6" />“ ‘Se naña nditọ ideen abọọñ keedekeed ke Isrel e-ebaaha ke ufọọd mfo ekama adudu ammọ eduọk iyiib. <verse eid="EZK 22:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 22:7" />Ammọ emiom ete ye eka ke ufọọd mfo; ammọ efiik asenawo enyʌñ etʌkkọ ayịnakpa ye ebekpa ke ufọọd mfo. <verse eid="EZK 22:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 22:8" />Afo amesịn mme ndisana ñkpọ mmi ke ndek anyʌñ asappa mme Sabad mmi. <verse eid="EZK 22:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 22:9" />Mbon se ibia mbia nọ ato do eduọk iyiib mmọ eba ke ufọọd mfo; mbon se idia ñkpọ ke mme ñwommo anyọñ abod inyʌñ inañña mbubiam ido mmọ eba ke ufọọd mfo. <verse eid="EZK 22:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 22:10" />Mbon se isuenne ñkpana nnaa ete ammọ mmọ eba ke ufọọd mfo; mbon se isappa ibaan idaha ebaaha ke itieisọñ ke ini ammọ imiisanake mmọ eba ke ufọọd mfo. <verse eid="EZK 22:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 22:11" />Awodeen keed asappa anwaan mbọhọidʌñ amọ, mfen asappa anwaan ayịn amọ ikoppo abuud, mfen anyʌñ asappa ayịneka amọ awonwaan, ataa ayịn e-ete amọ abonno, mmọdo eba kpa ke ufọọd mfo. <verse eid="EZK 22:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 22:12" />Mbon se ibọ ubọkedem nọ ato do eduọk iyiib mmọ ke ufọọd mfo; afo abọ uweene udod. Afo adia idiọọk udod ato mbọhọidʌñ mfo. Ndin afo amemfre miin, Abọọñ Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 22:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 22:13" />“ ‘Ke akpanikọ ñyaamia ubọk mmi mbaña idiọọk udod a-afo adiaha ye iyiib a-afo aduọkkọ ke ufọọd mfo. <verse eid="EZK 22:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 22:14" />Nte afo ayaasọñ esịd me ubọk mfo ayaasọọñọ ke usen a-ami nduunam fiin ñkpọ? Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmetañ, ndin ñyaanyʌñ nnam. <verse eid="EZK 22:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 22:15" />Ami ñyausuan fiin ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ usuan ndọñ ke mme abio; ñnyʌñ nnam ndek mfo atre. <verse eid="EZK 22:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 22:16" />Ke ini emausappa fiin ema ke anyen mme idịd, afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 22:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 22:17" />Ndin ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 22:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 22:18" />“Ayịn awo, ufọk Isrel ibaaha ufọn aba innọ miin; afịd ammọ edo kọpa, ye tian, ye ukwak ye leed e-eyaaha esịn ke esịd ñkpọdiọhọ ikañ. Ammọ edo nduwai silfa. <verse eid="EZK 22:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 22:19" />Ke ntoro, se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: ‘Sia afịd ndufo emaekappa nduwai, ami ñyaitañ ndufo mbok ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="EZK 22:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 22:20" />Kpa naña etañ silfa, kọpa, ukwak, leed ye tian edọñ ke ikañ nọ ammọ etara akeene akpọsọñ ufiob, kpa ntoro ke ami ndiikoono ndufo ke iyadesịd ye ifiobesịd mmi ndọñ ke esịd abio ñnyʌñ nnam ndufo etara. <verse eid="EZK 22:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 22:21" />Ami ñyaikoono ndufo mbok ñnyʌñ ifuut ndufo ke ikañ ifiobesịd mmi, ndin ndufo eyaetara ke esịd amọ. <verse eid="EZK 22:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 22:22" />Kpa naña silfa atara ke ikañ, ntoro ke ndufo ediitara ke esịd amọ, ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmenwañña ifiobesịd mmi ifʌk ndufo.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 22:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 22:23" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaamaana adinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 22:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 22:24" />“Ayịn awo, dọkkọ isọñ bo ate, ‘Afo ado isọñ a-awo imiinamma asana, edịm inyʌññọ idep iduọkkọ ke usen ifiobesịd.’ <verse eid="EZK 22:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 22:25" />Nditọ ideen abọọñ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22:25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Septuakin; ke Hibru </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mme aku</char></note>, mme adaiwuod amọ, edʌk adu ke esịd amọ nte ekpe akuun ke ini awaiya se anye amʌm; ammọ eta mme awo, ekoono inie ye ñkpọuto enyʌñ enam mme ebekpa ewak ke esịd amọ. <verse eid="EZK 22:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 22:26" />Mme aku amọ ebiat mbed mmi enyʌñ esappa mme ndisana ñkpọ mmi; ammọ ikịtte ukpʌhọde ke ufọọd adisana ñkpọ ye ñkaña ñkpọ; ammọ ekpeep mme awo ebo ke ukpʌhọde ibaaha ke ufọọd se isana ye se imiisanake; ndin ammọ enyʌñ ebọọp anyen ebaña mme Sabad mmi, anam ammọ ensịn miin ke ndek ke atu ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 22:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 22:27" />Mme ikpọawo amọ eba nte mme ewaikọd ewai unam; ammọ eduọk iyiib enyʌñ ewot mme awo nọ ato do edia idiọọk udod. <verse eid="EZK 22:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 22:28" />Mme prọfed amọ ekama nsu-nsu ñkukịd ye idiọñ abiaña efʌk mme adinam ami. Ammọ ebo ete, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami’ ke ini <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> imiitañña. <verse eid="EZK 22:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 22:29" />Mbon isọñ ado ewo ñwo enyʌñ eyịp inọ; ammọ efiik mme uweene ye mbon unana enyʌñ ediọọk mme isenawo ukama, inọọhọ ammọ unen ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 22:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 22:30" />“Ami mmaayem awo ke atu ammọ se ikeme adibọp akọ inyʌñ ida ke iwuod isọñ ado ke iso mmi ke itie nte awuudo mbaak ami ndisobo anye, ado ami ñkekịtte awo ndomokeed. <verse eid="EZK 22:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 22:31" />Ke ntoro ami ñyaanwañña ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk ammọ ñnyʌñ nsobo ammọ ke ikañ iyadesịd mmi, ñnyʌñ mben afịd se ammọ ekenam ndot ammọ ke iwuod, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 22:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 22" />
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="EZK 23" />
  <para style="s1">Mme Asịnefịbe Nditọeka Ibaan Iba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 23:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 23:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 23:2" />“Ayịn awo, ibaan iba ekeba, nditọeka keed. <verse eid="EZK 23:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 23:3" />Ammọ emaekappa ibaan akpara ke Iyib, esaña akpara tọọñọ ke uyịn ammọ. Ke isọñ ado emaefiọññọ ammọ eba enyʌñ enuak eba uyịn ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 23:4" />Adiaha akekere Ohola, ñnwa akekere Oholiba. Ammọ ekedo ake mmi enyʌñ emaan nditọ ideen ye ibaan. Ohola ado Sameria, ndin Oholiba ado Yeruselem.<verse eid="EZK 23:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 23:5" />“Ohola akesaña akpara tọọñọ naña akesʌkkọ ado ake mmi; itọñ mbon ima amọ, mbon ekọñ Asiria amaadọñ anye <verse eid="EZK 23:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 23:6" />e-ekesiineke bru afọñ ke idem, mme adaukara ye mme adaiso ekọñ, afịd ammọ mfọọn ñkparawa, ye mme awad enañmbakara. <verse eid="EZK 23:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 23:7" />Anye amaaben idem amọ anọ afịd mme awuọiso awo ke Asiria nte akpara anyʌñ asappa idem amọ ye mme ubobodñkpọ afịd awo a-anye akenieghe udọñ abʌkidem anọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 23:8" />Anye ikisịññeke idem ikpọñ usaña akpara a-anye aketọọñọke ke Iyib ye mme ideen ekesinaaha ye anye ke ini uyịn amọ, enuak eba uyịn amọ enyʌñ enwañña udọñ abʌkidem ammọ efʌk anye ke idem.<verse eid="EZK 23:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 23:9" />“Ke ntoro ami mmaayaak anye nsịn ke ubọk mbon ima amọ, mbon Asiria, i-itọñ ammọ akedọññọ anye. <verse eid="EZK 23:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 23:10" />Ammọ emaesuuk anye ifed, ekoono nditọ amọ ideen ye ibaan enyʌñ ewot anye ke akañkañ. Anye amaakappa ado ufiid ke atu ibaan, ndin emaenọ anye ufen.<verse eid="EZK 23:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 23:11" />“Ayịneka amọ Oholiba amaakịt ami, kpayeado anye amaanam use ye akpara akan ayịneka amọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 23:12" />Anye ñko amaanie idiọọk udọñ anọ mbon Asiria, mme adaukara ye mme adaiso ekọñ, mbon ekọñ e-esịneke ayọhọ afọñ ekọñ, mbon e-ewatta enañmbakara, afịd ammọ mfọọn ñkparawa. <verse eid="EZK 23:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 23:13" />Ami mmaakịt ke anye ñko amaasappa idem amọ; ammọ awo iba ekenie ukem ido.<verse eid="EZK 23:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 23:14" />“Ado anye amaakaa iso asaña akpara amọ. Anye amaakịt ideen nte ekewette ke ndibene, ubobodñkpọ mbon Kaldi<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mbon Babilọn</char></note> e-ekewette ke ndad-ndad, <verse eid="EZK 23:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 23:15" />mme ñkpaha ke isịn ye nduọ-nduọ tọban ke iwuod ammọ; afịd ammọ ekebit mme etubom mbon ekọñ Babilọn, ubon mbon Kaldi<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23:15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mbon Babilọn;</char><char style="ft" closed="false">se ñko ke Esi 23:16</char></note>. <verse eid="EZK 23:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 23:16" />Anye akesʌk akekịt ammọ, anye amaanie udọñ efịbe abaña ammọ ndin adọñ mme isʌñutom ebịne ammọ ke Kaldi. <verse eid="EZK 23:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 23:17" />Ndin mbon Babilọn emaedi ebịne anye, edina ke ikʌk ima ye anye, enyʌñ esappa anye ke ido efịbe ammọ. Ke ammọ emaekesappa anye ema, anye amaadakka akpọñ ammọ ye akpọsọñ itekesịd. <verse eid="EZK 23:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 23:18" />Ke ini anye akesʌkkọ akaiso asaña akpara amọ anwa-anwa anyʌñ anịm idem amọ ifed, anye amandooro miin ke itekesịd, kpa naña ayịneka amọ akendooro. <verse eid="EZK 23:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 23:19" />Kpayeado anye amaanenekke anam ido efịbe, anyʌñ atoiyo mme usen uyịn amọ, idaha anye akedooho akpara ke Iyib. <verse eid="EZK 23:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 23:20" />Do, anye amaanie udọñ use anọ mbon ima amọ, i-idem ideen ammọ ekebaaha nte ake dọñki, a-nsene ammọ akenyʌññọ awuọ nte ake enañmbakara. <verse eid="EZK 23:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 23:21" />Ke ntoro afo amaakappa anie udọñ anọ abʌd-abʌd ido ini uyịn mfo, ke ini afo akebaaha ke Iyib e-ekufiọññọke ikpanesịd enyʌñ unuak ñkpʌk eba mfo.<verse eid="EZK 23:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 23:22" />“Ke ntoro, Oholiba, se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaademme usua ke esịd mbon ima mfo ubaña fiin; mbon e-ekudooroke fiin, ñyaanyʌñ ñkoono ammọ ke afịd ñkanñkʌk ubịne fiin, <verse eid="EZK 23:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 23:23" />mbon Babilọn ye afịd mbon Kaldi, ideen Pekod ye Soa ye Koa, ye afịd mbon Asiria se ikiba ye ammọ, mfọọn ñkparawa, afịd ammọ mme adaukara ye mme adaiso ekọñ, mme etubom mbon ekọñ ye mme awuọiso awo, afịd ammọ ewat ke enañmbakara. <verse eid="EZK 23:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 23:24" />Ammọ eyaedi ubịne fiin ye ñkpọ ekọñ, sariọd ye wakọn ye uwak atu awo; ammọ eyaukanna fiin ekʌk ye ikpọ ye ntək atuekọñ ye itam ukwak enwana ekọñ ye afo. Ami ñyauyaak fiin nnọ ammọ nọ umia ufen, ndin ammọ eyaumia fiin ufen naña asaña akekem ye ido ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 23:25" />Ami ñyaadat ufịb mmi nnam ikọ ye afo ke iyadesịd, ndin ammọ eyaunam fiin ñkpọ ke ifiobesịd. Ammọ eyaekpịkke mme iwuo ye utọñ ndufo esio, ndin ndufo se isʌhọ eyaekpa ke akañkañ. Ammọ eyaekoono nditọ ndufo ideen ye ibaan enyọñ, ndin ikañ ayaita ndufo se isʌhọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 23:26" />Ammọ eyaenyʌñ usịññe fiin afọñidem usuuk ifed enyʌñ ekoono ñkpọ mbanaidem mfo. <verse eid="EZK 23:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 23:27" />Ke ntoro ami ñyaatre abʌd-abʌd ido ye efịbe a-afo aketọọñọke ke Iyib. Afo uduubenneke anyen mfo use ammọ aba, uduunyʌññọ utoiyo Iyib aba.<verse eid="EZK 23:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 23:28" />“Sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ntom: Ami ñyem uyaak fiin nsịn ke ubọk mbon afo asuaha, ke ubọk mbon emaekudooro fiin. <verse eid="EZK 23:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 23:29" />Ammọ eyaunam fiin ñkpọ usua-usua enyʌñ ubọ afịd se akenwana. Ammọ eyauyaak edaaha ataa ifed, ndin eyaeyaara asuenne akpara mfo. Abʌd-abʌd uwem ye use mfo <verse eid="EZK 23:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 23:30" />edat ami usọk fiin, sia afo amaanam use ye mme idịd anyʌñ asappa idem mfo ye mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 23:31" />Afo asaña ke ikpadisañ ayịneka mfo awonwaan; ke ntoro ami ñyaaben kọọb amọ usịn fiin ke ubọk.<verse eid="EZK 23:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 23:32" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 23:32">“Afo ayaanwọñ kọọb ayịneka mfo awonwaan,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:32">ekamba ñnwaña ye ntotəño kọọb;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 23:32">anye ayaadat nsaha ye asuenne adi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:32">sia anye akama uwak ñkpọ.<verse eid="EZK 23:32" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 23:33" />Afo ayaakpa mmịn ye mfʌhọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:33">kọọb ñwuudo ye atahade,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:33">kọọb Sameria ayịneka mfo.<verse eid="EZK 23:33" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 23:34" />Afo ayaanwọñ anyʌñ adai anye asat,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:34">anyʌñ ata ñwai amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:34">afo ayaanyʌñ awai eba mfo.</para>
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 23:34">Ami mmetañ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 23:34" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 23:35" />“Ke ntoro, se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Sia afo umaumfre miin unyʌñ ukpa edem uñwọt, ana afo abiom ufen abʌd-abʌd ido mfo ye usaña akpara mfo.”<verse eid="EZK 23:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 23:36" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amambo miin ate: “Ayịn awo, afo ayaakpe ikpe anọ Ohola ye Oholiba? Akpedo ntoro ben mme mbubiam adinam ammọ wọt ammọ, <verse eid="EZK 23:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 23:37" />sia ammọ esịn efịbe ñko iyiib anyʌñ ayere ammọ ke ubọk. Ammọ emaesịn efịbe ye mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ; ammọ emaeben nditọ a-ammọ ekemanna ennọọ miin enam uwa, nte ndidia ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 23:38" />Ammọ emaenyʌñ ennam miin ñkpọ ami ñko: Kpa ke ukem ini ado ammọ emaesappa adisana itie mmi enyʌñ ebiat mme Sabad mmi. <verse eid="EZK 23:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 23:39" />Ukem usen a-ammọ ekewaaha nditọ ammọ enọ mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ do, ammọ emaedʌk esappa adisana itie mmi. Se ammọ ekenam ke ufọk mmi ado ado.<verse eid="EZK 23:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 23:40" />“Ñko ammọ emaedọñ mme isʌñutom ekekoot mme awo ke anyan idịd, ndin ke ini ammọ emaekedi afo amaayie idem mfo, adeppe ñkpọ ke anyen anyʌñ adat ñkpọ mbanaidem abana idem mfo anọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 23:41" />Afo amaatie ke uyaiya ñkpọitie, ediọọk akpokoro ke iso amọ, ndin afo amaadot insensi ye adan ọlif mmi ke anyọñ akpokoro ado.<verse eid="EZK 23:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 23:42" />“Uyom atu awo e-ebaaha ke ifuuro amaaba akanna anye; emaekoono mme akpammịn eto ke akpautatan edi enyʌñ ekoono mbon ntịme ke idʌñ edi, ammọ emaenyʌñ esịn awonwaan ado ye ayịneka amọ akpohoubọk ke ubọk enyʌñ eyat ammọ mfọọn anyanya ke iwuod. <verse eid="EZK 23:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 23:43" />Ndin ami mmaatañ mbaña anye a-amaakebiaña ato usịn efịbe nte, ‘Yak ammọ ekama anye nte akpara, sia kpa ado ke anye ado.’ <verse eid="EZK 23:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 23:44" />Ndin ammọ emaenaa ye anye. Kpa naña ideen esina ye akpara, ntoro ke ammọ ekenaa ye mme abʌd-abʌd ibaan ado, Ohola ye Oholiba. <verse eid="EZK 23:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 23:45" />Ado ndinen mme akpeikpe eyaekpe ikpe ammọ enyʌñ enọ ammọ ufen naña akem ye ufen ibaan e-esịnne efịbe enyʌñ eduọk iyiib, sia ammọ edo mme asịn efịbe, iyiib anyʌñ asịne ammọ ke ubọk.<verse eid="EZK 23:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 23:46" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ben ekamba atu awo bịne ammọ nyʌñ yaak ammọ nọ enam ñkpọndịk ye ammọ enyʌñ eyiip ñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 23:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 23:47" />Atu awo ado eyaetọọñ ammọ ke itiad enyʌñ ekpok ammọ ke akañkañ ammọ; eyaewot nditọ ideen ye nditọ ibaan ammọ enyʌñ efọọmọ ufọk ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 23:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 23:48" />“Ntoro ke ami ndiinam abʌd-abʌd ido atre ke isọñ ado, mbaak afịd ibaan edat ukpeebñkpọ, ke enyʌñ ekeene ammọ edem. <verse eid="EZK 23:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 23:49" />Ndufo eyaebọ ufen abʌd-abʌd ido ndufo enyʌñ ebiom mbiomo idiọọkñkpọ a-ndufo enamma ke adikpono ubobodñkpọ. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara.”<verse eid="EZK 23:49" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 23" />
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="EZK 24" />
  <para style="s1">Yeruselem nte Ako Utem Ñkpọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 24:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua usʌkkeed, ke ayọhọ afiọñ duob ke ayọhọ usen duob, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 24:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 24:2" />“Ayịn awo, wet usen afiọñ mfịn ami nịm, kpa usen afiọñ mfịn ami, sia adidem Babilọn a-asiak ekọñ ye Yeruselem kpa usen mfịn ami. <verse eid="EZK 24:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 24:3" />Top ntəño-ntəño ñke nọ mbon nsọñiwuod ami bo ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:3">“ ‘Dot ako ke ikañ; dot ako</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:3">nyʌñ nwañña mmọọñ sịn ke esịd.<verse eid="EZK 24:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 24:4" />Tañ mme mbio unam dọñ ke esịd,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:4">afịd nti itie unam, ukod ye afara.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:4">Koono ataa nti akpọ dọñ ke esịd amọ nọ ayọhọ;<verse eid="EZK 24:4" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 24:5" />dat ataa eti edọñ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:5">Dọñ ifia ke idak amọ nọ mme akpọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:5">nekke tem anye nọ afịd</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:5">nyʌñ tem mme akpọ ke esịd ado ñko.<verse eid="EZK 24:5" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 24:6" />“ ‘Sia se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:6">“ ‘Adọdiọọk anọ abio uduọkiyiib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:6">ako a-atakka ñkarafañ idahami,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:6">a-ñkarafañ ado imiidiidiaññake!</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:6">Sịññe unam ado ñkukʌk keedekeed,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:6">kuusaasat ndomokeed.<verse eid="EZK 24:6" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 24:7" />“ ‘Sia iyiib a-anye akeduọkkọ mmọdo asịne ke ufọọd amọ:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:7">Anye akeduọk anye ke nsaad ekamba itiad;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:7">anye ikiduọkkọ ke isọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:7">se ntọñ akpekefʌk.<verse eid="EZK 24:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 24:8" />Nọ ifiobesịd adọọk nọ enyʌñ esio usiene;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:8">ami ñkeduọk iyiib amọ ke nsaad ekamba itiad,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:8">mbaak edifʌk anye.<verse eid="EZK 24:8" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 24:9" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:9">“ ‘Adọdiọọk anọ abio uduọk iyiib!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:9">Ami ñko ñyaakọọk eboho ifia ikañ akoñ.<verse eid="EZK 24:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 24:10" />Ke ntoro kọọk ifia nọ awak,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:10">nyʌñ bara ikañ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:10">Tem unam ado nọ afọn,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:10">waaha mme ñkpadia;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:10">nyʌñ fọp mme akpọ yak asak.<verse eid="EZK 24:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 24:11" />Ndin tem ñkaña ako ke ikañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:11">tutu anye afiop anyʌñ adat,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:11">nọ ato do ndek amọ atara,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:11">ikañ anyʌñ ata ñkarafañ amọ afịd asio.<verse eid="EZK 24:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 24:12" />Afịd ufen ado ke ikpu-ikpu;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:12">ekamba ñkarafañ amọ imaaha adiwuọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:12">kpak ikañ ikanna isio anye.<verse eid="EZK 24:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 24:13" />“ ‘Ndek mfo ado abʌd-abʌd ido mfo. Sia ami mmaanwana adinam yak afo asana ado afo umaaha isana, afo uduusanake aba tutu ifiobesịd mmi ye afo asuuhọ.<verse eid="EZK 24:13" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 24:14" />“ ‘Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmetañ. Ini akem ami adinam ñkpọ. Ami ndiitreke adinam; ndiikoppo mbọm, ndiinyʌññọ ntua ñkpọfiọk. Ediikpe ikpe mfo ikeene ido mfo ye mme adinam mfo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 24:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Anwaan Esikeel Akpa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 24:15" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 24:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 24:16" />“Ayịn awo, ñyaaben eta ubọk keed nsobo se anyen mfo ama ataa eti-eti. Ado kuuseeme, kuunyʌñ utua, kuunyʌñ uyak mmọọñayịd uwuọ ke anyen. <verse eid="EZK 24:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 24:17" />Seeme ke ndobuyio; kuufʌhọ unọọ mme akpañkpa. Kaa iso tobo tọban mfo nọ asọñ nyʌñ sịne ikpaukod mfo ke ukod; kuufʌk ñwainua ye ñwaebek mfo, kuunyʌñ udia ndidia mbon ufʌk ikpo.”<verse eid="EZK 24:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 24:18" />Ndin ami mmaatañ ikọ nnọ afịd awo ubakusen, ndin akesịm ndubiayio anwaan mmi amaakpa. Ubakusen edem usen ami mmaanam naña ekennọọ uyio ebo nnam.<verse eid="EZK 24:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 24:19" />Ndin mbon awo emaembịp miin ebo ete, “Nte afo ubooho udọkkọ ñnyịn naña mme ñkpọ ami ibeghe ñnyịn? Ntak afo anamma ñkpọ ntom-o?”<verse eid="EZK 24:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 24:20" />Ndin ami mmaabo ammọ nte, “Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 24:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 24:21" />Dọkkọ nditọ Isrel bo, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaasappa adisana itie mmi, itie udịbe a-ndufo etañña idem ebaña, ñkpọ anọọhọ anyen ndufo inemesịd, ñkpọ a-ndufo emaaha ataa eti-eti. Nditọ ndufo ideen ye ibaan a-ndufo edakkake ekpọñ eyaekpañña ke akañkañ. <verse eid="EZK 24:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 24:22" />Ndin ndufo eyaenam kpa naña ami nnam. Ndufo idiifʌkkọ ñwainua ye ñwaebek, idiinyʌññọ idia ndidia mbon esitieghe ikpo. <verse eid="EZK 24:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 24:23" />Ndufo eyaekaa iso eyara tọban ndufo ke iwuod enyʌñ esịne ikpaukod ndufo ke ukod. Ndufo idiifʌhọke, idiinyʌññọ itua, ado ndufo eyaeyeet ke ntak ndiọiñkpọ ndufo enyʌñ eseeme ke atu ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 24:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 24:24" />Esikeel adiido idiọọñọ inọ ndufo; ndufo eyaenam ukem-ukem se anye anam. Ñkpọ ami amaatịppe, ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara.’<verse eid="EZK 24:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 24:25" />“Ndin afo, ayịn awo, ke usen se ami ndiibọ ammọ itie udịbe ammọ, inemesịd ye ubọọñ ammọ, ñkpọ anọọhọ anyen ammọ inemesịd, udọñ esịd ammọ, ye nditọ ideen ye ibaan ammọ ñko, <verse eid="EZK 24:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 24:26" />usen ado awo a-abọkkọke ayaadi adunọ fiin mbʌk. <verse eid="EZK 24:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 24:27" />Ke ini ado inua mfo ayaatara; afo ayaatañ ikọ ye anye, ndin uduudoppo uyio aba. Ke ntoro afo ayaado ñkpọ idiọọñọ anọ ammọ, ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="EZK 24:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 24" />
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="EZK 25" />
  <para style="s1">Etañ Prọfesi Ebaña Amọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 25:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 25:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 25:2" />“Ayịn awo, wuuk iso mfo se nditọ Amọn nyʌñ tañ prọfesi baña ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 25:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 25:3" />Bo mbon Amọn ate, ‘Ikop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara. Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Sia amaabo “Aha!” ke abaña adisana itie mmi ke ini ekesappake anye, ye ke abaña isọñ Isrel ke ini ekebiatta anye, ye ke abaña ufọk Yuda ke ini eketañña ammọ enyọñọ, <verse eid="EZK 25:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 25:4" />ke ntoro ami ñyauben fiin nnọ mbon edem Usakkautịn nte inie ammọ. Ammọ eyaebọp itie nnaaekọñ ammọ ye itie nnaa ammọ ke atu ndufo; ammọ eyaedia mfịd ndufo enyʌñ enwọñ mmọọñeba ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 25:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 25:5" />Ami ñyaanam Raba akappa itie ndidia kamel ñnyʌñ nnam Amọn ado itie nnaa mme edọñ. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 25:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 25:6" />Sia se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Sia afo amaakwak ubọk anyʌñ atuak ñkpad mfo, anem esịd ke afịd idiọọkesịd mfo abaña isọñ Isrel, <verse eid="EZK 25:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 25:7" />ke ntoro ami ñyaanyanna ubọk mmi udot fiin ke idem ñnyʌñ uben fiin nnọ mme idịd nte ñkpọ mbịme. Ami ñyausọọk fiin nsio ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ usobo fiin nsio ke atu mme abio. Ami ñyaubiat fiin, ndin afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 25:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi ke Abaña Mọb</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 25:8" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: ‘Sia Mọb ye Sei ekebooho ete, “Se Yuda, ayekappa aba nte afịd mme idịd mfen,” <verse eid="EZK 25:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 25:9" />ke ntoro ami ñyaatat ñkañ Mọb nnịm anwa-anwa, tọọñọ ke mme abio adaña amọ, Bed Yesimod, Baal Mọọn ye Kiriataim, e-edoññoke uku isọñ ado. <verse eid="EZK 25:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 25:10" />Ami ñyaaben Mọb ñkọrọ ye nditọ Amọn nnọ mbon edem Usakkautịn nte inie ammọ, mbaak editoiyo mbon Amọn ke atu mme idịd; <verse eid="EZK 25:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 25:11" />ñko ami ñyaanọ Mọb ufen. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 25:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi ke Abaña Edọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 25:12" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: ‘Sia Edọm akesioho ufọk Yuda usiene anyʌñ anam ataa ekamba ndudue ke adinam ntoro, <verse eid="EZK 25:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 25:13" />ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaanyanna ubọk mmi ndot mbon Edọm ke idem ñnyʌñ ñwot awo ye unam. Ami ñyaasobo anye, ndin tọọñọ ke Teman tutu awuọ Dedan ammọ eyaekpa ke akañkañ. <verse eid="EZK 25:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 25:14" />Ami ñyaasio Edọm usiene ke ubọk ikọd mmi Isrel, ndin ammọ eyaenam Edọm naña asaña akekem ke iyadesịd ye ifiobesịd mmi; ammọ eyaediọọñọ usiene mmi, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 25:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi ke Abaña Filistia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 25:15" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: ‘Sia mbon Filistia ekenamma ñkpọ ami ke usiene, enyʌñ esio usiene ye idiọọkesịd ke esịd ammọ, enyʌñ ekama akaan usua eyem adisobo Yuda, <verse eid="EZK 25:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 25:16" />anam kop se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ mi: Ami ñyaanyanna ubọk mmi ndot mbon Filistia ke idem, ndin ami ñyaasọọk mbon Kered nsio, ñnyʌñ nsobo mbon se isʌhọ ke mben inyañ. <verse eid="EZK 25:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 25:17" />Ami ñyaasio ammọ ekamba usiene ñnyʌñ mmia ammọ ufen ke ifiobesịd mmi. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini ami mmaasio ammọ usiene.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 25:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 25" />
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="EZK 26" />
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi ke Abaña Tai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 26:1" />Ke ayọhọ afiọñ duob mme keed ke ayọhọ isua duob mme iba, ke akpa usen afiọñ, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 26:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 26:2" />“Ayịn awo, sia Tai aketañña abaña Yeruselem abo ate, ‘Aha! Inuaatob mme idịd abʌññọ, ndin mme udọk amọ ebeere ennọ; idaha anye amaadʌk atahade do, ami ñyaaforo,’ <verse eid="EZK 26:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 26:3" />ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaanam ikọ ye afo, Tai, ndin ñyaanyʌñ nnam uwak idịd enam ikọ ye afo, nte inyañ atọ adọọk. <verse eid="EZK 26:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 26:4" />Ammọ eyaewuut mme ndibene Tai enyʌñ enyui mme tọwa amọ eduọọñọ ke isọñ; ami ñyaakwọọk mbio amọ nsio ñnyʌñ nnam anye ado nsaad itiad. <verse eid="EZK 26:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 26:5" />Ko ke akpainyañ anye adiido itie se ebịt iyịre ukọ iyak, sia ami mmetañ mma, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. Anye ayaakappa ado ñkpọ ndubịme anọ mme idịd, <verse eid="EZK 26:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 26:6" />ndin akañkañ ayaasobo mme idʌñ amọ ke abod. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="EZK 26:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 26:7" />“Sia se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaaben Nebukadnesa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26:7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Nebukadnesa, </char><char style="ft" closed="false">asʌk ado </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Nebukadnesa;</char><char style="ft" closed="false">ke ufañ ami ye ke uwak itie ke mme ñwed Esikeel ye Yerimaiya.</char></note> adidem Babilọn, adidem mme ndidem, nto adoro ye mme enañmbakara ye mme sariọd, ye mme mbon ewatta enañmbakara ye ekamba udịmekọñ mbịne Tai. <verse eid="EZK 26:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 26:8" />Anye ayaakama akañkañ asobo mme idʌñ ndufo ke abod; ayaanyʌñ abọp ñkpọ ekọñ adidat ñnwana ye afo, abọp usʌñ se esaña edọọk ekewuọ ndibene mfo anyʌñ adịppe atuekọñ anwana ye afo. <verse eid="EZK 26:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 26:9" />Anye ayaabono ñkpọ uwuut ñkpọ ke itie ndibene mfo anyʌñ akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ awuut mme tọwa mfo. <verse eid="EZK 26:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 26:10" />Enañmbakara amọ ayaawak tutu esio ntọñ ufʌk fiin. Mme ndibene mfo eyaenyeeñe emaekop uyom mme enañ ekọñ, wakọn ye sariọd ke ini anye adʌkkọ inuaatob mfo nte mme awo edọñọ abio e-emaekewuut ndibene amọ. <verse eid="EZK 26:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 26:11" />Ñkpad mme enañmbakara amọ eyaesọnnọ afịd efaak mfo; anye ayaawot mbon mfo ye akañkañ, ndin mme ñkpọsọñ abai mfo eyaeduọññọ ke isọñ. <verse eid="EZK 26:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 26:12" />Ammọ eyaebịme inie mfo enyʌñ edat ñkpọ udua mfo ke ñwo; eyaeboom ndibene mfo enyʌñ ewuut mfọọn ufọk mfo, etoomo mme itiad mfo eduọọk, ñkọrọ eto ye mbio mfo edọñ ke akpainyañ. <verse eid="EZK 26:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 26:13" />Ami ñyaanam uyom ikwọ mfo atre, ndin awo idiikoppo mbiiñe ikwọ a-atooho mme ekpa mfo aba. <verse eid="EZK 26:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 26:14" />Ñyaanam afo ado nsaad itiad, anyʌñ akappa itie se etat iyịre ukọ iyak enwan. Awo iduubọppọ fiin aba tutu amama, sia ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ntañ, uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara ado ami.<verse eid="EZK 26:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 26:15" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara adọkkọ Tai ado ami: Nte mme isuọ idiinyeeñeke ke uyom iduọ mfo, ke ini mbon se idat unan esioho ñkpo ke ini ewotto mme awo ke ufọọd mfo? <verse eid="EZK 26:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 26:16" />Ndin afịd nditọ ideen abọọñ mben inyañ eyaesọiyọ ke mme ebekpo ammọ enyʌñ ekpọnnọ afọñ ammọ enịm, enyʌñ esịññe mme aweedeñwed afọñidem ammọ ke idem. Ammọ eyaedat ndịk esịne ke idem, ammọ eyaesọiyọ etie ke isọñ, enyeñ idem afịd ini, eba ke ñkpaidem ubaña fiin. <verse eid="EZK 26:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 26:17" />Ndin ammọ eyaeseeme eseeme ubaña fiin enyʌñ ubo fiin ete:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 26:17">“ ‘Se naña usobo fiin, ñwuọnda abio,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:17">a-ayọhọke ye mme awadinyañ!</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 26:17">Afo akedo adudu ke mme akpainyañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:17">afo ye mme andidʌñ ke afo;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 26:17">amaanam ndịk mfo amʌm</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:17">afịd awo se ikidʌñ do.<verse eid="EZK 26:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 26:18" />Idahami mme isuọ enyeeñe</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:18">ke usen iduọ mfo;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 26:18">mme isuọ ke akpainyañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:18">ekop ndịk ebaña iduọ mfo.’<verse eid="EZK 26:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 26:19" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke ini ami mmaanam nọ afo ado mbiara abio, nte mme abio a-awo imiidʌññọ aba, ndin ami mmaanam akpa atọ adọọk usịm fiin nọ akwa mmọọñ amọ ufʌk fiin, <verse eid="EZK 26:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 26:20" />idaha ado ami ñyauben fiin nsọiyọ ye mbon e-esọiyọke edʌk ube ebịne mbon esed. Ami ñyaanam afo adʌñ ke ataa idak isọñ, ke itie a-amaakebiara ikpeene, ye mbon e-esọiyọke edʌk ube, ndin afo uduutịmmeke ududat itie mfo ke isọñ mme aduuwem. <verse eid="EZK 26:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 26:21" />Ami ñyaanam utịd mfo adiọọk, ndin afo uduubaaha aba. Eyauyem fiin, ado awo iduukịtte fiin aba tutu amama, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 26:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 26" />
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="EZK 27" />
  <para style="s1">Aseeme ke Abaña Tai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 27:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 27:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 27:2" />“Ayịn awo, seeme aseeme baña Tai. <verse eid="EZK 27:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 27:3" />Bo Tai, adaaha ke esʌk ekamba akpainyañ, a-adooho esʌk mbeghe mme awo ke uwak mben akpainyañ, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:3">“ ‘Afo, abio Tai, abo ate,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:3">“Ami mmenekke ñyaiya.”<verse eid="EZK 27:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 27:4" />Itie mfo akeba ke akpainyañ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:4">mme abọbufọk emaenam afo anekke ayaiya.<verse eid="EZK 27:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 27:5" />Afịd adukpọk yunipa mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:5">e-ekenamma eketo Seni<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho Ekamba abod Hemọn</char></note>;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:5">ammọ emaedat sida ke Lebanọn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:5">se ekama enam eto ubom unọọ fiin.<verse eid="EZK 27:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 27:6" />Ekedat afriyo ke Basan</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:6">enam mme udeñ mfo;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:6">emaedat eto saipres ke mme mben akpainyañ Saiprọs;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:6">ammọ ekekama nnʌk eniin ebana anyọñ ubom mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 27:7" />Uyaiya awedeñwed linen a-atooho Iyib akedo afada mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:7">anyʌñ ado afọñidiọọñọ mfo;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:7">se ekedat ufʌk fiin ekedo bru ye iduod-iduod</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:7">e-eketooho mme mben akpainyañ Elisa.<verse eid="EZK 27:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 27:8" />Ideen Sidọn ye Afaad ekedo mme awadudeñ mfo;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:8">nta mme anam usọ mfo, Tai, mmọdo ekedọñọ nte mme awad nsʌñikañ mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 27:9" />Nta mme adiọọñọ usọ a-Baiblos emaeba do ye afo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:9">nte mme adaaha udiọñ nsʌñikañ adisiit mme ndudu ke nsʌñikañ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:9">Afịd nsʌñikañ ke akpainyañ ye mme andiwad ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:9">emaekeene edi adinyam ñkpọudua mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:9" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 27:10" />“ ‘Ideen Pesia, Lidia ye Pud</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:10">ekesịne ke atu udịmekọñ mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:10">Ammọ emaekọọñ atuekọñ ye itam ukwak ammọ ke ndibene mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:10">a-akunọọhọ fiin uyai.<verse eid="EZK 27:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 27:11" />Ideen Afaad ye Helek</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:11">emaekpeme ndibene mfo ekanna ekʌk;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:11">ideen Kamaad</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:11">ekeba ke mme tọwa mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:11">Ammọ emaekọọñ atuekọñ ammọ ke ndibene mfo;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:11">ammọ emaenam uyai mfo afọn ama.<verse eid="EZK 27:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 27:12" />“ ‘Taasis ekenam ndubeghe ye afo ato ntak uwak inie mfo; ammọ emaedat silfa, ukwak, tian ye leed edikpuho ebọ ñkpọ udua mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 27:13" />“ ‘Kriis, Tubal ye Mesek emaenam ndubeghe ye afo; ammọ emaesidat mme awo ye mme ñkpọ udua brọns edinyam unọ fiin enyʌñ ebọ mme ñkpọ udua mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 27:14" />“ ‘Ideen Bed Tokama ekekama enañmbakara sariọd, enañmbakara kafalri ye ñwaahadọñki ekpəho ye ñkpọ udua mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 27:15" />“ ‘Ideen Rod ye Dedan emaenyam udua ye afo, uwak mme mben akpainyañ ñko ekedo mme adebudua mfo; ammọ ekukpe fiin ke nnʌk eniin ye abubịd eto.<verse eid="EZK 27:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 27:16" />“ ‘Aram<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ataa uwak mme ikpañwed Hibru; usʌk mme ikpañwed Hibru ye Siriak ewet </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Edom</char></note> ekenam ndubeghe ye afo ke ntak uwak ñkpọ udua mfo; ammọ emaedat nsem-nsem itiad, iduod-iduod afọñ, awedeñwed ñkpọ usọ, eti linen, kọral ye mme rubi edep ñkpọ udua mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 27:17" />“ ‘Yuda ye Isrel emaenyam udua ye afo; ammọ emaedat wiid ye usasañ ñkpọ a-atooho Minịd ekpəho, ekama adanakwọọk, adan ọlif ye baam ekpəho ye mme ñkpọ udua mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 27:18" />“ ‘Damaskọs ekenam ndubeghe ye afo ato ntak uwak ñkpọ usọ mfo ye uwak inie mfo. Ammọ ekekama wain a-atooho Helbon, idededọñ a-atooho Saha <verse eid="EZK 27:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 27:19" />ye mme atu ukọd mbon Daan ye mbon Kriis e-ekebenne eto Wedan ke Aisal ekpəho ye mme ñkpọ udua mfo: uyaiya ukwak, akesia ye kalamus.<verse eid="EZK 27:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 27:20" />“ ‘Dedan ekekama blañked esibịtte ke edem enañmbakara enyam udua ye afo.<verse eid="EZK 27:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 27:21" />“ ‘Arebia ye afịd nditọ ideen abọọñ Keda ekedo mbon udua mfo; ammọ ekekama nditọedọñ, mme akukịmedọñ ye mme ebod enam ndubeghe ye afo.<verse eid="EZK 27:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 27:22" />“ ‘Mme anyamudua Seba ye Raama emaenyam udua ye afo; ammọ ekedat ataa nti ye kutọ-kutọ anem ufịk mfiọññọ ye nsọñudua itiad, ye kold enyam udua ye afo.<verse eid="EZK 27:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 27:23" />“ ‘Haran, Kane ye Idịn ye mbon udua Seba, Asiria ye Kilmad emaenyam udua ye afo. <verse eid="EZK 27:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 27:24" />Ke itie udua mfo ammọ ekenyam udua ye afo ke mfọọn afọñidem, bru afọñ, awedeñwed ñkpọ usọ ye udʌk e-ewañña enyʌñ ebọp yak anekke asọñ.<verse eid="EZK 27:24" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 27:25" />“ ‘Mme nsʌñikañ Taasis edo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:25">se ikoono ñkpọ udua mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:25">Ndoppo mbiomo uyọhọ fiin ke esịd</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:25">nte afo awatta ke akpainyañ.<verse eid="EZK 27:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 27:26" />Mme awadudeñ mfo uben fiin</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:26">edʌk akpainyañ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:26">Ado ekamba ayobio edem usakkautịn ayaubʌñ fiin mbai-mbai</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:26">ke ufọọd akpainyañ.<verse eid="EZK 27:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 27:27" />Inie mfo, ñkpọudua ye ñkpọmbịn mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:27">mme anamutom ubom, mme awadinyañ ye mme asiit ndudu ubom mfo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:27">mme anyamudua mfo ye afịd mbon ekọñ mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:27">ye afịd mbon mfen se isịne ke esịd</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:27">eyaedeñ ke esịd akpainyañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:27">ke usen iduọ mfo.<verse eid="EZK 27:27" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 27:28" />Mme mben inyañ eyaenyeeñe</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:28">ke ini mme awadinyañ mfo edịisio ñkpo.<verse eid="EZK 27:28" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 27:29" />Afịd mbon se iwat udeñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:29">eyaewuọñọ ekpọñ nsʌñikañ ammọ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:29">mme anamutom ubom ye afịd mme awadinyañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:29">eyaesọiyọ eda ke mben mmọọñ.<verse eid="EZK 27:29" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 27:30" />Ammọ eyaedịppe uyio</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:30">enyʌñ etua ndod-ndod mmọọñayịd ubaña fiin;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:30">ammọ eyaeben ntan eduọk ke iwuod ammọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:30">enyʌñ ewere ke ntọñ.<verse eid="EZK 27:30" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 27:31" />Ammọ eyaekwaat ided ammọ ke ntak mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:31">enyʌñ esịne afọñikpo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:31">Ammọ eyaetua ubaña fiin ke mbʌññọ esịd</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:31">ye ke ndod-ndod aseeme.<verse eid="EZK 27:31" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 27:32" />Naña ammọ etua enyʌñ eseeme ubaña fiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:32">ammọ eyaeseeme aseeme ubaña fiin:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:32">“Anie ke ekekʌp inua akpa nte Tai,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:32">a-akpainyañ akannake anye akʌk?”<verse eid="EZK 27:32" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 27:33" />Ke ini ñkpọ udua mfo akewuọhọ aka mme akpainyañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:33">afo amaanam uwak idịd ekop uyʌkkọ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:33">ye uwak inie mfo ye ñkpọ udua mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:33">afo amaanam mme ndidem ederimbod eforo.<verse eid="EZK 27:33" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 27:34" />Idahami akpainyañ usep fiin mbai-mbai</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:34">ke utəño mmọọñ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:34">ñkpọ udua mfo ye afịd udịm awo mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:34">edeñ ye afo.<verse eid="EZK 27:34" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 27:35" />Afịd mbon se idʌñ ke mben akpainyañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:35">ekop ñkpaidem ubaña fiin;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:35">mme ndidem ammọ ekop ekamba ndịk,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:35">iso ammọ anyʌñ akpəho anọ ndịk.<verse eid="EZK 27:35" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 27:36" />Mme anyamudua ke atu mme idịd usaha fiin;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:36">utịd mfo adiọọk eti-eti,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:36">uduunyʌññọ uba aba ke nsi-nsi.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 27:36" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 27" />
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="EZK 28" />
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi A-abañake Adidem Tai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 28:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 28:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 28:2" />“Ayịn awo, dọkkọ adaukara Tai ate, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:2">“ ‘Ke ntañidem esịd mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">afo abo ate, “Ami ndo abasi;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:2">ami ntie ke ebekpo abasi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">ke ufọọd akpainyañ.”</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:2">Ado afo ado ñkaña awo, abʌk ye iyiib, udooho abasi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">akpesʌkado a-afo akereke ke imọ iminie aniọñ nte abasi.<verse eid="EZK 28:2" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 28:3" />Nte afo amediọọñọ ñkpọ akan Dandiel? <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Danel, </char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọ etob awo ke mbʌk esed</char></note></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:3">Ibaaha ndịbeñkpọ ndomokeed u-udịppe fiin?<verse eid="EZK 28:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 28:4" />Ato ke aniọñ ye mbufiọk mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:4">afo amekọ inie anọ idem mfo</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:4">amenyʌñ akọ kold ye silfa</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:4">adọñ ke itie unịm inie mfo.<verse eid="EZK 28:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 28:5" />Ato ke ataa eti ifiọk a-afo anieghe ke unyam udua</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:5">afo amenam inie mfo atọt,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:5">ñko ke ntak inie mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:5">esịd mfo ayọhọ ye ntañidem.<verse eid="EZK 28:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 28:6" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:6">“ ‘Sia afo akereke ke imọ iminie aniọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:6">inie aniọñ ukem nte abasi,<verse eid="EZK 28:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 28:7" />ami ñyaaben mme isenawo edinwana ndufo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:7">mme afai idịd i-imiikoppo mbọm;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:7">ammọ eyaesio akañkañ ammọ ekpii uyai ye aniọñ mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:7">enyʌñ ekịm uyamma uyai mfo ebiat.<verse eid="EZK 28:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 28:8" />Ammọ eyauben fiin eduọọk ke ube,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:8">ndin afo ayaakpa ñkpa afai</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:8">ke ufọọd inyañ.<verse eid="EZK 28:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 28:9" />Nte afo ayaabo, “Ami ndo abasi,”</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:9">ke iso mbon se uwot fiin?</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:9">Afo adiido ñkaña awo, udooho abasi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:9">ke ubọk mbon se uwot fiin.<verse eid="EZK 28:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 28:10" />Afo ayaakpa ñkpa mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:10">ke ubọk isenawo.</para>
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 28:10">Ami mmetañ mma, ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 28:10" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 28:11" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 28:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 28:12" />“Ayịn awo, seeme aseeme baña adidem Tai nyʌñ bo anye ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:12">“ ‘Afo akedo idiọọñọ mfọnmma,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:12">ayọhọ ye aniọñ anyʌñ ayaiya ama.<verse eid="EZK 28:12" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 28:13" />Afo akeba ke Idịn,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">inwañ Abasi;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:13">afịd nsọñudua itiad emaubana fiin idem:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">kanelian, krisolaid ye emeraal,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">topas, ọniks ye yaspa,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">lapis lasuli, nsem-nsem itiad ye beril.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:13">Ubonoñkpọ ye udodñkpọ mfo ekenam ke kold;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">ke usen e-ekubotto fiin ke ekeneeñe ammọ ebono.<verse eid="EZK 28:13" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 28:14" />Ekuyet fiin adan enịm nte serub ukpeme,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:14">ntoro ke ami ñkumek fiin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:14">Afo akeba ke adisana abod Abasi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:14">amaasaña ke ufọọd mme itiad e-esakka ke ikañ.<verse eid="EZK 28:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 28:15" />Afo amaanana ndo ke mme usʌñ mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:15">tọọñọ ke usen e-ekubotto fiin</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:15">tutu edikịt ibak uwem ke idem mfo.<verse eid="EZK 28:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 28:16" />Ato ke naña mbịn udua mfo atara,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">afai amauyọhọ fiin idem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">ndin afo amaanam idiọọkñkpọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:16">Ke ntoro ami mmaubịn fiin nsio ke abod Abasi ke asuenne,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">ami mmaanyʌñ udiañña fiin nsio, serub ukpeme,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">ke ufọọd mme itiad esakka ke ikañ.<verse eid="EZK 28:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 28:17" />Esịd mfo akediyọhọ ye ntañidem</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:17">akeene ntak uyai mfo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:17">afo amaanyʌñ abiat aniọñ mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:17">ke ntak ubọọñ mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:17">Anam ami mmautop fiin nduọọk ke isọñ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:17">ami mmaunam fiin ado ñkpọ ndise ke iso mme ndidem.<verse eid="EZK 28:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 28:18" />Ato ke uwak idiọọkñkpọ mfo ye nsu-nsu udua mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:18">afo amesappa mme ndisana itie mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:18">Anam ami mmaanam ikañ uwuọ fiin ke idem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:18">anyʌñ uta fiin,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:18">ndin ami mmaanam afo akappa ntọñ ke isọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:18">ke iso afịd awo se ikida ise.<verse eid="EZK 28:18" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 28:19" />Afịd idịd se ikudiọọñọ fiin</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:19">ekop ñkpaidem ubaña fiin;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:19">utịd mfo adiọọk eti-eti</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:19">ndin uduunyʌññọ uba aba ke nsi-nsi.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 28:19" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi ke Abaña Sidọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 28:20" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 28:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 28:21" />“Ayịn awo, wuuk iso mfo se Sidọn; tañ prọfesi baña anye <verse eid="EZK 28:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 28:22" />nyʌñ bo ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:22">“ ‘Sidọn, ami ñyaanam ikọ ye afo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:22">ami ñyaanyʌñ ñwọt ubọọñ mmi ke atu ndufo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:22">Ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:22">ke ini ami mmaimia ndufo ufen</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:22">ndin ndufo eyaekịt ke ami ndo adisana.<verse eid="EZK 28:22" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 28:23" />Ami ñyaanọ idiọọk udọñọ nsobo isọk ndufo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:23">ñnyʌñ nnam iyiib afiọrọ ke mme efaak ndufo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:23">Mbon se ikpañña afai eyauduọññọ fiin ke idem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:23">ndin akañkañ ayaato afịd ñkanñkʌk adudoro fiin ke idem.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:23">Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="EZK 28:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 28:24" />“ ‘Mbon Isrel idiinieghe ndiọi mbọhọidʌñ e-edooho akpab a-abiakka awo ye ñkukịm a-asọppọ aba. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara.<verse eid="EZK 28:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 28:25" />“ ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke ini ami mmaakekoono mbon Isrel nto mme idịd a-ammọ ekesuanake edọñọ, eyaenam nọ ami ndo adisana ke anyen mme idịd ke ntak ammọ. Ndin ammọ eyaedʌñ ke isọñ ammọ, a-ami ñkenọọhọ awo mmi Yekọb. <verse eid="EZK 28:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 28:26" />Ammọ eyaedʌñ do ke ifuuro enyʌñ ebọọp ufọk, enyʌñ etọ inwañ fain; ammọ eyaedʌñ ke ifuuro ke ini ami mmaamia afịd mbọhọidʌñ ammọ e-esịnne ammọ ke ndek ufen. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 28:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 28" />
  <chapter number="29" style="c" sid="EZK 29" />
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi A-abañake Iyib</para>
  <para style="s2">Ubiereikpe Nnọọ Fero</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 29:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua duob, ke ayọhọ afiọñ duob ke ayọhọ usen duob mme iba, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 29:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 29:2" />“Ayịn awo, wuuk iso mfo se Fero adidem Iyib nyʌñ tañ prọfesi baña anye ye afịd Iyib. <verse eid="EZK 29:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 29:3" />Tañ ikọ ye anye nyʌñ bo anye ate: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:3">“ ‘Fero adidem Iyib, ami mmetọhọ ye afo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:3">afo ekamba aniendịk amọn a-anaaha ke ufọọd mme idịm mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:3">Afo ate, “Akpa Nail annie miin;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:3">ami ñkenam anye nnọ idem mmi.”<verse eid="EZK 29:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 29:4" />Ado ami ñyaasịn mme ekọb uwaam ke mbañ mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:4">ñnyʌñ nnam iyak idịm mfo uyịre fiin ke mme ikpọk mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:4">Ami ñyaudʌt fiin nsio ke ufọọd mme idịm mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:4">afịd iyak ke idịm mfo eyauyịre fiin ke ñkpọk.<verse eid="EZK 29:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 29:5" />Ami ñyaukpọñ fiin nnịm ke anaan,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5">afo ye afịd iyak ke mme idịm mfo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:5">Afo ayaaduọ ke iso isọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5">awo idiinyʌññọ utañ ibok aba.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:5">Ami ñyauben fiin nte ndidia</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5">nnọ mme unam ikọd ye mme inuen anyọñ.<verse eid="EZK 29:5" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 29:6" />Ndin afịd mbon se idʌñ ke Iyib eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 29:6" />
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 29:6">“ ‘Afo amedo esañ ñnyanyaha anọ mbon Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 29:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 29:7" />Ke ini ammọ ekumʌmmọ fiin ke ubọk ammọ, afo amaasaiya anyʌñ asiak ammọ afara; ke ini ammọ ekebette idem ke afo, afo amaabʌññọ ndin edem ammọ amaanyʌñ abʌññọ.<verse eid="EZK 29:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 29:8" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaaben akañkañ ukeene fiin ñnyʌñ ñwot awo ye unam. <verse eid="EZK 29:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 29:9" />Isọñ Iyib ayaakappa ado ñwuudo ndoon. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 29:9">“ ‘Sia afo amaabo ate, “Akpa Nail ado ake mmi; ami ñkenam anye,” <verse eid="EZK 29:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 29:10" />ke ntoro ami mmetọhọ ye afo ye mme idịm mfo, ndin ami ñyaanam isọñ Iyib ado nsobo itie ye ñwuudo ndoon tọọñọ ke Mikdol akewuọ Aswan, tutu akesịm adaña Kuus. <verse eid="EZK 29:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 29:11" />Ñkpad awo me unam idiisañake iboiyo ke esịd; awo ndomokeed idiidʌññọ do ke isua aba. <verse eid="EZK 29:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 29:12" />Ami ñyaanam isọñ Iyib anaa ukpọk ke atu mme idịd se esobo, ndin mme abio amọ eyaenaa nte ñwuudo itie ke atu mme ñwuudo abio ke isua aba. Ami ñyaanyʌñ mbịne mbon Iyib ndọñ ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ nsuan ammọ ndọñ ke atu mme abio.<verse eid="EZK 29:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 29:13" />“ ‘Kpayeado, se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke utịd isua aba, ami ñyaakoono mbon Iyib nto mme idịd se ekesuan ammọ edọñ mmaana mbok. <verse eid="EZK 29:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 29:14" />Ami ñyaakoono mbon eketañña esio ke idʌñ ke isọñ Iyib mmaana ñnyọñ Adoro Iyib, isọñ emana ammọ. Do ke ammọ ediido usuuhọ idịd. <verse eid="EZK 29:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 29:15" />Anye adiido andisịb ñkan ke atu mme idịd mfen, idiinyʌññọ ibenne idem amọ aba ikan mme idịd mfen tutu amama. Ami ñyaanam idem amem anye tutu anye ikanna ikara mme idịd mfen aba. <verse eid="EZK 29:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 29:16" />Iyib idiidooho ibededem inọ mbon Isrel aba, ado eyaetoiyo idiọọkñkpọ ammọ ke ini ekannake eyem unwam eto Iyib. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 29:16" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Utịb Nebukadnesa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 29:17" />Ke ayọhọ isua edịb mme itiaba, ke akpa afiọñ ke akpa usen, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 29:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 29:18" />“Ayịn awo, Nebukadnesa adidem Babilọn amaanam mbon ekọñ amọ eka ekọñ ye Tai; emaefʌnnọ ammọ ke edikwaat afịd iwuod enyʌñ efoñ afịd afara. Kpayeado anye ye mbon ekọñ amọ ikinieghe ñkpọ ayịnutom ito ekọñ a-ammọ ekenwanake ye Tai sia ammọ ikikanna Tai. <verse eid="EZK 29:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 29:19" />Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaayaak Iyib nnọ Nebukadnesa adidem Babilọn, ndin anye ayaaben inie amọ anyọñ. Anye ayaabịme ñkpọ amọ anyʌñ awo isọñ ado adidat ñkpe udịmekọñ amọ. <verse eid="EZK 29:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 29:20" />Ami mmenọ anye Iyib nte utịb amọ ke afịd ifịk se anye akesịn sia anye ye udịmekọñ amọ ekenam ado ennọ miin, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 29:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 29:21" />“Ke usen ado ami ñyaanam nnʌk atịppe anọ mbon Isrel, ami ñyaanyʌñ ukʌppọ fiin inua ke atu ammọ. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="EZK 29:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 29" />
  <chapter number="30" style="c" sid="EZK 30" />
  <para style="s2">Aseeme ke Abaña Iyib</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 30:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 30:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 30:2" />“Ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:2">“ ‘Tua seeme nyʌñ bo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:2">“Mbọm ke usen ado!”<verse eid="EZK 30:2" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 30:3" />Sia usen ado akpere,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:3">usen <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akpere,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:3">usen idiọọk anyọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:3">adiido ini idiọọk ñkpọntịppe inọ mme idịd.<verse eid="EZK 30:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 30:4" />Akañkañ ayaadi abịne Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:4">ekamba ubiak ayaanyʌñ adi abịne Kuus.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:4">Ke ini mme akpañña afai emaeduọññọ ke Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:4">eyaekoono inie amọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:4">enyʌñ ewuut itiad idakisọñ amọ.<verse eid="EZK 30:4" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 30:5" />Kuus ye Libia, Lidia ye afịd Arebia, Kub ye mbon isọñ enwọñọ eyaeduọññọ ke akañkañ ye Iyib.<verse eid="EZK 30:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 30:6" />“ ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:6">“ ‘Mme ufan Iyib eyaeduọññọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:6">ndin iseri adudu amọ ayaakpu.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:6">Tọọñọ ke Mikdol tutu akewuọ Aswan</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:6">ammọ eyaeduọ ke akañkañ ke esịd amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:6">ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 30:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 30:7" />Ammọ eyaenaa ukpọk</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:7">ke atu mme abio se inaa ukpọk,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:7">ndin mme abio ammọ eyaeba</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:7">ke atu mme ñwuudo abio.<verse eid="EZK 30:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 30:8" />Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:8">ke ini ami mmaakịm ikañ nsịn ke Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:8">enyʌñ enuak afịd mbon se isinwam anye.<verse eid="EZK 30:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 30:9" />“ ‘Ke usen ado mme isʌñutom eyaento miin esaña ke mme ubom ekedịkke Kuus ke ndueidem. Ammọ eyaekop ekamba ubiak ke usen idiọọk ñkpọntịppe ke Iyib, sia ke akpanikọ ayaatịppe.<verse eid="EZK 30:9" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 30:10" />“ ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:10">“ ‘Ami ñyaanam ekamba atu awo ke Iyib ekweeñe</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:10">ato ke ubọk Nebukadnesa adidem Babilọn.<verse eid="EZK 30:10" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 30:11" />Anye ye udịmekọñ amọ, mbon se isọñ esịd ikan ke atu mme idịd,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:11">eyaedʌk edisobo idịd ado.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:11">Ammọ eyaesịññe mme akañkañ ammọ enwana ye Iyib</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:11">enyʌñ enam akpo awo ayọhọ isọñ.<verse eid="EZK 30:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 30:12" />Ami ñyaanam mmọọñ ke akpa Nail asat</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:12">ñnyʌñ mben isọñ ado ñnyam nnọ idiọọk idịd;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:12">ato ke ubọk isenawo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:12">ami ñyaasobo idịd ado ye afịd se idọñọ ke esịd.</para>
  <para style="m" vid="EZK 30:12">Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmetañ.<verse eid="EZK 30:12" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 30:13" />“ ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:13">“ ‘Ami ñyaasobo mme ubobodñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:13">ñnyʌñ nnam mme ubobodñkpọ ke Memfis atre.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:13">Akpanabọọñ ndomokeed idiibaaha aba ke Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:13">ami ñyaanyʌñ nsuan ndịk ke afịd isọñ abio.<verse eid="EZK 30:13" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 30:14" />Ami ñyaasobo Adoro Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:14">ñnyʌñ ñkịm ikañ nsịn ke Soan,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:14">ñnyʌñ nnọ Tebes ufen.<verse eid="EZK 30:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 30:15" />Ami ñyaanwañña ifiobesịd mmi mfʌk Pelusium,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:15">akpọsọñ itie Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:15">ñnyʌñ nsọọk ekamba atu awo ke Tebes nsio.<verse eid="EZK 30:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 30:16" />Ami ñyaakịm ikañ nsịn ke Iyib;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:16">Pelusium ayaakop ataa ubiak.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:16">Eyaedat Tebes ke afai-afai usʌñ:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:16">Memfis adiiba ke ukuud afịd ini.<verse eid="EZK 30:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 30:17" />Eyaewot ñkparawa Heliopolis ye Bubastis</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:17">ke akañkañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:17">ndin eyaetañ mme abio ammọ esio nte ifʌn,<verse eid="EZK 30:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 30:18" />Abio Tapanes ayaakịm ke usen ado</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:18">ke ini ami mmaabuuñ akpọnọ Iyib;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:18">do ndin ke iseri adudu amọ adiitre.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:18">Ntọñanyọñ ayaafʌk anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:18">eyaenyʌñ ekoono mbon idʌñ amọ esịññe.<verse eid="EZK 30:18" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 30:19" />Ke ntoro ami ñyaanọ Iyib ufen,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:19">ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 30:19" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Ebʌñ Fero Ubọk</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 30:20" />Ke ayọhọ isua duob mme keed, ke akpa afiọñ ke ayọhọ usen itiaba, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 30:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 30:21" />“Ayịn awo, ami mmebuuñ Fero adidem Iyib ubọk. Awo ibọppọ anye nọ ato do unan ado akpa, awo inyʌññọ isịn anye ke afọñ nọ ato do akop adudu se amʌm akañkañ. <verse eid="EZK 30:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 30:22" />Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami mmenam ikọ ye Fero adidem Iyib. Ami ñyaabuuñ anye naña ubọk iba, ñyaabuuñ ubọk se ifọn ndian ye anye amaakebọbʌññọ, ñnyʌñ nnam akañkañ abọkkọ anye ke ubọk aduọ. <verse eid="EZK 30:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 30:23" />Ami ñyaabịn nditọ Iyib ndọñ ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ nsuan ammọ ndọñ ke mme abio. <verse eid="EZK 30:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 30:24" />Ami ñyaasọọñọ adidem Babilọn ubọk ñnyʌñ nsịn anye akañkañ mmi ke ubọk amọ, ado ñyaabuuñ Fero ubọk, ndin anye ayaamịm mmịm ke iso amọ nte awo a-akpaaha afai. <verse eid="EZK 30:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 30:25" />Ami ñyaasọọñọ adidem Babilọn ubọk, ado ubọk Fero ayaamem. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini ami mmaaben akañkañ mmi nsịn adidem Babilọn ke ubọk nọ anye aben anyan ke isọ Iyib. <verse eid="EZK 30:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 30:26" />Ami ñyaabịn nditọ Iyib ndọñ ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ nsuan ammọ ndọñ ke mme abio. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="EZK 30:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 30" />
  <chapter number="31" style="c" sid="EZK 31" />
  <para style="s2">Fero nte Sida Lebanọn A-aduọhọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 31:1" />Ke akpa usen afiọñ, ke ayọhọ afiọñ ita ke ayọhọ isua duob mme keed, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 31:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 31:2" />“Ayịn awo, bo Fero adidem Iyib ye afịd atu awo amọ ate:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:2">“ ‘Anie ke ekeme adiben ndomo ye afo ke uteeñe?<verse eid="EZK 31:2" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 31:3" />Tịm se Asiria, akesidooho sida ke Lebanọn,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:3">anieñe mfọọn ñkọk a-awuọhọ afuuk mme akai;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:3">ndaha amọ akoñ ke anyọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:3">anyọñ amọ adịppe akan mme mfuud eto.<verse eid="EZK 31:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 31:4" />Mme mmọọñ enam anye aseghe,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:4">ntotəño mmọọñ ke abaitiad enam anye akọt anyọọñ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:4">mme idịm ammọ efeeñe</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:4">afịd ke mben amọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:4">enyʌñ esio ñkọk amọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:4">esịn enọ afịd mme eto ke inwañ.<verse eid="EZK 31:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 31:5" />Ke ntoro anye akaiso akoñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:5">akan afịd eto se iba ke inwañ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:5">akpan ñkọk amọ akọt,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:5">mme ñkọk amọ enyʌñ enyọọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:5">etaara ke ntak uwak mmọọñ a-anye anieghe.<verse eid="EZK 31:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 31:6" />Afịd inuen ke ikpaanyọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:6">ekebọp efọk ke akpan ñkọk amọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:6">afịd mme unam ke akai</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:6">eman nditọ ke idak ñkọk amọ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:6">afịd mme ikpọ idịd</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:6">edʌñ ke idak mfuud amọ.<verse eid="EZK 31:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 31:7" />Anye amaayaiya ke ubọọñ amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:7">ye ke ntatara akpan ñkọk amọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:7">sia adooho adʌñ amọ amaatịkke adʌk isọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:7">akesịm uwak mmọọñ.<verse eid="EZK 31:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 31:8" />Mme sida ke inwañesa Abasi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:8">ikidomoke idem ye anye,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:8">ñko mme yunipa ikikanna</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:8">idukemme ye akpan ñkọk amọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:8">me ñkaña eto edikan</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:8">ndomo idem ye mme ñkọk amọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:8">ibaaha eto ndomokeed ke inwañesa Abasi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:8">se ekeben edomo ye uyai amọ.<verse eid="EZK 31:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 31:9" />Ami ñkenam anye ayaiya</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:9">anieñe uwak ñkọk, ndin</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:9">afịd eto ke Idịn efịbe anye ufịb</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:9">ke inwañesa Abasi.<verse eid="EZK 31:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 31:10" />“ ‘Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Sia adooho ekamba sida akọt afʌk mme ñkọñ eto mfen, ñko sia adooho anye amaadaara abaña unyọọñ amọ, <verse eid="EZK 31:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 31:11" />ami mmaayaak anye nsịn ke ubọk mme andikara ke mme idịd, nọ anye anam ye anye akeene naña ibak amọ ado. Ami mmenịm anye ñkañ keed, <verse eid="EZK 31:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 31:12" />ñko mme isen idịd enanake mbọm ekan e-ekpịkke anye eyaak enịm edakka ekpọñ. Akpan ñkọk amọ aduọ ke ikpọabod ye ke mme itịkke isọñ; mme ñkọk amọ ebʌñọ ebono ke mme abedeñ isọñ. Afịd mme idịd ke isọñ ewuọ ekpọñ idak mfuud amọ. <verse eid="EZK 31:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 31:13" />Afịd mme inuen emaedʌñọ ke eto ado a-amaakeduọ, afịd mme ndiọi unam enyʌñ edʌñọ ke mme ñkọk amọ. <verse eid="EZK 31:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 31:14" />Ke ntoro, idiibaaha eto ndomokeed mfen ke mben mmọọñ se idiiwuọ unyọọñ inyʌñ inie ntañidem, idịppe atịñe ammọ ifuuk ñnyan eto mfen. Ibaaha eto ndomokeed mfen se ikinekke inie mmọọñ a-akekanna anyọọñ ntoro; iniiso afịd ammọ akena anọ ñkpa, ke idak isọñ, ke atu mbon awo e-ekesọiyọke eka abioekpo.<verse eid="EZK 31:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 31:15" />“ ‘Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ke usen ekesuuhọke anye esịn ke abioekpo ami ñkefʌk mme mmọọñ ye ntua ayịd nnọ anye; ami ñkemʌm idịm amọ ñkama, ndin uwak mmọọñ amọ emaetre utom. Ke ntak amọ ami mmaaben afọñ aseeme nsịn Lebanọn, ndin afịd eto ke inwañ emaeyeeme. <verse eid="EZK 31:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 31:16" />Ami mmaanam mme idịd enyeñ ke uyio iduọ amọ ke ini ami ñkenyuuho anye nsịn ke abioekpo yak akeba ye mbon e-emaekesọiyọ idʌk ube. Ndin afịd mme eto ke Idịn, nti ye mfọọn ñkan eto ke Lebanọn, mme eto se enekke eduọk mmọọñ, emaebọ idọñesịd ke idak ederimbod. <verse eid="EZK 31:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 31:17" />Ammọ ñko, nte akpọsọñ sida, emaesọiyọ ekaa abioekpo, ebịne mbon se ekewot ke akañkañ, ye mbon ekọñ e-ekedʌññọ ke idak mfuud amọ ke atu mme idịd.<verse eid="EZK 31:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 31:18" />“ ‘Akee ke atu mme eto ke Idịn ke ekeme adiben ndomo ye afo ke uyai ye ke ubọọñ? Ado eyaenyʌñ usuuk fiin ñko enịm ye mme eto Idịn ke idak isọñ ami; afo ayaanaa ye mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd, ye mbon e-ekewotto ke akañkañ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 31:18">“ ‘Anyem ado Fero ye afịd atu awo amọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 31:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 31" />
  <chapter number="32" style="c" sid="EZK 32" />
  <para style="s2">Eseeme A-abañake Fero</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 32:1" />Ke akpa usen, ke ayọhọ afiọñ duob mme iba, ke ayọhọ isua duob mme iba, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 32:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 32:2" />“Ayịn awo, benne ikwọ aseeme baña Fero adidem Iyib nyʌñ bo anye:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:2">“ ‘Afo aba nte ekpe ke atu mme idịd;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:2">afo aba nte akukubarakpa ke mme akpainyañ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:2">abebịmme ke mme idịm mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:2">afo atịmede mmọọñ ke ukod mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:2">anyʌñ anam mmọọñ amọ abat.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 32:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 32:3" />“ ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:3">“ ‘Ke atu uwak mme awo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:3">ami ndiitat iyịre mmi ufʌk fiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:3">ndin ammọ eyaedat iyịre mmi ukoot fiin esio.<verse eid="EZK 32:3" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 32:4" />Ami ñyautop fiin nnịm ke isọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:4">ñnyʌñ udʌt fiin ke akpa inwañ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:4">Ami ñyaanam nọ afịd inuen ke ikpaanyọñ usọrọ fiin ke idem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:4">ñnyʌñ nnam afịd ndiọi unam ekop uyʌkkọ ke aduta fiin.<verse eid="EZK 32:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 32:5" />Ami ñyaadette abʌk mfo nnịm ke mme ikpọabod</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:5">ñnyʌñ ndat ñyọhọñsʌhọ mfo ñyọhọ ke mme abedeñ.<verse eid="EZK 32:5" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 32:6" />Ami ñyaanam iyiib mfo afiọrọ ke isọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:6">afịd usʌñ tutu akewuọ mme ikpọabod,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:6">ñko mme abedeñ adiiyọhọ ye ikpọkidem mfo.<verse eid="EZK 32:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 32:7" />Ke ini ami unịmeke fiin, ami ñyaafʌk anyọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:7">ñnyʌñ nnam mme ntantaafiọñ ammọ ekịm;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:7">Ami ñyaadat ntọñanyọñ mfʌk ayio,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:7">afiọñ ñko idiinọọhọ unwana amọ.<verse eid="EZK 32:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 32:8" />Ami ñyaanam afịd ikañ a-ayamake ke anyọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:8">akịm ubaha fiin; ami ñyaaben ekịm mfʌk isọñ mfo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:8">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 32:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 32:9" />Ami ñyaatịmede esịd uwak awo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:9">ke ini ami mbenne iduọ mfo ndi ke ufọọd mme idịd,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:9">ke ufọọd mme idʌñ ake afo uduudiọọñọke.<verse eid="EZK 32:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 32:10" />Ami ñyaanam nọ mme atu awo enie ñkpaidem ubaña fiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">ñko ndidem ammọ eyaeyeeme nsia ke ntak mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">ke ini a-ami ndiifʌñ akañkañ mmi ke iso ammọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:10">Ke usen iduọ mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">ammọ keedekeed eyaenyeñ idem</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">afịd ini ebaña uwem ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 32:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 32:11" />“ ‘Sia adooho se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:11">“ ‘Akañkañ adidem Babilọn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:11">ayaadi ubịne fiin.<verse eid="EZK 32:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 32:12" />Ami ñyaanam udịm awo mfo eduọññọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:12">ke mme akañkañ mbon uko,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:12">kpa mme idịd e-efaiyake afai ekan.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:12">Ammọ eyaebiat asian mbon Iyib,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:12">eyaenyʌñ ewọññọ afịd udịm awo amọ etọọñ.<verse eid="EZK 32:12" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 32:13" />Ami ñyaasobo afịd mme enañ amọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:13">ke mben ekamba mmọọñ</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:13">ndin ukod awo idiitịmekede ammọ aba</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:13">me ñkpad udịm enañ aditịmede mmọọñ ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 32:13" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 32:14" />Ndin ami ñyaayaak mme mmọọñ amọ ateñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:14">ñnyʌñ nnam idịm amọ afeghe nte adan,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:14">ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 32:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 32:15" />Ke ini ami nnamma isọñ Iyib akappa ndoon</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:15">ñnyʌñ nsịññe afịd se ikiba ke isọñ ado,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:15">ke ini ami ñwotto afịd mbon se idʌñ do nsio,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:15">do ke ammọ ediidiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’<verse eid="EZK 32:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 32:16" />“Aseeme se ammọ ediiseeme inọ anye ado ami. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ abo ke nditọ ibaan ke idịd eyaekwọ; eyaekwọ enọ Iyib ye afịd udịmekọñ amọ.”<verse eid="EZK 32:16" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Aditịkke Iyib Ndʌk Itịkke Ñkpa.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 32:17" />Ke ayọhọ isua duob mme iba, ke ayọhọ usen duob mme ition ke afiọñ, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin: <verse eid="EZK 32:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 32:18" />“Ayịn awo, tua baña ekamba atu awo Iyib nyʌñ yaak anye ye nditọ ibaan ñkpọsọñ idịd sịn ke idak isọñ, dian ye mbon e-esọiyọke eka abioekpo. <verse eid="EZK 32:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 32:19" />Bo ammọ, ‘Nte ndufo emenie mfọniso ekan mbon mfen? Isọiyọ ikinaa ye mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd.’ <verse eid="EZK 32:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 32:20" />Amọ eyaeduọ ke atu mbon e-ewotto ke akañkañ. E-esio akañkañ ke efọk; yak edʌt anye ye mbon amọ esio. <verse eid="EZK 32:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 32:21" />Ikpọ mme adadusʌñ eyaeto abioekpo editañ ebaña Iyib ye mbon amọ ete, ‘Ammọ esọiyọ ediba ye mbon se imiifọọrọke edʌd, ye mbon se ekewot ke akañkañ.’<verse eid="EZK 32:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 32:22" />“Asiria mmọdo aba ye udịmekọñ amọ; udi afịd mbon amọ se ekewot ekanna anye ekʌk, afịd mbon se ikiduọ ke akañkañ. <verse eid="EZK 32:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 32:23" />Udi ammọ eba ke ataa esịd ube ndin udịmekọñ amọ enaa ekanna udi amọ. E-ewot afịd mbon se ikisịn ndịk ke isọñ mme aduuwem, e-ewot ammọ ke akañkañ.”<verse eid="EZK 32:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 32:24" />“Elam mmọdo, ye afịd udịm mbon amọ e-ekannake udi amọ ekʌk. E-ewoot afịd ammọ ke akañkañ. Afịd mbon se ikisuan ndịk ke isọñ mme aduuwem emaesọiyọ edʌk abioekpo, ifọọrọke edʌd. Ammọ ekama abuud ammọ ye mbon e-ekesọiyọke edʌk abioekpo. <verse eid="EZK 32:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 32:25" />E-enam ikʌk enịm enọ anye ke atu mbon se ewot, ye afịd udịm awo amọ e-ekannake udi amọ. Afịd ammọ edo mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd, e-ewotto ke akañkañ. Sia adooho ndịk ammọ amaasuana ke isọñ mme aduuwem, ammọ esaña ye abuud ammọ ye mbon e-esọiyọke eka abioekpo; e-enịm ammọ ke atu mbon se ekewot.”<verse eid="EZK 32:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 32:26" />“Mesek ye Tubal mmọeba do, ye afịd mbon ammọ e-ekannake udi ammọ ekʌk. Afịd ammọ edoñño mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd, e-ewotto ke akañkañ sia adooho ammọ esuan ndịk ke isọñ mme aduuwem. <verse eid="EZK 32:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 32:27" />Ado ammọ inaaha ye nta mbon ekọñ esed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32:27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Septuakin; Ke Hibru </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nta mbon ekọñ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">a-awo imiikifọọrọke edəd</char></note> e-ekekpaññake ke ekọñ, mbon e-ekesọiyọke edʌk itịkke ñkpa ye mme ñkpọ ekọñ ammọ, e-ekenịmme akañkañ ammọ ke idak iwuod ammọ, atuekọñ ammọ anyʌñ abere ke akpọ ammọ, akpesʌkado mbon ekọñ ami ñko emaedịkke mme awo ke isọñ mme aduuwem.”<verse eid="EZK 32:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 32:28" />“Fero, afo ñko ayaanuaha anyʌñ ana ye mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd, ye mbon se ekewot ke akañkañ.”<verse eid="EZK 32:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 32:29" />“Edọm mmọdo, ndidem ye mme akpanabọọñ amọ; akpesʌkado a-ammọ enieghe adudu, e-enyanna ammọ enịm ye mbon ewotto ke akañkañ. Ammọ enaa ye mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd, ye mbon e-esọiyọke edʌk ube.”<verse eid="EZK 32:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 32:30" />“Afịd mme akpanabọọñ e-etooho adoro ye afịd mbon Sidọn mmọdo; ammọ esọiyọ ekaa abioekpo ye mbon e-ekewotto ke ndọk akpesʌkado ammọ ekesịnne awo ndịk ke idem ke ntak adudu ammọ ekenieghe. Ammọ enaa nte mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd ye mbon se ewot ke akañkañ enyʌñ edia ndọk ammọ ye mbon e-esọiyọke eka abioekpo.”<verse eid="EZK 32:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 32:31" />“Fero, anye ye afịd udịmekọñ amọ, ayaakịt ammọ, ndin anye ayaabọ idọñesịd ke afịd udịm awo a-ammọ ekewotto ke akañkañ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 32:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 32:32" />Akpesʌkado a-adooho ami ñkenam anye asuan ndịk ke isọñ mme aduuwem, Fero ye udịm awo amọ ediina ye mbon i-imiifọọrọke edʌd, ye mbon se ekewot ke akañkañ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 32:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 32" />
  <chapter number="33" style="c" sid="EZK 33" />
  <para style="s1">Udemme Ikood Esikeel nte Awoukpeme</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 33:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 33:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 33:2" />“Ayịn awo, dọkkọ mbon mfo ate: ‘Ke ini ami mbenne akañkañ mbịne idʌñ, ndin mme andinie idʌñ ado esio awodeen ammọ keed enam anye ado awoukpeme anọ ammọ, <verse eid="EZK 33:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 33:3" />ndin anye akịt naña akañkañ adʌkkọ idʌñ anyʌñ afịt adukpoñ adʌt mme awo utọñ, <verse eid="EZK 33:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 33:4" />ado adieke awo ndomokeed akoppo adukpoñ ado inamma item ndin akañkañ adiben uwem ammọ, iyiib ammọ adiidoro ammọ ke iwuod. <verse eid="EZK 33:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 33:5" />Sia adooho ammọ emaekop uyio adukpoñ, ado ikpañña utọñ inọ ndʌdutọñ, iyiib ammọ adiidoro ammọ ke iwuod. Akpedo ammọ emaekop ndʌdutọñ, ammọ ekpaekenyaaña idem ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 33:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 33:6" />Ado adieke awoukpeme akịtte akañkañ naña adi ado anye ifịtte adukpoñ adidʌt mme awo utọñ ndin akañkañ adi anyʌñ asobo uwem awo, ediiben uwem mbon awo ado ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ammọ, ami ñyaamʌm awoukpeme mbịp mbaña iyiib ammọ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 33:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 33:7" />“Ayịn awo, ami mmunịm fiin nte awoukpeme nnọ mbon Isrel; ke ntoro kop ikọ se ami ntañ nyʌñ dat ado dʌt ammọ utọñ. <verse eid="EZK 33:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 33:8" />Ke ini ami mbooho awo ibak, ‘Afo awo ibak, ke akpanikọ afo ayaakpa,’ ado afo utañña usio nọ anam ammọ ewuọ ekpọñ usʌñ ibak ammọ, awo ibak ado ayaakpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ amọ, ndin iyiib amọ aduudoro fiin ke idem. <verse eid="EZK 33:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 33:9" />Ado adieke afo adʌttọ awo ibak utọñ nọ awuọ akpọñ idiọọk usʌñ ammọ ndin ammọ inamma ado, ammọ eyaekpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ammọ, ado afo ayaabọkkọ.”<verse eid="EZK 33:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 33:10" />“Ayịn awo, dọkkọ nditọ Isrel ate, ‘Se ndufo etañ ado ami, nnamndue ye ndiọiñkpọ ñnyịn isuuhọ ñnyịn anịm, ñko ñnyịn imiyeppe ke ntak ammọ. Die ndin ke ñnyịn idiidu uwem?’ ” <verse eid="EZK 33:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 33:11" />Dọkkọ ammọ ate, adaña nte ami nduuho uwem, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ, ami nnemme esịd mbaña ñkpa awo ibak, ado yak ammọ ekappa esịd ekpọñ idiọọkñkpọ ammọ enyʌñ edu uwem. Iwọññọ! Iwọññọ ikpọñ mme idiọọk usʌñ ndufo! Mbon Isrel, nsoo ido ntak a-ndufo ekpekpaaha?<verse eid="EZK 33:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 33:12" />“Ke ntoro, ayịn awo, dọkkọ mbon mfo ate, ‘Adieke adinen awo atreke utọñ, eyaebat akaan adinenido amọ ke ikpu-ikpu. Ñko adieke awo ibak akappake esịd, akaan ibak awo ado idiibenne ubiomikpe isọk anye. Awo idiiyakka adinen awo a-anamma idiọọkñkpọ adu uwem akpesʌkado ammọ ekedoññoke ndinen.’ <verse eid="EZK 33:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 33:13" />Adieke ami mbooho adinen awo ke akpanikọ ke ana ammọ edu uwem, ado ammọ ebuọt idem ke adinenido ammọ enyʌñ enam idiọọk ido, awo idiitoiyoke ndinen ñkpọ ndomokeed se awo ado akenam; ammọ eyaekpa ke idiọọkñkpọ a-ammọ enamma. <verse eid="EZK 33:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 33:14" />Ñko adieke ami mbooho awo ibak, ‘ke akpanikọ afo ayaakpa,’ ado ammọ ewọññọ ekpọñ idiọọkñkpọ ammọ enyʌñ enam se idot inyʌñ ifọn, <verse eid="EZK 33:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 33:15" />adieke ammọ enọọhọ se ammọ ekebọọ ke isọn ke idak unwọñọ, eyaak se ammọ ekeyịp enọ unie, ekeene mme mbed edatta uwem edi, inyʌññọ inam idiọọkñkpọ ndomokeed, ke akpanikọ awo ado ayaadu uwem; ammọ idiikpaaha. <verse eid="EZK 33:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 33:16" />Awo idiitoiyoke idiọọkñkpọ ndomokeed se awo ado akenam inọ anye. Ammọ e-enam se idot inyʌñ inen; ana ammọ edu uwem.”<verse eid="EZK 33:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 33:17" />“Ado mbon mfo ebo, ‘Usʌñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inenne.’ Ado usʌñ ammọ ado se iminenne. <verse eid="EZK 33:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 33:18" />Adieke adinen awo awọññọke akpọñ adinenido amọ akenam idiọọkñkpọ, ammọ eyaekpa ke ntak ado. <verse eid="EZK 33:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 33:19" />Ñko idiọọk awo akpekpọñ idiọọk usʌñ ibak amọ anyʌñ anam se ifọn ye se idot, ammọ eyaedu uwem ke adinam ado. <verse eid="EZK 33:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 33:20" />Ado ndufo nditọ Isrel ebo, ‘Usʌñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inenne.’ Ado ami ndiikpe ikpe ndufo keedekeed ñkeene usʌñ ndufo.”<verse eid="EZK 33:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Enam Iduọ Yeruselem Anwaña</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 33:21" />Adikem ke ayọhọ isua duob mme iba tọọñọ ekitañ ñnyịn efep, ke ayọhọ afiọñ duob ke ayọhọ usen ition, awodeen a-akebọkkọke afeghe akpọñ Yeruselem amaadi ambịne miin adibo, “Abio ado aduọ!” <verse eid="EZK 33:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 33:22" />Ndin ndubiayio ado mbemiso awodeen ado adiwuọ, ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amandoro miin ke idem, ñko anye amaatat inua mmi mbemiso awodeen ado adi ambịne miin ubakusen. Ke ntoro inua mmi amaatara, ñko ami ñkidoppo uyio aba.<verse eid="EZK 33:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 33:23" />Akem ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 33:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 33:24" />“Ayịn awo, mme mbon e-edʌññọ ke ndoon ke isọñ Isrel ebo, ‘Ebraham akedo awo keed kpọd, ado anye amaadat isọñ anie. Ado ñnyịn imiwak; ke akpanikọ i-inọ ñnyịn isọñ nte udeeme ñkpọ ñnyịn.’ <verse eid="EZK 33:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 33:25" />Ke ntoro dọkkọ ammọ ate ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo: ‘Sia adooho ndufo eta unam i-iyiib asʌkkọ asesịne anye ke idem, enyʌñ ese mme ubobodñkpọ ndufo, enyʌñ eduọk iyiib, nte ado se ndufo edat isọñ enie? <verse eid="EZK 33:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 33:26" />Ndufo ebuọt idem ke akañkañ ndufo, ndufo enañña mbubiam ñkpọ, ñko ndufo keedekeed emesappa ibaan mbọhọidʌñ ndufo. Akpa asʌk ado se ndufo edat isọñ enie?’ ”<verse eid="EZK 33:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 33:27" />“Tañ ami nọ ammọ: ‘Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Adaña nte ami nduuho uwem, mbon esʌhọke ke mme nsobo eyaeduọññọ ke akañkañ, mbon esʌhọke ke ñwuudo eyaeduọññọ ke akañkañ, ami ñyaayaak nnọ mme idiọọk unam nọ eta, mbon e-ebaaha ke akpọsọñ itie ye ke abaitiad ediikpa ke idiọọk udọñọ nsobo. <verse eid="EZK 33:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 33:28" />Ami ñyaanam isọñ akappa ado ataha ndoon, ñko adudu ñkịdidem amọ ayaanie utịd, ndin mme ikpọabod Isrel eyaedoñño ikpu-ikpu nọ ato do awo isañake ammọ iboiyo. <verse eid="EZK 33:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 33:29" />Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini ami mmaanam isọñ ado akappa ntaha ndoon ke ntak mme mbubiam ñkpọ a-ammọ enamma.’<verse eid="EZK 33:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 33:30" />“Ayịn awo, amaado afo, mbon mfo esʌk etie keed etañ ikọ ubaña fiin ke mben ndibene ye ke inuausʌñ ufọk, ebo emọ-emọ, ‘Idikop etob a-atooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adi.’ <verse eid="EZK 33:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 33:31" />Mbon mmi edi ubịne fiin, naña ammọ esidak enam, enyʌñ utie fiin ke iso adikop ikọ mfo, ado ibenne ammọ isịn ke adinam. Inua ammọ atañ abaña ima, ado esịd ammọ ayem idiọọk udod. <verse eid="EZK 33:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 33:32" />Ke aditʌm ntañ, afo udooho ñkpọ ndomokeed ke iso ammọ ukan awo a-akwọọhọ ikwọ ima ke inem uyio anyʌñ akwak ñkukwak mfọn-mfọn, sia adooho ammọ e-ekop se afo atañ ado ibenne isịn ke adinam.”<verse eid="EZK 33:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 33:33" />“Ke ini afịd ñkpọ ami amaawuọ iwọt idem, a-adooho ayaawuọ iwọt, ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke prọfed mmọdo ke ufọọd ammọ.”<verse eid="EZK 33:33" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 33" />
  <chapter number="34" style="c" sid="EZK 34" />
  <para style="s1">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Ayaado Akpemeedọñ Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 34:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin idem ate: <verse eid="EZK 34:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 34:2" />“Ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi baña mme akpemeedọñ Isrel; tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo ammọ ate: ‘Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Adọdiọọk inọ ndufo mme akpemeedọñ Isrel e-eseeghe ñkpọ ebaña idem ndufo ikpọọñ! Nte mme akpemeedọñ ikpinaaha ese ñkpọ ebaña mme edọñ? <verse eid="EZK 34:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 34:3" />Ndufo emenwọñ mmọọñeba, emesịne afọñidem e-enamma ke idededọñ enyʌñ ewot unam se ema, ado ndufo iseeghe ñkpọ ibaña udịmedọñ. <verse eid="EZK 34:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 34:4" />Ndufo isọọñọke mbon mmemidem idem, inyʌññọ ikọk mbon udọñọ me adinwam mbon e-enieghe unan. Ndufo ibenne mbon se iyooñ itịmme idi, inyʌññọ iyem mbon e-esoppo. Ndufo ekara ammọ ke mfiomo ye ke ntiim. <verse eid="EZK 34:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 34:5" />Ke ntoro ammọ emaesuana sia mme andikpeme ikibaaha, ndin ke ini ammọ ekesuanake, ammọ emaekappa edo ndidia enọ afịd mme afai unam. <verse eid="EZK 34:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 34:6" />Mme edọñ mmi emaeyooñ ke afịd ikpọabod ye ke afịd ñkoñ-ñkoñ abod. Ammọ emaesuana ke afịd ederimbod, ndin ibaaha awo se ikiyeem me iduuñọ ibaña ammọ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 34:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 34:7" />“Do ndin, ndufo mme akpemeedọñ, ikop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>: Se <verse eid="EZK 34:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 34:8" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo, ‘Ma uwem mmi, sia adooho mme ufene mmi e-enana andikpeme ñko ke ntoro e-ekappa edo mbịme enyʌñ edo ndidia enọ mme unam afai, ñko sia mme akpemeedọñ imiikiyemme mme edọñ mmi ado ese ñkpọ ebaña idem ammọ utu ke mme ufene mmi, <verse eid="EZK 34:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 34:9" />ke ntoro ndufo mme akpemeedọñ ikop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>: <verse eid="EZK 34:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 34:10" />Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ami mmeyat esịd ye mme akpemeedọñ, ndin ami ñyaamʌm ammọ nọ enam ibad ufene mmi. Ami ñyaasio ammọ ñkpọñ adise ñkpọ mbaña mme udịmedọñ mmi nọ ato do mme akpemeedọñ edikan enọọ idem ammọ ndidia aba. Ami ñyaafak edọñ mmi nsio ammọ ke inua ndin ammọ idiidooho ndidia aba inọ ammọ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 34:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 34:11" />“ ‘Sia se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ke idem mmi ñyaayem mme edọñ mmi ñnyʌñ nse ñkpọ mbaña ammọ.’ <verse eid="EZK 34:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 34:12" />Kpa naña akpemeedọñ ase ñkpọ abaña udịmedọñ amọ esuanake ke ini anye abaaha ye ammọ, kpa ntoro ke ami ndiise ñkpọ mbaña mme edọñ mmi. Ami ñyaafak ammọ nsio ke afịd itie se ammọ ekesuana ke usen ntọñanyọñ ye akịm. <verse eid="EZK 34:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 34:13" />Ami ñyaasịññe ammọ ke atu mme idịd ñnyʌñ ñkoot ammọ mbok ke atu mme idʌñ, ñko ami ñyaaben ammọ ntịmme ndi isọñ emana ammọ. Ami ñyaabọọk ammọ ke mme ikpọabod Isrel, ke mme abedeñ ye ke afịd itie idʌñ ke isọñ Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 34:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 34:14" />Ami ñyaabọọk ammọ ke eti mbid, ñko mme ñkoñ-ñkoñ ikpọabod Isrel ediido itie ndidia ammọ. Do ke ammọ ediisuuk inaa ke eti itie ndidia, do ñko ke ammọ ediita nsek mbid ke ikpọabod Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 34:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 34:15" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ, ‘Ami ke idem mmi ñyaabọọk edọñ mmi ñnyʌñ nnam ammọ esuuk enaa’ <verse eid="EZK 34:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 34:16" />Ami ñyaayem mbon se isop ñnyʌñ ñkoono mbon se iyooñ ntịmme ndi. Ami ñyaabọp se inie unan ñnyʌñ nsọọñọ mbon mmemidem idem, ado mbon se ikpoon inyʌñ isọọñ ke ami ndiisobo. Ami ñyaakpeme ufene ke unen.”<verse eid="EZK 34:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 34:17" />“ ‘Amaado ndufo, mme ufene mmi, ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ami ñyaakpe ikpe ke ufọọd emọ-emọ edọñ, ye ke ufọọd mme akukịmedọñ ye mme ebod. <verse eid="EZK 34:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 34:18" />Ado nte ikemme ndufo adita eti mbid? Akena nte ndufo esọnnọ mme mbid se isʌhọ ke ñkpad? Ado nte ikemme ndufo adinwọñ nsana mmọọñ? Akena nte ndufo etịmede se isʌhọ ke ñkpad? <verse eid="EZK 34:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 34:19" />Nte ana mme ufene mmi edia se ndufo ekesọnnọ me se ndufo ekenuakka ke ñkpad?’ ”<verse eid="EZK 34:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 34:20" />“ ‘Ke ntoro, ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ anọ ammọ: Se, ami ke idem mmi ñyaakpe ikpe ke atu edọñ ekponno idem ye mbon e-esịppe idem. <verse eid="EZK 34:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 34:21" />Sia adooho ndufo ekama ñkañ ye afara enuuk, enyʌñ ekama nnʌk etuai mme edọñ i-idem amemme tutu ndufo ebịne ammọ esio, <verse eid="EZK 34:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 34:22" />ami ñyaanyaaña ufene mmi tutu ammọ idooho mbịme aba. Ami ñyaakpe ikpe ke ufọọd edọñ keed ye aken. <verse eid="EZK 34:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 34:23" />Ami ñyaanịm akpemeedọñ keed nnọ ammọ, ayịnufọk mmi Defid, anye ñko ayaabọọk ammọ; anye ayaabọọk ammọ anyʌñ ado akpemeedọñ anọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 34:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 34:24" />Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñyaado Abasi ammọ, ndin ayịnufọk mmi Defid adiido akpan abọọñ ke atu ammọ. Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ntañ.<verse eid="EZK 34:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 34:25" />“ ‘Ami ñyaanam edioomo emem ye ammọ ñnyʌñ nsịññe ndiọi unam ke isọñ nọ ato do ammọ edʌñọ ke anaan enyʌñ ena edaiya ke mme akai ke ifuuro. <verse eid="EZK 34:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 34:26" />Ami ñyaanam ammọ ye mme itie e-ekannake abod mmi ekʌk edo adidiọñ. Ami ñyaanam edịm adep ke akemini; mbara adidiọñ ayaaba. <verse eid="EZK 34:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 34:27" />Mme eto eyaenwịm mfịd ammọ, isọñ ayaanyʌñ anọ mbunwịm amọ; mme awo eyaedʌñ ke isọñ ke ifuuro. Ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ini ami mmaabuuñ akpọnọ mbiomo ammọ ñnyʌñ mfak ammọ nsio ke ubọk mbon ekesịnne ammọ ke ufʌn. <verse eid="EZK 34:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 34:28" />Ammọ idiidooho aba mbịme inọ mme idịd, ñko ndiọi unam ikọd idiitaaha ammọ. Ammọ eyaedʌñọ ke ifuuro, ndin awo ndomokeed idiinamma ammọ ekop ndịk. <verse eid="EZK 34:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 34:29" />Ami ñyaanọ ammọ isọñ awuọhọ etob ke ntak mbunwịm amọ, ñko ammọ idiikịtte akañ aba, idiinyʌññọ ido ñkpọ nsaha inọ mme idịd. <verse eid="EZK 34:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 34:30" />Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ, mmọdo mba ye ammọ ndin ke ammọ, nditọ Isrel, edo mbon mmi, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 34:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 34:31" />Ndufo edo mme edọñ mmi, edọñ a-ami mbọọhọ, ñko ami ndo Abasi ndufo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 34:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 34" />
  <chapter number="35" style="c" sid="EZK 35" />
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi A-abañake Edọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 35:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 35:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 35:2" />“Ayịn awo, nen iso se Abod Sei; tañ prọfesi baña anye <verse eid="EZK 35:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 35:3" />nyʌñ bo: ‘Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ami ñyaanam ikọ ye afo, Abod Sei, ñko ami ñyaanyan ubọk mmi ubaña fiin ñnyʌñ nnam afo ado itie nsobo ye mbiara. <verse eid="EZK 35:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 35:4" />Ami ñyaanam mme idʌñ mfo ekappa edo ndoon. Ndin afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 35:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 35:5" />“ ‘Sia adooho afo amaamʌm akaan udu asịn ke esịd anyʌñ ayaak nditọ Isrel anọ akañkañ ke ini ukuud ammọ, ini se ufen ammọ akenekke akpon, <verse eid="EZK 35:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 35:6" />ke ntoro, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo, maama uwem mmi, ami ñyaiyaak ndufo nnọ uduọkiyiib ndin anye ayaadubịnne ndufo. Sia ndufo imiikisuaha uduọk iyiib, uduọkiyiib ayaibịne ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 35:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 35:7" />Ami ñyaanam Abod Sei ado ataa idiọọk nsobo ñnyʌñ ñkpịkke afịd mbon se ika inyʌñ inyọñ ke ukañ amọ nsio. <verse eid="EZK 35:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 35:8" />Ami ñyaayọhọ mme ikpọabod ndufo ye mbon e-ekpaññake afai; mbon ewotto ke akañkañ eyaeduọññọ ke abod ndufo ye ke mme ndua ndufo ye ke mme abedeñ ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 35:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 35:9" />Ami ñyaanam ndufo edo ñwuudo ke nsi-nsi; awo idiidʌññọ ke mme abio ndufo aba. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="EZK 35:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 35:10" />“ ‘Sia adooho afo amebo, “Mme idịd ye mme abio iba ami eyaedo ake ñnyịn ndin ñnyịn iyaidat ammọ inie,” akpesʌkado ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñkebaaha do, <verse eid="EZK 35:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 35:11" />ke ntoro <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abo, ma uwem mmi, ami ndiinam ñkpọ ye afo ñkeene iyadesịd ye ufịb a-ndufo ekewọttọ ke usua a-ndufo ekenieghe enọọ ammọ, ndin ami ñko ñyaanam ammọ endiọọñọ miin ke ini ami ñkpeeghe ikpe iwuod ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 35:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 35:12" />Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, mmaakop afịd abʌd-abʌd ñkpọ se ndufo eketañ ebaña mme ikpọabod ke Isrel. Ndufo ekebo “Emaeyaak ammọ enịm nọ abiara enyʌñ eyaak inọ ñnyịn ebo isobo.” <verse eid="EZK 35:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 35:13" />Ndufo emaenam inua embaña miin, enyʌñ etaañ ikọ embaña miin inieghe ubere, ami mmaanyʌñ ñkop. <verse eid="EZK 35:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 35:14" />Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ke ini afịd ederimbod edaarake, ami ñyainam ndufo edo ñwuudo. <verse eid="EZK 35:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 35:15" />Sia adooho ndufo emaenem esịd ke ini udeeme ñkpọ Isrel akedooho ñwuudo, kpa ntoro ke ami ndiinam ndufo. Abod Sei, afo ye afịd Edọm ediido ñwuudo. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 35:15" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 35" />
  <chapter number="36" style="c" sid="EZK 36" />
  <para style="s1">Idodanyen A-anieghe Ikpọabod Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 36:1" />“Ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi nọ ikpọabod Isrel nyʌñ bo, ‘Ikpọabod Isrel, ikop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ <verse eid="EZK 36:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 36:2" />Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Awo usua akubo fiin, ‘Aha! Mme ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie esed e-ekappa edo udeeme ñnyịn.’ ” <verse eid="EZK 36:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 36:3" />Ke ntoro tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo, “Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Sia adooho ammọ unuak enyʌñ usọnnọ fiin ke afịd usʌñ nọ ato do afo akanna ado udeeme mme idịd mfen ye ñkpọ se ekama etop ufiid ye ñkpọ asuenne, <verse eid="EZK 36:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 36:4" />ke ntoro, mme ikpọabod Isrel ekop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara: Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ anọ mme ikpọabod ye ntəkabod, mme itịkke isọñ ye abedeñ, mme ñwuudo ndoon ye mme idʌñ e-emaekesịn a-mme idịd e-edaaha idiana ndufo emaekebịme enyʌñ edọọñ ndọk ado ami, <verse eid="EZK 36:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 36:5" />se Ndakeidem <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke ikañ akpọsọñ ufịb esịd mmi ke ami ntañ mbaña idịd mbon ako, ñnyʌñ ntañ mbaña afịd Edọm, sia ke idadesịd ye ke esịd usua ammọ e-eben isọñ mmi enịm udeeme ammọ nọ ato do ammọ eben mbid e-edatta ebọọk ufeene enịm mbịme. <verse eid="EZK 36:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 36:6" />Ke ntoro tañ prọfesi nọ isọñ Isrel nyʌñ bo mme ikpọabod ye ntəkabod, mme abedeñ ye mme itịkke isọñ: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ntañ ikọ ke ufịb ye ifiobesịd sia adooho ndufo emaebiom asuenne mme idịd. <verse eid="EZK 36:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 36:7" />Ke ntoro, se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami mmedịppe ubọk ke anyọñ ñnwọñọ mbo ke mme idịd e-edaaha idiana ndufo eyaenyʌñ ebọ ndọk.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 36:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 36:8" />“ ‘Ado ndufo, ikpọabod Isrel, eyaesakka ñkọk ye mfịd enọ ikọd mmi Isrel, sia adooho ammọ eyaesọp enyọñ edi ufọk. <verse eid="EZK 36:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 36:9" />Ami mmenie akikere unọ fiin, ñko ami ñyause fiin ke anyen mfọn; eyautem fiin enyʌñ etọ, <verse eid="EZK 36:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 36:10" />ñko ami ñyaanam uwak awo edʌñọ ke anyọñ mfo, ii, afịd Isrel. Eyaedʌñọ ke mme idʌñ ado enyʌñ emaana ebọọp mme ndoon. <verse eid="EZK 36:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 36:11" />Ami ñyaanam ibad awo ye unam se idʌñọ ke anyọñ mfo etọt, ndin ammọ eyaenwịm mfịd ekappa ewak. Ami ñyaanam mme awo edidʌñọ ke anyọñ mfo naña akedo ke esed, ñko ami ñyaanam afo amọinyọ akan akpa. Ndin afo ayaadiọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="EZK 36:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 36:12" />Ami ñyaanam ikọd mmi Isrel edʌñọ ke afo. Ammọ eyaudat fiin enie, ndin afo ayaado udeeme ñkpọ ammọ; tutu amama afo uduuyakka ammọ enana nditọ aba.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 36:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 36:13" />“ ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Sia adooho usʌk awo ibo ndufo, “Ndufo esibeben awo emen, inyʌññọ iyak idịd ndufo enie nditọ,” <verse eid="EZK 36:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 36:14" />ke ntoro, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo, afo uduumenne awo aba, uduunyʌññọ unam idịd mfo anana nditọ. <verse eid="EZK 36:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 36:15" />Ami ndiiyakka nọ akop aseeme mme idịd aba, ñko ndiiyakka afo abiom isuuñọ mme awo aba me adinam nọ mme abio mfo aduọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 36:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Eyaemaana Edịppe Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 36:16" />Akem ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaamaana adinsịm miin idem ate: <verse eid="EZK 36:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 36:17" />“Ayịn awo, ke ini nditọ Isrel ekedʌñọke ke idʌñ ammọ, ammọ emaesappa anye ato ke se ammọ ekenañña. Adinam ammọ akeba ke iso mmi nte ndek itieisọñ a-awonwaan anieghe kwa afiọñ. <verse eid="EZK 36:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 36:18" />Ke ntoro ami mmaanwañña iyadesịd mmi nduọk ammọ sia emaeduọk iyiib ke isọñ, ñko sia ammọ emaesappa isọñ ye mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 36:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 36:19" />Ami mmaasuan ammọ ndọñ ke mme idịd, ñko ammọ emaesuana ke mme idʌñ; ami ñkekpe ikpe nnọ ammọ ñkeene mme adinam ammọ <verse eid="EZK 36:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 36:20" />Ndin itie keed akeedodo a-ammọ ekekaaha ke atu mme idịd ammọ emaesappa adisana anyịñ mmi, sia emaetañ ebaña ammọ ebo, ‘Mbon ami edoñño mbon <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> kpayeado akena ammọ ekpọñ isọñ amọ.’ <verse eid="EZK 36:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 36:21" />Ami mmaakop mbọm mbaña adisana anyịñ mmi a-mbon Isrel ekesappake ke atu mme idịd se ammọ ekekaiya.<verse eid="EZK 36:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 36:22" />“Ke ntoro tañ nọ nditọ Isrel bo, ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Nditọ Isrel idooho ke ntak ndufo ke ami ñyem inam ñkpọ ami, ado ke ntak adisana anyịñ mmi, a-ndufo ekesappake ke atu mme idịd se ndufo ekekaiya. <verse eid="EZK 36:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 36:23" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara anyʌñ abo ntom, ami ñyaawọt naña akwa anyịñ mmi ado adisana, a-ndufo ekesappake ke atu mme idịd, anyịñ a-ndufo ekesappake ke atu ammọ. Ndin mme idịd eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini ndufo emaenam nọ ami ndo adisana ke anyen ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 36:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 36:24" />“ ‘Sia ami ñyaisịññe ndufo mfep ke mme idịd; ami ñyaikoot ndufo mbok nto mme abio, ñnyʌñ iben ndufo ntịmme ñkaa isọñ ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 36:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 36:25" />Ami ñyaisiime ndufo adisana mmọọñ, ndin ndufo eyaesana; ami ñyaisio ndufo afịd ndek ke idem ñnyʌñ idiañña ndufo ñkpọñ mme ubobodñkpọ ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 36:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 36:26" />Ami ñyainọ ndufo ufa esịd ñnyʌñ isịn ndufo ufa sịbidịd ke idem; ami ñyaasịññe esịd itiad ndufo ñkanna inọ ndufo esịd a-anieghe abʌk. <verse eid="EZK 36:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 36:27" />Ami ñyaisịn ndufo sịbidịd mmi ke idem ñnyʌñ inək ndufo nọ ekeene ewʌhọ mmi enyʌñ ekpeme adinịm mme mbed mmi. <verse eid="EZK 36:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 36:28" />Ndin ndufo eyaedʌñ ke isọñ a-ami ñkenọọhọ mme eteete ndufo; ndufo eyaedo mbon mmi, ami ñko ñyaado Abasi ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 36:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 36:29" />Ami ñyainyaaña ndufo nsio ke ndek ndufo. Ami ñyaanam abakpa awak inọ ndufo, ndin ndiinamma akañ aba ke atu ndufo aba. <verse eid="EZK 36:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 36:30" />Ami ñyaanam mfịd eto ye mbunwịm inwañ ndufo ewak, nọ ato do ndufo ikiibọọ ndọk ito mme idịd aba ke ntak akañ. <verse eid="EZK 36:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 36:31" />Ndin ndufo eyaetoiyo mme idiọọk usʌñ ndufo ye mme adinam ibak ndufo, ñko ndufo eyaesua idem ndufo ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ye mme ñkpọ a-atekke awo esịd a-ndufo ekenamma. <verse eid="EZK 36:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 36:32" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo, ami ñyem nọ ndufo ediọọñọ ke ami nnamma ami ke ntak ndufo. Ikop abuud ye asuenne ke adinam ndufo, nditọ Isrel!<verse eid="EZK 36:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 36:33" />“ ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ke usen a-ami ndiiyet afịd ndiọiñkpọ ndufo nsio, ami ñyaamaana nnam ndufo edʌñ ke abio ndufo ñnyʌñ mmaana mbọp ndoon ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 36:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 36:34" />Eyaemaana etọ ñkpọ ke isọñ amaakebiara utu ke anye ana nsobo ke iso mme awo se isaña iboiyo. <verse eid="EZK 36:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 36:35" />Ndin ammọ eyaebo, “Isọñ a-akedooho mbiara a-akappa aba nte inwañ Idịn; mme idʌñ e-ekekappake ndoon, nsobo ye ñwuudo, e-ekappa enie ndibene idahami enyʌñ edo se edʌñ.” <verse eid="EZK 36:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 36:36" />Ndin mme idịd se isʌhọ e-edaaha idiana ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmemaana mbọp se emaekewuut, ñko mmaana ntọ se emaekesobo. Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmetañ, ndin ñyaanam.’<verse eid="EZK 36:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 36:37" />“Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ini keed mfen ami ñyaakpañ utọñ nnọ ebeeñe Isrel ñnyʌñ nnam ami nnọ ammọ: Ami ñyaanam ammọ ewak nte edọñ, <verse eid="EZK 36:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 36:38" />nte ibad mme ufene e-edatta enam uwa ke Yeruselem ke mme ini usọrọ ekemme. Kpa ntoro ke ñwuudo abio adiiyọhọ ye mme atu awo. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="EZK 36:38" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 36" />
  <chapter number="37" style="c" sid="EZK 37" />
  <para style="s1">Abedeñ Nsaad Akpọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 37:1" />Ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amandoro miin ke idem, ndin anye amansio miin awuọ ke Sịbidịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anyʌñ amben miin akaa ufọọd abedeñ; a-akeyọhọke ye nsaad akpọ. <verse eid="EZK 37:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 37:2" />Anye amamben miin asaña akaa iso ye edem ke ufọọd ammọ, ndin ami mmaakịt ekamba uwak akpọ ke isọñ abedeñ ado, mme akpọ emaekenekke esaat. <verse eid="EZK 37:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 37:3" />Anye amambịp miin, “Ayịn awo, nte mme akpọ ami ekeme edidu uwem?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 37:3">Ami mmaabo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara, afo ikpọọñ adiọọñọ.”<verse eid="EZK 37:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 37:4" />Ndin anye amambo miin, “Tañ prọfesi nọ mme akpọ ami nyʌñ bo ammọ, ‘Mme nsaad akpọ, ikop ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>! <verse eid="EZK 37:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 37:5" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ anọ mme akpọ ami ado ami: Ami ñyaanam ibifịk<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ibifịk akeme iwuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">afịm</char><char style="ft" closed="false">me </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">sịbidịd</char><char style="ft" closed="false">(se ke Esi 37:6-14).</char></note> idʌk ndufo, ndin ndufo eyaetịmme edu uwem. <verse eid="EZK 37:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 37:6" />Ami ñyaadat asịb idian ndufo ñnyʌñ nnam abʌk ito ndufo awuọ, ñnyʌñ ifʌk ndufo ikpaidem; ami ñyaisịn ndufo ibifịk, ndin ndufo eyaenie uwem. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 37:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 37:7" />Ntoro ke ami ñketañ prọfesi kpa naña ekendọñ. Ndin ke ami nsʌkkọ ntatañ prọfesi do, mmaakop uyom, uyio ñkpoyo, ñko mme akpọ emaesaña ediana keed, akpọ adiana akpọ. <verse eid="EZK 37:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 37:8" />Ami mmaase, ndin asịb ye abʌk emaewuọñọ ke ammọ, ikpaidem anyʌñ afʌk ammọ, ado ibifịk ikibaaha ammọ ke idem.<verse eid="EZK 37:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 37:9" />Ndin anye amambo miin, “Tañ prọfesi nọ ibifịk; ayịn awo tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo anye, ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ibifịk, to ke mbeñ afịm inaañ nyʌñ nweek uwem sịn ke mme akpañña afai ami, nọ ato do ammọ ekeme edidu uwem.’ ” <verse eid="EZK 37:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 37:10" />Ke ntoro, ami mmaatañ prọfesi naña anye akembo miin, ndin ibifịk amaadʌk ammọ; ammọ emaenie uwem enyʌñ edakka eda ke ukod, ekamba udịmawo.<verse eid="EZK 37:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 37:11" />Ndin anye amambo miin: “Ayịn awo, mme akpọ ami edoñño mbon Isrel. Ammọ ebo, ‘Mme akpọ ñnyịn esaat ñko idodanyen ñnyịn akpa mfʌhọ; i-isobo ñnyịn esio.’ <verse eid="EZK 37:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 37:12" />Ke ntoro tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo ammọ: ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Mbon mmi, ami ñyaakʌppọ mme udi ndufo ñnyʌñ isịññe ndufo ndi; ami ñyaiben ndufo ntịmme ñkaa isọñ Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 37:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 37:13" />Ndin ndufo, mbon mmi, eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke ini ami mmaakʌppọ udi ndufo ñnyʌñ isịññe ndufo ndi. <verse eid="EZK 37:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 37:14" />Ami ñyaisịn ndufo Sịbidịd mmi ke idem ndin ndufo eyaedu uwem, ñko ami ñyaanam ndufo eba ke isọñ ndufo. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmetañ, ke mmenyʌñ nnam, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>atañ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 37:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Idịd Keed ke Idak Adidem Keed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 37:15" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin idem ate: <verse eid="EZK 37:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 37:16" />“Ayịn awo, ben akpọk eto keed nyʌñ wet, ‘A-anieghe Yuda ye mbon Isrel se iwuana ye anye.’ Ñko, ben akpọk eto mfen nyʌñ wet, ‘A-anieghe Yosef (a-adooho ake Ifrem) ye afịd mbon Isrel se iwuana ye anye.’ <verse eid="EZK 37:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 37:17" />Dian ammọ keed nọ ekappa edo eto keed nọ ato do ammọ ekappa edo keed ke ubọk mfo.<verse eid="EZK 37:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 37:18" />“Ke ini mbon mfo ubịppe fiin ebo, ‘Afo uduudọkkọke ñnyịn se ami awuọñọ?’ <verse eid="EZK 37:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 37:19" />Bo ammọ ntom, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaaben eto Yosef, a-asịneke ke ubọk Ifrem, ye ake mme esiin Isrel ewaanake ye anye, ñnyʌñ ndian keed ye eto Yuda. Ami ñyaanam ammọ ekappa edo adukpọk eto keed, ndin ammọ eyaekappa edo keed ke ubọk mmi.’ <verse eid="EZK 37:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 37:20" />Kama akpọk eto ado a-afo awette ñkpọ da ke iso ammọ <verse eid="EZK 37:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 37:21" />nyʌñ bo ammọ, ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaasio mbon Isrel ke mme idịd a-ammọ ekekaiyake. Ami ñyaakoot ammọ mbok nsịññe ke afịd mme itie se ammọ ekebañña ñnyʌñ mben ammọ ntịmme ñnyọñ ndi isọñ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 37:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 37:22" />Ami ñyaanam ammọ edo idịd keed ke isọñ ado, ke mme ikpọabod Isrel. Do adidem keed adiikaara afịd ammọ ndin tutu amama ammọ idiidooho idịd iba aba me adibakka ndo abioubọọñ iba. <verse eid="EZK 37:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 37:23" />Ammọ idiisappake idem ammọ aba ye mme idiọñ ye mme ubobodñkpọ me ye nnamndue ammọ ndomokeed, sia ami ñyaanyaaña ammọ nsio ke afịd ndiọiñkpọ mfiakedem ammọ, ñko ami ñyaayet ammọ esana. Ammọ eyaedo mbon mmi, ami ñko ñyaado Abasi ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 37:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 37:24" />“ ‘Ayịnufọk mmi Defid ayaado adidem anọ ammọ, ñko ammọ eyaenie akpemeedọñ keed. Ammọ eyaekeene mme mbed mmi enyʌñ ekpeme adinịm mme ewʌhọ mmi. <verse eid="EZK 37:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 37:25" />Ammọ eyaedʌñọ ke isọñ a-ami ñkenọọhọ Yekọb ayịnufọk mmi, isọñ a-mme eteete ndufo ekedʌñọke. Ammọ ye nditọ ammọ ye nditọnditọ ammọ eyaedʌñọ do ke nsi-nsi, ñko Defid ayịnufọk mmi adiido akpanabọọñ ammọ ke nsi-nsi. <verse eid="EZK 37:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 37:26" />Ami ñyaanam edioomo emem ye ammọ, a-adiido nsi-nsi edioomo. Ami ñyaanam ammọ esọọñ eda enyʌñ etọt ewak ke ibad, ñko ami ñyaadaaha adisana itie mmi ke atu ammọ ke nsi-nsi. <verse eid="EZK 37:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 37:27" />Itie idʌñ mmi adiiba ye ammọ; ami ñyaado Abasi ammọ, ñko ammọ eyaedo mbon mmi. <verse eid="EZK 37:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 37:28" />Ndin mme idịd eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> nnam Isrel esana, ke ini adisana itie mmi abaaha ye ammọ ke nsi-nsi.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 37:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 37" />
  <chapter number="38" style="c" sid="EZK 38" />
  <para style="s1">Akwa Adikan <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Atu mme Idịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 38:1" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadinsịm miin ate: <verse eid="EZK 38:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 38:2" />“Ayịn awo, nen iso mfo nọ ñkañ Kọk ke utịd ñkañ Makọk, a-adooho abọọñ ke atu nditọ ideen mbọọñ Mesek ye Tubal; tañ prọfesi baña anye <verse eid="EZK 38:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 38:3" />nyʌñ bo: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Kọk, abọọñ ke atu nditọ ideen mbọọñ ke Mesek ye Tubal, ami mmenie ikọ ye afo. <verse eid="EZK 38:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 38:4" />Ami ñyaukanna fiin nnịm, usịn fiin uwaam ke mbañ ñnyʌñ udʌt fiin nsio ndi ye afịd udịmekọñ mfo; mme enañmbakara mfo, mme awad enañmbakara mfo e-ekamake mme ñkpọ ekọñ, ye mme ikpọ uwak atu awo e-enieñeke mme ikpọ ye mme ntək atuekọñ, a-afịd ammọ ekamake mme akañkañ ammọ ke ubọk. <verse eid="EZK 38:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 38:5" />Pesia, Kuus ye Pud eyaeba ye ammọ, afịd ammọ ye atuekọñ ye itamukwak, <verse eid="EZK 38:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 38:6" />ñko Koma ye afịd udịmekọñ amọ, ye Bed Tokama e-etooho ataa esịd adoro ye afịd udịmekọñ amọ, mme uwak idịd e-ebaaha ye afo.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 38:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 38:7" />Itịm idem; iba ke mbeeñeidem, ndufo ye afịd udịm awo u-ukannake fiin ekʌk, nyʌñ bọ uyio to ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 38:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 38:8" />Ke uwak usen amaaboiyo eyaukoot fiin enọ ñkpọ ekọñ. Ke mme isua ke iso, afo ayaadʌk aben isọñ a-akebọkkọke ekọñ, e-ekekoonoke mbon ammọ eto nsio-nsio mme idịd ekebon ke mme ikpọabod Isrel, e-ekebaaha ke nsobo ke uwak isua. Ekesịññe ammọ ke mme idịd, ñko idahami afịd ammọ edʌñ ke ifuuro. <verse eid="EZK 38:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 38:9" />Ndufo ye afịd mme udịmekọñ ndufo ye mme uwak idịd e-ebaaha ye ndufo eyaedọọk ke anyọñ, e-ebịmme nte ayobio; ndufo ediiba nte ntọñanyọñ afʌkkọ isọñ.<verse eid="EZK 38:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 38:10" />“ ‘Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ke usen ado akikere ayaudʌk fiin esịd ndin afo ayaaduak idiọọk uduak.’ ” <verse eid="EZK 38:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 38:11" />Afo ayaabo, “Ami ñyaadʌk isọñ mme abio e-enanake ndibene; ami ñyaatịmede mbon e-etieghe ke ifuuro ye mbon e-etieghe ke ndueidem; afịd ammọ e-edʌñọke inieghe ndibene ye itịm ye eto usʌñ. <verse eid="EZK 38:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 38:12" />Ami ñyaabịme mbịme ñnyʌñ ñwo ñwo ñnyʌñ ñwọññọ ubọk mmi nse ndoon e-emaanake edidʌñọ ye mbon e-ekoonoke eto mme idịd, e-emọinyọke ke ufene ye ke mme ñkpọ mfen, e-edʌñọke ke ufọọd isọñ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru udịmikọ ami awuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">akob isọñ.</char></note> ado.” <verse eid="EZK 38:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 38:13" />Seba ye Dedan ye mme anyam udua Taasis ye afịd mme abio amọ eyaubo fiin, “Nte afo amedi adibịme mbịme? Afo amekoono atu awo mfo adiwo ñwo, adiben silfa ye kold, adiben ufene ye mme inie ye adibọi mme mbịme?”<verse eid="EZK 38:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 38:14" />“Ke ntoro, ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi nyʌñ bo Kọk: ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke usen ado, ke ini Isrel mbon mmi edʌññọ ke ifuuro, nte afo uduukịtte? <verse eid="EZK 38:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 38:15" />Afo ayaato itie mfo ke anyan adoro adi, afo ye uwak idịd mfen e-esañake ye afo, afịd ammọ ediiwat ke enañmbakara, ekamba atu awo ye mme asọñ idem mbon ekọñ. <verse eid="EZK 38:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 38:16" />Afo ayaawuọ abịne mbon mmi Isrel nte ntọñanyọñ a-afʌkkọ isọñ. Kọk, ke mme usen ediighe ke iso, ami ñyaanam afo anwana ye mbon mmi, nọ ato do mme idịd endiọọñọ miin ke ini ami ndiiwọt idem nte adisana uto fiin ke anyen ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 38:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 38:17" />“ ‘Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Afo ke ami ñketañ mbaña ke mme usen edem nto ke inua nditọufọk mmi e-edooho mme prọfed ke Isrel. Ke ini ado ammọ emaetañ prọfesi ke uwak isua ebo ke ami ñyaanam nọ ndufo etuaha ye ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 38:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 38:18" />Ami ado se idiitịppe ke usen ado: Ke ini Kọk atuahake ye isọñ Isrel, ufiob iyadesịd mmi ayaadakka nduduai, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 38:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 38:19" />Ke nsịnifịk mmi ye akpọsọñ iyadesịd mmi ami mmetañ mbo ke ini ado ekamba unyekisọñ ayaaba ke isọñ Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 38:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 38:20" />Mme iyak ke akpainyañ, mme inuen ke ikpaanyọñ, mme unam ke ikọd, afịd ñkpọ se ebod e-esañake ke isọñ, ye afịd awo e-ebaaha ke unadod eyaenyeñ idem ke iso mmi. Mme ikpọabod eyaewuuro, mme ikpọ itiad eyaesuana, ñko afịd ndibene eyaeduọ ke isọñ. <verse eid="EZK 38:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 38:21" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ami ñyaadọñ akañkañ nnọ Kọk ke afịd ikpọabod mmi. Ayịneka awodeen ayaaben akañkañ akeene emọ-emọ ayịneka awodeen. <verse eid="EZK 38:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 38:22" />Ami ndiidat idiọọk unọmọ ye uduọkiyiib ñkpe ikpe nnọ anye; ami ñyaanam ekamba edịm, edịmitiad ye ikañ adep anọ anye ye mme udịm ammọ ye mme uwak idịd e-ebaaha ye anye. <verse eid="EZK 38:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 38:23" />Ke ntoro ke ami ndiiwọt naña ami ñkpon ñnyʌñ nsana, ndin ami ñyaanam nọ endiọọñọ miin ke uwak mme idịd. Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 38:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 38" />
  <chapter number="39" style="c" sid="EZK 39" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 39:1" />“Ayịn awo, tañ prọfesi baña Kọk nyʌñ bo: ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ abo: Kọk, iwuod ke atu nditọ ideen adidem Mesek ye Tubal, ami mmenie ikọ ye afo. <verse eid="EZK 39:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 39:2" />Ami ñyauwọññọ fiin nnịm ñnyʌñ udʌt fiin ñwere. Ami ñyauben fiin nto anyan adoro ñnyʌñ udọñ fiin aka ikpọabod Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 39:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 39:3" />Ndin ami ñyaukpakka fiin utịgha ke ubọk ufiin nsio ñnyʌñ nnam mme idañ mfo eduọ ke ubọk nnasia. <verse eid="EZK 39:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 39:4" />Afo ayaaduọ ke mme abod Isrel, afo ye afịd udịmekọñ mfo ye mme idịd e-ebaaha ye afo. Ami ñyauben fiin nnọ afịd utọ inuen mba ye mme afai unam ke ikọd nte ndidia. <verse eid="EZK 39:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 39:5" />Afo ayaaduọ ke akpa inwañ, sia ami mmetañ: Uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara ado ami. <verse eid="EZK 39:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 39:6" />Ami ñyaadọñ ikañ aketa Makọk ye mbon e-edʌñọke ke ifuuro ke mme mben inyañ, ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’<verse eid="EZK 39:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 39:7" />“ ‘Ami ñyaanam ammọ ediọọñọ adisana anyịñ mmi eto mbon mmi Isrel. Ami ndiiyakka aba nọ esappa anyịñ mmi ndin mme idịd eyaediọọñọ ke ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ndo Adisana ke Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 39:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 39:8" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> andikara atañ: Asʌk adi! Anye idiitreke adidat itie. Usen a-ami ñketañña mbaña ado ami.<verse eid="EZK 39:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 39:9" />“ ‘Ndin mbon e-edʌññọ ke mme abio Isrel eyaewuọ ekekama ñkpọ ekọñ ebara ikañ esịn enyʌñ efọp ammọ, ntək ye ikpọ atuekọñ, mme utịgha ye idañ, esañ ubọk ekọñ ye eduad. Ke isua itiaba ediikama ammọ nte ñkpọ ubaraikañ. <verse eid="EZK 39:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 39:10" />Ammọ idiikịtte ntak adikitañ ifia ke inwañ me adikikpịkke ke akai, sia adooho ammọ ediidat ñkpọ ekọñ ammọ nte ifia. Ñko ammọ eyaebịme mbon se ikibịme ammọ enyʌñ ewo mbon e-ekewooho ammọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ.<verse eid="EZK 39:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 39:11" />“ ‘Ke usen ado ami ñyaanọ Kọk itie ubuuk awo ke Isrel, kpa ke abedeñ mbon e-ekaaha isañ ke Akpainyañ edem usakkautịn. Anye ayaasiit usʌñ mbon esikaaha isañ, sia adooho Kọk ye afịd udịm ammọ ediibʌhọ do. Ke ntoro ediikoot anye Abedeñ Hamọn Kọk.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39:11 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hamọn Kọk </char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mme atutu Kọk.</char></note><verse eid="EZK 39:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 39:12" />“ ‘Ndin ufọk Isrel eyaedat afiọñ itiaba ebuuk ammọ nọ ato do enam isọñ asana. <verse eid="EZK 39:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 39:13" />Afịd mbon isọñ ami ediibuuk ammọ, ndin usen se ami ndiiyaara ubọọñ mmi adiido usen uwuọetob editoiyo inọ ammọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 39:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 39:14" />Ammọ eyaebakka mme awo enịm kwa ini ebo enam isọñ asana. Ammọ eyaesuana eyọhọ isọñ ye mme mbon mfen, ammọ eyaebuuk afịd mme akpo awo akeedodo e-enaaha ke isọñ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 39:14">“ ‘Ke afiọñ itiaba ado amaaboiyo, ammọ eyaenekke enam nduuñọ. <verse eid="EZK 39:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 39:15" />Kpa naña ammọ esaña ekanna isọñ, awo ndomokeed a-akịtte akpọ awo ana anịm idiọọñọ ke ndo tutu mme atịppe udi ediben ebuuk ke Abedeñ Hamọn Kọk, <verse eid="EZK 39:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 39:16" />ke ñkpere abio e-ekoodo Hamọna<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39:16 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hamọna </char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">atutu.</char></note>. Ndin ammọ eyaenam isọñ asana.’<verse eid="EZK 39:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 39:17" />“Ayịn awo, ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Sio uyio koot afịd utọ inuen ye afịd mme afai unam ikọd: ‘Iboho keed inyʌñ ito ke naña afịd ñkọk idi akpokoro uwa a-ami nnamma inọọ ndufo, ekamba uwa ke mme abod ke Isrel. Do ke ndufo ediita abʌk enyʌñ enwọñ iyiib. <verse eid="EZK 39:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 39:18" />Ndufo eyaeta abʌk ñkpọsọñ ideen enyʌñ enwọñ iyiib nditọ ideen mbọọñ ke ederimbod nte ammọ edoñño mme akukịmedọñ ye nditọedọñ, ebod ye ñyaaraenañ, afịd ammọ edoñño mme ukọkʌk unam e-etooho Basan. <verse eid="EZK 39:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 39:19" />Ke uwa a-ami ndiinam inọ ndufo, ndufo eyaeta akpọñ tutu anye ikak ndufo enyʌñ enwọñ iyiib tutu anye inaam. <verse eid="EZK 39:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 39:20" />Ke akpokoro mmi ndufo eyaekop uyʌkkọ edita enañmbakara ye mme awad enañmbakara, mme ñkpọsọñ awo ye mbon ekọñ ke utọ ke utọ’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 39:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 39:21" />“Ami ñyaayaara ubọọñ mmi ñwọt mme idịd, ndin afịd idịd eyaekịt ufen se ami ndiimia ammọ ye ubọk se ami ndiiyaak ndot ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 39:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 39:22" />Tọọñọ ke usen ado kaa iso, nditọ Isrel eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 39:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 39:23" />Ndin mme idịd eyaediọọñọ ke eketañ ufọk Isrel efep ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ammọ, sia adooho ammọ ikinamma akpanikọ ye ami. Ke ntoro ami mmaadịp ammọ iso mmi ñnyʌñ ñyaak ammọ nnọ mme asua ammọ, afịd ammọ enyʌñ eduọññọ ke akañkañ. <verse eid="EZK 39:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 39:24" />Ami ñkenam ammọ ñkeene ndedeghe ye idiọọk ido ammọ, ndin ami mmadịp ammọ iso mmi.”<verse eid="EZK 39:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 39:25" />“Ke ntoro se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ami ñyaamaana ndemme mfọnọñkpọ Yekọb, ñyaanyʌñ ñkop mbọm mbaña afịd mbon Isrel, ñnyʌñ nsịn ifịk mbaña adisana anyịñ mmi. <verse eid="EZK 39:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 39:26" />Ammọ eyaefre abuud ammọ ye afịd idiọọk ido a-ammọ ekenamma ye ami ke ini ammọ ekedʌññọ ke isọñ ke ifuuro ndin awo ndomokeed ibaaha se idịkke ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 39:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 39:27" />Ke ini ami mmaakeben ammọ nto mme idịd ñnyọñ ndi ñnyʌñ ñkoono ammọ nto mme abio mbon usua ammọ ndibok, afịd mme idịd eyaennịm miin nte adisana eto ke ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 39:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 39:28" />Ndin ammọ eyaediọọñọ ke ami ndo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ, sia akpesʌkado a-ami ñkeyakka etañ ammọ efep ke atu mme idịd, ami ñyaakoono ammọ mbok ke isọñ ammọ, awo ndomokeed idiisʌhọke. <verse eid="EZK 39:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 39:29" />Ami ndiidịppe ammọ iso mmi aba, sia ami ñyaaduọk Sịbidịd mmi nnọ mbon Isrel, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.”<verse eid="EZK 39:29" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 39" />
  <chapter number="40" style="c" sid="EZK 40" />
  <para style="s1">Emaana Ediọñ Itie Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 40:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua edịb mme ition tọọñọ ekitañ ñnyịn efep, ke ntọọñọ isua, ke ayọhọ usen duob ke afiọñ, ke ayọhọ isua duob mme inaañ nte abio akeduọ, ke usen ado ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amandoro miin ke idem anyʌñ amben miin akaa do. <verse eid="EZK 40:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 40:2" />Ke mme ñkukịd Abasi anye amamben miin akaa isọñ Isrel anyʌñ akennịm miin ke ataa ñkoñ-ñkoñ abod ke usuuk-usuuk e-ekenieñeke mme ufọk e-ekebaaha nte abio. <verse eid="EZK 40:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 40:3" />Anye amamben miin akaa do, ami mmaanyʌñ ñkekịt awodeen keed a-akebitte brọns. Anye akeda ke mben inuaatob ye udʌk linen ye ukwak udomoñkpọ ke ubọk amọ. <verse eid="EZK 40:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 40:4" />Awo ado amambo miin, “Ayịn awo, nekke se nyʌñ nekke kop ke utọñ nyʌñ nekke nọ ñkpañutọñ ke afịd se ami ñyem uwọt fiin, sia ntak ado anam nọ uben fiin edi mmi. Tañ afịd se afo akịt nọ nditọ Isrel.”<verse eid="EZK 40:4" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Inuaatob Usakkautịn awuọhọ Anwaesiin Akwere</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 40:5" />Ami mmaakịt ndibene naña akanna ñkanñkʌk tembịd akʌk afịd-afịd. Unyọọñ ukwak udomoñkpọ ke ubọk awo ado akedo anyan kubid itiokeed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 11 me ñkpọ nte mita 3.2; se ñko ke Esi 40:12.</char></note>, ammọ keedekeed ekedo kubid keed ye udomoubọk keed. Anye amaadomo ndibene ado; anye akedo ukwak udomoñkpọ keed ke ubara ye keed ke unyọọñ.<verse eid="EZK 40:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 40:6" />Akem anye amaadika inuaatob usakkautịn. Anye amaadọọk mme utọukod amọ akedomo nsañandʌk inuaatob; anye ado aketəño ukwak keed. <verse eid="EZK 40:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 40:7" />Udomo ntoñwuọ mbon ukpeme akedo ukwak keed ke unyọọñ ye ukwak keed ke ubom, ñko mme ndibene esịneke ke ufọọd ntoñwuọ ekedo kubid ition<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 8 3/4 me ñkpọ nte mita 2.7; se ñko ke Esi 40:48 </char></note> ke udob. Udomo nsañandʌk inuaatob a-asakkaiso ase esa tembịd akedo ukwak keed.<verse eid="EZK 40:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 40:8" />Ndin anye amaadomo esa usʌñ inuaatob ñko; <verse eid="EZK 40:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 40:9" />anye akedo kubid itiaita<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 14 me ñkpọ nte mita 4.2.</char></note> ke utəño; mme adaaha amọ ekedo kubid iba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 3 1/2 me ñkpọ nte mita keed.</char></note> ke ubom. Adaaha inuaatob ado akekanna iso ase tembịd.<verse eid="EZK 40:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 40:10" />Ke esịd inuaatob ñkañ usakkautịn ubeed ita emaeba ke mbeñ keedekeed; afịd ita ado ekenieñe ukem udomo, ñko iso ndibene nsakiso ammọ ekenieñe ukem udomo. <verse eid="EZK 40:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 40:11" />Ndin anye amaadomo ubom ntondʌk inuaatob; anye akedo kubid duob, ñko unyọọñ amọ akedo kubid duob mme ita<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 18 ke ukpa ye ikpad 23 ke unyọọñ me ñkpọ nte mita 5.3 ke ukpa ye mita 6.9 ke unyọọñ.</char></note>. <verse eid="EZK 40:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 40:12" />Ke iso ubeed keedekeed ndibene a-akebaaha akedo ibio udomo keed ke unyọọñ. Mme ubeed ekedoñño udomo kubid itiokeed ke naña mbañ inaañ. <verse eid="EZK 40:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 40:13" />Ndin anye amaadomo inuaatob tọọñọ ke akọm ndibene keed tutu asịm akọm ndibene anye a-asakkaiso ase anye. Ufañ ammọ akedo kubid edịb mme ition<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 44 me ñkpọ nte mita 13; se ñko ke Esi 40:21, 25, 29, 30, 33 ye 36.</char></note> tọọñọ ke itene keed tutu asịm nsakiso amọ. <verse eid="EZK 40:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 40:14" />Anye amaadomo adaaha iso ndibene ke afịd esịd inuaatob, udomo kubid ata<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 105 me ñkpọ nte mita 32.</char></note>. Udomo ami amaakesịm adaaha a-asakkaiso ase akwere. <verse eid="EZK 40:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 40:15" />Ndin tọọñọ ke ntondʌk inuaatob tutu akesịm akpatre esa akedo udomo kubid aba mme duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 88 me ñkpọ nte mita 27; se ñko ke Esi 40:21, 25, 29, 33 ye 36.</char></note>. <verse eid="EZK 40:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 40:16" />Mme esa ye mme ndibene ke esịd emaenie ntək ndudu ekanna kpa nte adaaha; mme ndudu ami ekewọt esịd. Emaetọ mme ayob ke iso mme ñwuọnda ndibene adinam anye ayaiya.<verse eid="EZK 40:16" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Esiin Esa Abọọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 40:17" />Ndin anye amamben miin akaa esiin esa abọọñ. Do ami mmaakịt mme ubeed ye esa e-emaekekọọk afịd ikanna; ubeed edịb mme duob ekeba ke esa ado. <verse eid="EZK 40:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 40:18" />Esa ami amaadiañña ye mben inuaatob, ndin ubom ammọ akeba nte unyọọñ ammọ; ami akedo ntịkke esa. <verse eid="EZK 40:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 40:19" />Ndin anye amaadomo unyọọñ tọọñọ ke esịd idak inuaatob tutu akewuọ esịd esa abọọñ; anye akedo udomo kubid ikie<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 175 me ñkpọ nte mita 53; se ñko ke Esi 40:23, 27 ye 47</char></note> ke edem usakkautịn; ukem ado ñko ke adoro.<verse eid="EZK 40:19" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Inuaatob Adoro</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 40:20" />Ndin anye amaadomo ubom ye unyọọñ inuaatob ake adoro e-esañake ewuọ esiin esa abọọñ. <verse eid="EZK 40:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 40:21" />Ndin mme ubeed ammọ, ekedoñño ita ke naña edem iba, mme ndibene ye mme adaaha ammọ ekenie ukem udomo ye akpa inuaatob. Anye akedo udomo kubid aba mme duob ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid edịb mme ition ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 40:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 40:22" />Mme usʌñ amọ, mme esa amọ ye mme ayob se eketọ ekama edemme uyai amọ ekenie ukem udomo ye inuaatob a-aseeghe usakkautịn. Mme utọukod itiaba ekeben awo ekaa do, ye mme adaaha amọ a-asakkaiso ase ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 40:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 40:23" />Amaaba inuaatob ke esịd akwere akesakkaiso ase inuaatob adoro, kpa naña akeba ke usakkautịn. Anye amaadomo tọọñọ ke inuaatob keed akesịm inuaatob ñkañ iso amọ; anye akedo udomo ikie.<verse eid="EZK 40:23" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Inuaatob Usuuk</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 40:24" />Ndin anye amamben miin akaa usuuk ndin ami mmaanyʌñ ñkịt inuaatob usuuk. Anye amaadomo mme adaaha ye esa amọ, ñko ammọ ekenie ukem udomo nte mbon mfen. <verse eid="EZK 40:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 40:25" />Mme usʌñ inuaatob ye mme esa amọ ekenieñe mfafaha usʌñ ekanna, kpa nte naña mbon mfen ekeba. Akedo udomo kubid aba mme duob ke ubom ye edịb mme ition ke unyọọñ. <verse eid="EZK 40:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 40:26" />Udọọkñkpọ itiaba ekedat awo eka do, esa amọ anyʌñ asak iso ase ammọ. Ke edem ñkañ iba emaetọ mme ayob enam mme ndibene amọ eyaiya. <verse eid="EZK 40:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 40:27" />Esịd esa abọọñ amaanyʌñ anie inuaatob a-awọttọ usuuk, ñko anye amaadomo tọọñọ ke inuaatob anyem tutu ke inuaatob usuuk; anye ado udomo kubid ikie.<verse eid="EZK 40:27" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Mme Inuaatob e-Ekaaha Esịd Esaabọọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 40:28" />Ndin anye amamben miin akanna adi esịd esa abọọñ ato inuaatob usuuk, ñko anye amaadomo inuaatob usuuk; anye akenie ukem udomo ye mbon ako. <verse eid="EZK 40:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 40:29" />Mme ubeed amọ, mme ndibene ye mme esa amọ emaenieñe ukem udomo ye mme mbon mfen. Inuaatob ye esa amọ emaenieñe mme ufañ ekanna. Anye akedo udomo kubid aba mme duob ke unyọọñ ye edịb mme duob ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 40:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 40:30" />(Mme esa usʌñ inuaatob e-ekannake esịd esa abọọñ ekedo udomo kubid edịb mme ition ke ubom anyʌñ atəño ke udomo kubid ition.) <verse eid="EZK 40:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 40:31" />Esa amọ akewọt esiin; mme ayob emaenam mme ñkanna amọ ayaiya, ñko udodukod itiaita ke ekedat esaña edọọk.<verse eid="EZK 40:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 40:32" />Ndin anye amamben miin akaa esịd esa abọọñ ke edem usakkautịn, ndin amaadomo inuaatob amọ; anye akenie ukem udomo ye mbon ako. <verse eid="EZK 40:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 40:33" />Mme ubeed amọ, mme ndibene amọ ye mme esa amọ ekenieñe ukem udomo ye mbon ako. Mme usʌñ amọ ye mme ubeed amọ emaenieñe ufañ ekanna. Anye akedo udomo kubid aba mme duob ke unyọọñ ye kubid edịb mme ition ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 40:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 40:34" />Esa amọ akewọt esiin esa abọọñ; emaetọ ayob adinam mme ñkanñkʌk amọ ayaiya ke mbeñ edem iba, ñko utọukod itiaita ke ekesaña edọọk.<verse eid="EZK 40:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 40:35" />Ndin anye amamben miin akaa inuaatob adoro anyʌñ akedomo anye. Anye akenie ukem udomo ye mbon ako, <verse eid="EZK 40:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 40:36" />kpa naña ubeed amọ, mme adaaha ye mme esa ekedo, ñko anye amaanie ubenafịm akanna akʌk. Anye akedo udomo kubid aba mme duob ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid edịb mme ition ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 40:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 40:37" />Esa amọ akewọt esiin esa abọọñ; mme ayob emaeba adinam ñkanñkʌk amọ ayaiya ke mbeñ edem iba, ñko utọukod itiaita ke ekesaña edọọk.<verse eid="EZK 40:37" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Mme Ubeed Ubeeñe Ñkpọuwa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 40:38" />Ubeed amaaba ke mben usʌñ ke ñkpere adaaha ke esịd usʌñ inuaatob keedekeed, ke itie e-ekesiyette ufọfọb uwa. <verse eid="EZK 40:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 40:39" />Ndin akpokoro iba emaeba ke ñkañ iba esa ñkañ usʌñ inuaatob, e-ekesidatta ewot ufọfọb uwa, uwa idiọọkñkpọ ye uwa ndudue. <verse eid="EZK 40:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 40:40" />Ke ñkpere ndibene esiin usʌñ inuaatob, ñkpere mme utọukod ntondʌk e-esañake edʌk usʌñ inuaatob adoro, akpokoro iba emaeba, ñko ke edem utọukod uko akpokoro iba emaenyʌñ eba. <verse eid="EZK 40:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 40:41" />Ke ntoro akpokoro inaañ ekeba ke mbeñ usʌñ inuaatob keed, akpokoro inaañ enyʌñ eba ke mbeñ uko, afịd akedo akpokoro itiaita se ekesikama ewot ñkpọ uwa. <verse eid="EZK 40:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 40:42" />Ñko akpokoro inaañ e-ekekamake adisọi itiad enam emaeba se ekesikama enam ufọfọb uwa, ammọ keedekeed ekedo udomo kubid keed mme ibio ke anyan, kubid keed mme ibio ke ubom ye kubid keed ke ukoñ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 2 2/3 ke unyọọñ ye ukpa ye ikpad 21 ke ukoñ me ñkpọ nte sentimita 80 ke unyọọñ ye ke ukpa ye sentimita 53 ke ukoñ</char></note>. Do ke ekesidot mme ñkpọ e-ekamake ewot unam ufọfọb uwa ye mme uwa mfen. <verse eid="EZK 40:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 40:43" />Ñko ayịre-iba ukwak, a-mbeñ keedekeed akedooho ekpaubọk keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte sentimita 9</char></note> ke unyọọñ ke ekeyịt ke mme ndibene ekanna. Mme akpokoro ado ekedo se edot abʌkunam e-ekesikamake enam uwa.<verse eid="EZK 40:43" /></para>
  <para style="s2">Ubeed mme Aku</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 40:44" />Ke esiin esịd inuaatob, ke ufọọd esịd esa abọọñ, ubeed iba emaeba, keed ke ubeñ inuaatob adoro a-akekannake iso awọt usuuk, mfen ke inuaatob usuuk a-akekannake iso awọt adoro. <verse eid="EZK 40:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 40:45" />Anye amambo miin, “Ubeed a-awọttọ usuuk ana anọ mme aku e-ekpemeke tembịd, <verse eid="EZK 40:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 40:46" />ndin ubeed a-awọttọ adoro ana anọ mme aku e-ekpemeke akpokoro uwa. Mbon ami edo nditọ ideen Sadọk, e-edoññoke ukweeñe Lifai se ikeme adisaña ñkpere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adinam utom ke iso amọ.”<verse eid="EZK 40:46" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 40:47" />Ndin anye amaadomo esa abọọñ: akedo udomo kubid ikie ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid ikie ke ubom. Ndin akpokoro uwa akeba ke iso tembịd.<verse eid="EZK 40:47" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ufa Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 40:48" />Anye amamben miin akaa esa tembịd anyʌñ akedomo mme adaaha esa ado; ammọ ekedoñño udomo kubid ition ke naña ñkañ iba. Ukpa ntondʌk akedo udomo kubid duob mme inaañ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 25 me ñkpọ nte mita 7.4</char></note>, ñko mme ñwuọnda ndibene amọ ekedo udomo kubid ita<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 5 1/4 me ñkpọ nte mita 1.6</char></note> ke mbeñ ñkañ iba. <verse eid="EZK 40:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 40:49" />Inuaatob esa akedo udomo kubid edịb<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 35 me mita 11</char></note> ke ubom, ñko udomo kubid duob mme iba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40:49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 21 me ñkpọ nte mita 6.4</char></note> tọọñọ ke iso sịm edem. Ekesisaña mme utọukod edʌk, ndin mme abai itiad e-ekemʌmmọ ufọk ekama emaeba ke naña edem amọ iba.<verse eid="EZK 40:49" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 40" />
  <chapter number="41" style="c" sid="EZK 41" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 41:1" />Ndin awo ado amamben miin akaa ufọọd ufọk anyʌñ akedomo mme adaaha amọ; ubom adaaha akedo udomo kubid itiokeed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 11 me ñkpọ nte mita 3.2; se ñko ke Esi 41:3, 5 ye 8.</char></note> ke ubeñ keedekeed. <verse eid="EZK 41:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 41:2" />Inuausʌñ amọ akedo udomo kubid duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 18 me ñkpọ nte mita 5.3</char></note> ke ubom, ndin mme ufañ ndibene ke edem ñkañ iba ekedoñño udomo kubid ition<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 8 3/4 me ñkpọ nte mita 2.7; se ñko ke Esi 41:9, 11 ye 12</char></note> ke ubom. Anye amaanyʌñ adomo ufọọdufọk; anye akedo udomo kubid aba ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid edịb ke ukpa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 70 ke unyọọñ ye ikpad 35 ke ukpa me ñkpọ nte mita 21 ke unyọọñ ye mita 11 ke ukpa</char></note>.<verse eid="EZK 41:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 41:3" />Ndin anye amaaboiyo adʌk ataa esịd adisana itie anyʌñ akedomo adaaha anyenusʌñ; ammọ keedekeed eketara kubid iba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 3 1/2 me ñkpọ nte mita 1.1; se ñko ke Esi41:22</char></note> ke ubom. Inuausʌñ ado aketara kubid itiokeed, ñko ufañ ndibene amọ ke mbeñ keedekeed ekedo udomo kubid itiaba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 12 me ñkpọ nte mita 3.7</char></note> ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 41:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 41:4" />Ñko anye amaadomo unyọọñ esịd adisana ubeed ado; anye akedo udomo kubid edịb to ke utịd ufọọdufọk. Ndin anye amambo miin, “Ami ado Nsana Ñkan Itie.”<verse eid="EZK 41:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 41:5" />Ndin anye amaadomo ndibene tembịd; anye akedo udomo kubid itiokeed ke udob, ñko ndian-ndian ubeed keedekeed a-akebaaha akanna tembịd akedo udomo kubid inaañ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 7 me ñkpọ nte mita 2.1</char></note> ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 41:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 41:6" />Mme ndian-ndian ubeed e-ekebaaha ke ñkañ ekedo ke ikpeghe ita, keed ke anyọñ mfen, edịb mme duob ke ikpeghe keedekeed. Mme mboi emaebañña ke mme ndibene tembịd nọ ato do emʌm mme ndian-ndian ubeed ñkañ ado ekama, nọ mme mboi ami ekuudʌk esịd ndibene tembịd. <verse eid="EZK 41:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 41:7" />Mme ndian-ndian ubeed afịd ñkañ e-ekannake tembịd ekʌk emaetara ke ikpeghe keedekeed. Ekebọp mme ufọk e-edaaha ekanna tembịd nọ edọdọọk ke ndaha ke ndaha, nọ ato do mme ubeed etara naña awo adọọk akaa. Udodukod amaaba tọọñọ ke isọñ akesịm ubeed ufọọd tutu akewuọ ubeed anyọñ.<verse eid="EZK 41:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 41:8" />Ami mmaakịt ke tembịd amanie esa a-akedịppeke ke afịd ñkanñkʌk amọ, a-akebaaha nte itiad idakisọñ anọ mme ubeed mben ado. Anye akedo nte anyan ukwak, anyọọñ udomo kubid itiokeed. <verse eid="EZK 41:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 41:9" />Ndibene esiin ye mme ubeed e-ekebaaha ke mben ekedo udomo kubid ition ke udob. Ufañ a-akebaaha ke ufọọd ubeed mben tembịd <verse eid="EZK 41:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 41:10" />ye ubeed mme aku akedo udomo kubid edịb ke ubom afịd se ikikanna tembịd ikʌk. <verse eid="EZK 41:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 41:11" />Mme usʌñ emaeba se eto mme ufañ e-ekebaaha do esaña edʌk mme ndian-ndian ubeed, keed ke adoro, mfen ke usuuk; ñko itiad idakisọñ e-ekedaaha eduseere anwa akedo udomo kubid ition akanna afịd ubom.<verse eid="EZK 41:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 41:12" />Ufọk a-akedaaha asak iso ase akwere tembịd ke edem usobutịn akedo udomo kubid ata mme duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 123 me ñkpọ nte mita 37</char></note> ke ubom. Ndibene ufọk ami akedo udomo kubid ition ke udob ke afịd ñkanna amọ, ñko unyọọñ amọ akedo udomo kubid anaañ mme duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 158 me ñkpọ nte mita 48</char></note>.<verse eid="EZK 41:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 41:13" />Ndin anye amaadomo tembịd; anye akedo udomo kubid ikie<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 175 me ñkpọ nte mita 53; se ñko ke Esi 41:14 ye 15</char></note> ke unyọọñ, ñko akwere tembịd ye mme ufọk mfen ye mme ndibene ammọ ekedo udomo kubid ikie ke unyọọñ. <verse eid="EZK 41:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 41:14" />Ubom akwere tembịd ke edem usakkautịn, dian ye iso tembịd, akedo udomo kubid ikie.<verse eid="EZK 41:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 41:15" />Ndin anye amaadomo unyọọñ ufọk a-akedaaha asakiso ase akwere ke edem tembịd, dian ye mme itie ubonoñkpọ ke mbeñ iba; anye akedo udomo kubid ikie.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 41:15">Akpan ufọọd ufọk, esịd nsasana itie ye esa a-aseeghe esa abọọñ, <verse eid="EZK 41:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 41:16" />ye mme nsañandʌk ye mme mfafaha ubenafịm ye itie ubonoñkpọ ke ñkanna ammọ naña ita, afịd ñkpọ tọọñọ ke isọñ ñko dian ye nsañandʌk ekefʌk ke eto. Emaenyʌñ efʌk isọñ, ndibene tutu asịm ubenafịm, ñko emaefʌk mme ubenafịm ado. <verse eid="EZK 41:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 41:17" />Tọọñọ ke ufañ a-akebaaha ke anyọñ esiin ntondʌk esịd adisana itie ye ke mme ndibene ñkanñkʌk esịd adisana itie <verse eid="EZK 41:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 41:18" />mme adisọi serubim ye eto ayob emaeba. Eto ayob keed akesịne ke ufọọd serubim. Serub keedekeed ekenie iso iba: <verse eid="EZK 41:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 41:19" />iso awo akese eto ayob ke ubọk ñkañ keed, iso ekpe anyʌñ ase ubọk ñkañ uko. Emaesọi ammọ edọñ ekanna afịd tembịd. <verse eid="EZK 41:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 41:20" />Tọọñọ ke isọñufọk tutu asịm ubeñ ñkpere ntondʌk, emaesọi serubim ye eto ayob ke ndibene akpan ufọọdufọk.<verse eid="EZK 41:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 41:21" />Akpan ufọọdufọk akenie anyan mbañinaañ abaiudọk, ñko anye a-akebaaha ke iso Ñkoññkan Adisana Itie akedo ukem-ukem. <verse eid="EZK 41:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 41:22" />Ndin amaaba akpokoro uwa e-ekenamma ke eto a-akedooho udomo kubid ita ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid iba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41:22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 5 1/4 me ñkpọ nte mita 1.5</char></note> ke naña mbañinaañ; ekenam mme mben amọ, idak amọ ye mme ñkañ amọ ke adukpọk. Awo ado amambo miin, “Ami ado akpokoro a-anaaha ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.” <verse eid="EZK 41:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 41:23" />Akpan ufọọdufọk ye Nsana Ñkan Itie ekenieñe usʌñ iba-iba. <verse eid="EZK 41:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 41:24" />Kwa usʌñ akenie itịm iba, itịm iba enyʌñ eyịre ke usʌñ keedekeed. <verse eid="EZK 41:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 41:25" />Ndin ke mme udọk akpan ufọọdufọk emaesọi serubim ye eto ayob edian ukem nte mbon se ekedian ke mme ndibene, ndin ñko ntọntekke ñkpọ e-enamma ke adukpọk amaaba ke iso esa ado. <verse eid="EZK 41:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 41:26" />Mme mfafaha ubenafịm emaebañña ke mme ndibene iso esa ado e-ekenieñeke usọsọi eto ayob ke ñkañ keedekeed. Mme ubeed edemesa tembịd emaenyʌñ enie ndoppo abọbọọk usʌñ.<verse eid="EZK 41:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 41" />
  <chapter number="42" style="c" sid="EZK 42" />
  <para style="s1">Mme Ubeed a-Anaaha anọ mme Aku</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 42:1" />Ndin ete ado amamben miin akaa adoro akedʌk ke esa abọọñ anyʌñ amben miin akedʌk ubeed a-akesakkaiso ase ufọkesa tembịd ye ndibene esiin ke adoro. <verse eid="EZK 42:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 42:2" />Ufọk anye u-usʌñ amọ akeseeghe ukañ adoro akedo udomo kubid ikie<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 175 ke unyọọñ ye ikpad 88 ke ukpa me ñkpọ nte mita 53 ke unyọọñ ye mita 27 ke ukpa</char></note> ke unyọọñ ye aba mme duob ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 42:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 42:3" />Naña iba ke ubeñ udomo kubid edịb<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 35 me ñkpọ nte mita 11</char></note> tọọñọ ke esịd esa abọọñ ye ke ubeñ a-akesakkaiso ase esa esiin esa abọọñ, ubeed ubonoñkpọ amaase mme ubeed mfen ke ndaha ita. <verse eid="EZK 42:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 42:4" />Ufañ se awo asaña amaaba ke iso mme ubeed ado, atiara udomo kubid duob anyʌñ anyọọñ udomo kubid ikie<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42:4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 18 ke ukpa ye ikpad 175 ke unyọọñ me ñkpọ nte mita 5.3 ke ukpa ye mita 53 ke unyọọñ</char></note>. Mme usʌñ ammọ ekeba ke adoro. <verse eid="EZK 42:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 42:5" />Ndin mme ubeed anyọñ ekedo mfaha-mfaha, sia mme ubeed ubonoñkpọ emaedat uwak ufañ ato ammọ akan mme ubeed ke isọñ ye ke ufọọd. <verse eid="EZK 42:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 42:6" />Mme ubeed anyọñ ikinieñeke adaaha naña mme esa abọọñ ekenie; ke ntoro ammọ emaesiip ke ufañ isọñ ekan mbon idak ye ufọọd itie. <verse eid="EZK 42:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 42:7" />Ndin amaaba ndibene akesakkaiso ase esa abọọñ anwa esiin; anye amaatara adʌk iso mme ubeed ke udomo kubid aba mme duob. <verse eid="EZK 42:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 42:8" />Ke ini mme ubeed e-ekedianake ke ubeñ a-adaaha adiana anwaesiin esa abọọñ ekedooho udomo kubid aba mme duob ke unyọọñ, mme ubeed ñkañ akekpereke adisana itie ekedoñño udomo ikie ke unyọọñ. <verse eid="EZK 42:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 42:9" />Mme ubeed isọñ ufọk ado emaenie inuausʌñ ke edem usakkautịn naña awo atooho anwaesiin esa abọọñ adʌk ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 42:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 42:10" />Ke ñkañ usuuk ke utịd anyan ndibene anwaesiin esa abọọñ, a-awuọhọ atịkke tembịd esa abọọñ ye nsakiso ndibene esiin, mme ubeed emaebañña <verse eid="EZK 42:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 42:11" />ye inuausʌñ ke iso ammọ. Mbon ami ekeba nte ubeed e-ebaaha ke adoro; ammọ ekenie ukem unyọọñ ye ukem ubom, edubitte ke ntoñwuọ ye ke mme udomo. Mme inuausʌñ ubeed ke usuuk edubitte inuausʌñ ke adoro <verse eid="EZK 42:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 42:12" />inuausʌñ amaaba ke ntondʌk a-akedooho nsakiso ndibene akenyannake aka usakkautịn, a-mme awo ekesisañake edʌk mme ubeed ado.<verse eid="EZK 42:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 42:13" />Ndin anye amambo miin, “Mme ubeed edem adoro ye edem usuuk ekannake iso ese akwere tembịd edo ubeed mme aku, ubeed a-mme aku e-enamma utom <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ediidia mme adisana uwa. Do ke ammọ ediisịn mme nsana ñkan uwa, uwa ñkpasi, uwa idiọọkñkpọ ye uwa ndudue, sia itie ado asana. <verse eid="EZK 42:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 42:14" />Mme aku emaedọdʌk ñkañ ataa adisana itie, inaaha ammọ ewuọ eka anwaesiin esa abọọñ ibọhọke ammọ esịññe ewịra a-ammọ ekesịneke enam utom enịm, sia mme ewịra ado edo adisana. Ammọ enie adisịne afọñ mfen mbemiso ammọ esaña ekpere mme itie a-anaaha anọ atu awo.”<verse eid="EZK 42:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 42:15" />Ke ini anye amaakedomo se ikidọñọ ke ñkañ tembịd ima, anye amandat miin usʌñ ato usakkautịn awuọ anyʌñ akedomo mme itie se ikiba ikanna: <verse eid="EZK 42:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 42:16" />Anye amaadomo ukañ usakkautịn ke ukwak udomoñkpọ, anye ado udomo kubid ikie ition<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Kubid 500 ado ñkpọ nte ikpad 875 me ñkpọ nte mita 265; se ñko ke Esi 42:17, 18 ye 19</char></note>. <verse eid="EZK 42:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 42:17" />Anye amaadomo ukañ adoro, anye akedo udomo ikie ition ke eto udomo ñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 42:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 42:18" />Anye amaakanna akedomo edem usuuk; anye ado udomo ikie ition ke eto udomo ñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 42:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 42:19" />Ndin anye amaakedomo ukañ usobutịn; anye akedo udomo kubid ikie ition ke eto udomo ñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 42:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 42:20" />Ke ntoro anye amaadomo ukpa afịd mbeñ inaañ. Anye amaanie ndibene akanna, a-akedooho udomo kubid ikie ition ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid ikie ition ke ubom, adidiañña se isana ñkpọñ mme ñkaña ñkpọ.<verse eid="EZK 42:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 42" />
  <chapter number="43" style="c" sid="EZK 43" />
  <para style="s1">Ubọọñ Abasi Atịmme Anyọñ Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 43:1" />Ndin awo ado amamben miin akaa inuaatob a-awọttọ usakkautịn, <verse eid="EZK 43:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 43:2" />ndin ami mmaakịt ubọọñ Abasi Isrel naña ato usakkautịn adi. Uyio amọ akeba nte uyio uwak mmọọñ e-efegheke, ndin isọñ amaayọhọ ye ubọọñ amọ. <verse eid="EZK 43:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 43:3" />Ñkukịd se ami ñkekịt akeba nte ñkukịd a-ami ñkekịtte ke ini anye akediighe adisobo abio anyʌñ abit mme ñkukịd a-ami ñkekịtte ke mben inyañ Keba, ndin ami mmaaduọ ñkʌp iso ke isọñ. <verse eid="EZK 43:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 43:4" />Ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaato inuaatob a-awọttọ usakkautịn adʌk tembịd. <verse eid="EZK 43:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 43:5" />Ndin Sịbidịd ado amandịppe miin ke anyọñ anyʌñ amben miin adʌk adi esịd esa abọọñ, ndin Ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayọhọ tembịd.<verse eid="EZK 43:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 43:6" />Idaha e-ete ado akesʌkkọ ada ke ñkañ mmi, ami mmaakop naña awo atañ ikọ ye ami ato esịd tembịd. <verse eid="EZK 43:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 43:7" />Anye akebo: “Ayịn awo, itie ebekpo mmi ye itie se ukod mmi adoro ado ami. Itie ami ke ami ndiidʌñ ye nditọ Isrel ke nsi-nsi. Tutu amama nditọ Isrel ye mme ndidem ammọ idiisịnne anyịñ mmi ke ndek aba ke usaña akpara ammọ ye se enọ ke itie ñkpa mme mbọọñ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 43:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 43:8" />Ke ini ammọ enịmme nsañandọọk ammọ ediana nsañandọọk mmi ye mme inuausʌñ ammọ ediana mme inuausʌñ mmi, a-adooho ndibene ikpọọñ andiañña miin akpọñ ammọ, ammọ emaesappa adisana anyịñ mmi ye mbubiam adinam ammọ. Ke ntoro ami mmaasobo ammọ ke iyadesịd mmi. <verse eid="EZK 43:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 43:9" />Idahami ndin yak ammọ esioñño idem ekpọñ usaña akpara ye uwa itie ñkpa ndidem ammọ, ndin ami ñyaadʌñ ye ammọ ke nsi-nsi.<verse eid="EZK 43:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 43:10" />“Ayịn awo, dọkkọ nditọ Isrel naña tembịd ado aba, nọ ato do abuud amʌm ammọ ke ntak ndiọiñkpọ ammọ. Yak ammọ ese naña anen, <verse eid="EZK 43:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 43:11" />ñko adieke ammọ ekoppo abuud ebaña afịd se ammọ enam, wọt ammọ naña tembịd ami aba, naña ebono ñkpọ, mme ntoñwuọ ye mme ntondʌk amọ, naña ediọñ anye ye afịd ewʌhọ ye mbed amọ. Wet mme ñkpọ ami nịm ammọ ke iso nọ ato do ammọ esaña nnen-nnen ke naña ediọñ anye enyʌñ ekeene mme ewʌhọ amọ.”<verse eid="EZK 43:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 43:12" />“Ami ado mbed tembịd: Afịd ñkanñkʌk anyọñ abod adiido se isana ikan. Mbed tembịd aba ntoro.<verse eid="EZK 43:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Emaana Ediọñ Ekamba Akpokoro Uwa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 43:13" />“Mme udomo akpokoro uwa ke udomo anyan kubid<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte sentimita 53; se ñko ke Esi 43:14 ye 17. Anyan kubid ado udomo e-ekamake ke afịd Esikeel 40-48. </char></note> edo ami, anyan kubid ado ado kubid keed ye ufuudubọk keed: Usaña mmọọñ amọ atəño kubid keed anyʌñ anwaña kubid keed, ye mben a-adooho ukpa keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte sentimita 27.</char></note> akanna mme utịd. Ñko unyọọñ akpokoro uwa ado ami: <verse eid="EZK 43:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 43:14" />Tọọñọ ke usiak isọñ a-abaaha ke isọñ sịm usuuhọ ufañ unyọọñ a-abaaha akanna akpokoro uwa akoñ ke udomo kubid iba, ñko ufañ amọ ado udomo kubid keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 3 1/2 ke ukoñ ye ikpad 1 3/4 ke ukpa me ñkpọ nte sentimita 105 ke ukoñ ye sentimita 53 ke ukpa</char></note> ke ukpa. Tọọñọ ke usuuhọ ufañ ami tutu asịm ufañ anyọñ a-akannake akpokoro uwa akʌk ado udomo kubid inaañ ke unyọọñ, ufañ ado ñko anyʌñ ado udomo kubid keed ke ukpa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 7 ke ukoñ ye ikpad 1 3/4 ke ukpa me ñkpọ nte mita 2.1 ke ukoñ ye sentimita 53 ke ukpa</char></note>. <verse eid="EZK 43:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 43:15" />Ke emaaha ado, ebʌkikañ akpokoro uwa ado udomo kubid inaañ ke unyọọñ, ñko nnʌk inaañ e-enyanna eto anyọñ ebʌkikañ ado ewuọ. <verse eid="EZK 43:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 43:16" />Itiad ebʌkikañ akpokoro uwa ado anie ukem mbañ inaañ, ado udomo kubid duob mme iba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 21 me ñkpọ nte mita 6.4</char></note> ke unyọọñ ye duob mme iba ke ubom. <verse eid="EZK 43:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 43:17" />Ufañ anyọñ ñko ado mbañ inaañ, udomo kubid duob mme inaañ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43:17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 25 me ñkpọ nte mita 7.4</char></note> ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid duob mme inaañ ke ubom. Ke afịd ñkanna akpokoro itie uwa, ufañ a-akenaaha akedo udomo kubid keed ye ibio ubaak kubid<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43:17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte sentimita 27</char></note>. Mme utọukod akpokoro uwa asak iso ase usakkautịn.”<verse eid="EZK 43:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 43:18" />Ndin anye amambo miin, “Ayịn awo, ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Mme mbed se idiikpeme naña efọp mme ufọfọb uwa ye usiime iyiib ke akpokoro uwa ke ini emaebọp anye ima ediido ami: <verse eid="EZK 43:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 43:19" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara abo ke ana afo anọ mme aku Lifai ekpək Sadọk, e-esañake ekpere iso mmi, ñyịn ayaaraenañ nte uwa idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 43:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 43:20" />Ana afo aben usʌk iyiib amọ asịn ke nnʌk inaañ e-ebaaha ke akpokoro uwa ye ke inuuk inaañ ufañ anyọñ ye ke afịd ñkanñkʌk ufañ, ke ntoro nam akpokoro uwa asana nyʌñ nam ñkpeubọk nọ anye. <verse eid="EZK 43:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 43:21" />Ana afo aben ayaaraenañ uwa idiọọkñkpọ akefọp anye ke itie e-esioho enịm ke tembịd ke esiin adisana itie.<verse eid="EZK 43:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 43:22" />“Ke ayọhọ usen iba, ana afo awa akpo ebod i-imiinieghe ndo nte uwa idiọọkñkpọ, ñko ana enam akpokoro uwa asana kpa naña ekekama ayaaraenañ enam anye asana. <verse eid="EZK 43:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 43:23" />Ke ini afo umaukweeñe adinam anye asana, ana afo awa ñyịn ayaaraenañ ye akukịmedọñ a-atooho udịmedọñ, naña iba inaaha enie ndo. <verse eid="EZK 43:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 43:24" />Ana afo awa ammọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ñko ana mme aku esiime inʌñ ke anyọñ ammọ enyʌñ ewa ammọ nte ufọfọb uwa enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="EZK 43:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 43:25" />“Afo anie adinọ akpo ebod kwa usen ke usen itiaba nte uwa idiọọkñkpọ; ñko afo anie adinọ ñyịn ayaaraenañ ye akukịmedọñ a-atooho udịmedọñ, naña iba inaaha enie ndo. <verse eid="EZK 43:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 43:26" />Ammọ ana enam ñkpeubọk enọ akpokoro uwa enyʌñ enam anye asana ke usen itiaba; ntoro ke ammọ ediidiọñ anye. <verse eid="EZK 43:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 43:27" />Ke utịd mme usen ami, tọọñọ ke ayọhọ usen itiaita kaa iso, mme aku ana eben mme ufọfọb uwa ye uwa adidiana keed ndufo enọ ke akpokoro uwa. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ; ndin ami ñyaanem esịd ye ndufo.”<verse eid="EZK 43:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 43" />
  <chapter number="44" style="c" sid="EZK 44" />
  <para style="s1">Emaana Edịppe Ndaha Aku</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 44:1" />Ndin awo ado amamben miin atịmme akaa inuaatob esiin adisana itie, ndin emaebet inuaatob a-akeseeghe usakkautịn. <verse eid="EZK 44:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 44:2" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amambo miin, “Ana nte inuaatob ami abebere afịd-afịd ini. Inaaha ebeere anye; inaaha awo ndomokeed asaña ke anye adʌk. Ana nte anye abebere sia adooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Abasi Isrel, amaasaña aboiyo ke anye adʌk. <verse eid="EZK 44:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 44:3" />Akpan abọọñ ke idem amọ ikpọọñ akeme aditie ke esịd inuaatob ndia ñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Anye ayaato ke usʌñ esa inuaatob adʌk anyʌñ asaña ukem usʌñ ado awuọ.”<verse eid="EZK 44:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 44:4" />Akem awo ado amamben miin ato usʌñ inuaatob adoro adiwuọ iso tembịd. Ami mmaase ñnyʌñ ñkịt ubọọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> naña ayọhọ tembịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin ami mmaaduọ ñkʌp iso ke isọñ.<verse eid="EZK 44:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 44:5" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amambo miin, “Ayịn awo, tịm se, nekke kpañ utọñ nyʌñ nịm esịd mfo nọ afịd mbed ye item a-ami unọọhọ fiin mbaña tembịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Tịñ anyen ke ntondʌk tembịd ye afịd mme inuausʌñ se esaña ewuọ ke adisana itie. <verse eid="EZK 44:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 44:6" />Dọkkọ Isrel mbon ntịdutọñ bo ke ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: ‘Nditọ Isrel, yak mbubiam adinam ndufo atre!’ <verse eid="EZK 44:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 44:7" />Ke adidian ye afịd mme mbubiam adinam mfen a-ndufo enaññake, ndufo emeben mme isenawo i-imiinịmme esịd ammọ asana ñko inyʌññọ ifọọrọ edʌd edʌk adisana itie mmi, e-esappa tembịd mmi ke ini ndufo ennọọhọ miin ndidia, akpọñ ye iyiib, enyʌñ ebiat edioomo mmi. <verse eid="EZK 44:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 44:8" />Utu ke ndufo enam ubiọñutom ndufo ke abaña mme ndisana ñkpọ mmi, ndufo emenam mbon mfen ese ñkpọ ebaña adisana itie mmi. <verse eid="EZK 44:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 44:9" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Inaaha asenawo ndomokeed ammiinịmme esịd amọ asana ñko inyʌññọ ifọọrọ edʌd adʌk adisana itie mmi, kpa ye mme isenawo e-edʌñọke ke atu nditọ Isrel.<verse eid="EZK 44:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 44:10" />“ ‘Mme Lifai e-ekedaañake eñkpọñ miin ekaa anyan usʌñ ke ini Isrel ekeyooño ekpọñ usʌñ, e-ekenyʌññọ eyooñ eñkpọñ miin ebịne mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ ana ebọ ufen idiọọkñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 44:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 44:11" />Ammọ ekeme adinam utom ke adisana itie mmi, enam utom adikpeme inuaatob tembịd enyʌñ enam ñkpọ do; ammọ ekeme adiwot mme ufọfọb uwa enyʌñ ewa uwa enọ mbon awo enyʌñ eda ke iso mbon awo enam ñkpọ enọ ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 44:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 44:12" />Ado sia ammọ ekenamma ñkpọ enọ ammọ ke iso mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ enyʌñ enam nditọ Isrel eduọ edʌk idiọọkñkpọ, ami mmebenne ubọk ñnwọñọ nnọ ammọ ke ana ebọ utịb idiọọkñkpọ ammọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 44:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 44:13" />Inaaha ammọ esaña ekpere edinam ñkpọ ennọ miin nte mme aku me adisaña ñkpere ndisana ñkpọ mmi me ataa ndisana uwa mmi; ana ammọ ekop abuud ke mbubiam adinam ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 44:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 44:14" />Ndin ami ñyaamek ammọ nọ ekpeme tembịd ke afịd utom se ediinam ke esịd amọ.<verse eid="EZK 44:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 44:15" />“ ‘Ado mme aku Lifai, e-edooho ubon Sadọk e-ekenyʌññọ ekpeme adisana itie mmi ke ini nditọ Isrel ekeyooño eñkpọñ miin, edo se isaña iñkpere miin idinam ñkpọ ke iso mmi; ammọ ana nte eda ke iso mmi enam uwa akpọñ ye iyiib, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 44:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 44:16" />Ammọ ikpọọñ edo se idʌk adisana itie mmi; ammọ ikpọọñ edo se isaña ikpere akpokoro mmi inam utom ke iso mmi inyʌñ iñkpeme miin.<verse eid="EZK 44:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 44:17" />“ ‘Ke ini ammọ edʌkkọ inuaatob esịd esa abọọñ, ana ammọ esịne mme afọñ linen; inaaha ammọ esịne afọñ idededọñ ndomokeed ke ini ammọ enamma utom ke inuaatob esịd esa abọọñ me ke esịd tembịd. <verse eid="EZK 44:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 44:18" />Ammọ enie ediyara mme uyadiwuod linen ke iwuod ammọ ye afọñ idakidem linen ekanna isịn ammọ. Ammọ inaaha esịne ñkpọ ndomokeed se inam ammọ etịppe ibibiak. <verse eid="EZK 44:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 44:19" />Ke ini ammọ ewuọhọ eka esiin esa abọọñ a-mme awo ebaaha, ana ammọ esịññe mme afọñidem unam utom ammọ enyʌñ eyaak enịm ke mme adisana ubeed, enyʌñ esịne mme afọñidem mfen, mbaak mme awo edisana ato ke edituaha ye ewịra ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 44:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 44:20" />“ ‘Inaaha ammọ ekwaat ided iwuod me enịm anyan ided, ado ana enịm ided iwuod ammọ ibio-ibio. <verse eid="EZK 44:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 44:21" />Inaaha aku ndomokeed anwọñ ukọd ke ini anye adʌkkọ esịd akwere. <verse eid="EZK 44:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 44:22" />Inaaha ammọ edọ mme ebekpa me ibaan emaekewuọñọ ndọ; ammọ ekeme idọ ubọikpa Isrel imiidiọọñọke awodeen me mme ebekpa mme aku. <verse eid="EZK 44:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 44:23" />Ana ammọ ekpeep mbon mmi ukpʌhọde a-abaaha ke ufọọd se ido adisana ye kwe-kwe ñkpọ enyʌñ ewọt ammọ naña ekpediọọñọ ukpʌhọde a-abaaha ke ufọọd ñkpọ se ideghe ye se isana.<verse eid="EZK 44:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 44:24" />“ ‘Ke ini utọk abaaha, ana mme aku eba nte mme abiideikpe enyʌñ ebiide ikpe ekeene ubonoñkpọ mmi. Ammọ enie edinịm mme mbed ye mme ewʌhọ mmi ke afịd mme usọrọ se ami mmek, ñko ana ammọ enịm mme Sabad mmi esana.<verse eid="EZK 44:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 44:25" />“ ‘Aku inaaha asappa idem amọ ke adida ñkpere akpo awo; ado, adieke awo ñkpa ado akedooho ete me eka amọ, ayịn amọ awodeen me ayịn awonwaan, ayịneka awodeen me ayịneka awonwaan ammiidọọhọ ebe, anye akeme adisappa idem amọ. <verse eid="EZK 44:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 44:26" />Ke anye amaakenam idem asana ama, anye ana abet usen itiaba. <verse eid="EZK 44:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 44:27" />Ke usen anye adʌkkọ esịd akwere adisana itie adikinam utom ke adisana itie, anye anie adiwa uwa idiọọkñkpọ nnọọ idem amọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 44:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 44:28" />“ ‘Ami nnie adido ukweeñe udeeme a-mme aku enieghe. Inaaha afo anọ ammọ inie ndomokeed ke Isrel; ami ndiido udeeme ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 44:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 44:29" />Ammọ ediidia uwa ñkpasi, uwa idiọọkñkpọ ye uwa ndudue; ndin afịd ñkpọ ke Isrel se ediinọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adiido ake ammọ asaña-asaña. <verse eid="EZK 44:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 44:30" />Mfọọnñkan afịd mme akpa mfịd ye afịd mme asaña-asaña enọ adiinie mme aku. Ana ndufo enọ ammọ akpa ndom abakpa ndufo nọ ato do adidiọñ aduọkkọ ke ufọk ndufo. <verse eid="EZK 44:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 44:31" />Mme aku inaaha eta ñkpọ ndomokeed, me ado inuen me unam, amaakekpa me se ndiọi unam ewot.<verse eid="EZK 44:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 44" />
  <chapter number="45" style="c" sid="EZK 45" />
  <para style="s1">Emaana Edịppe Isrel Edaaha Ayọhọ-Ayọhọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 45:1" />“ ‘Ke ini ndufo edeemeke isọñ nte udeeme, ana ndufo eyaak itie isọñ enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> nte adisana ubaak isọñ, udomo kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 8 me ñkpọ nte kilomita 13; se ñko ke Esi 45:3, 5 ye 6.</char></note> ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid tọsịn edịb (20,000) ke ukpa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 6 1/2 me ñkpọ nte kilomita 11</char></note>; afịd itie ado adiido adisana. <verse eid="EZK 45:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 45:2" />Ke atu ami, ubaak isọñ a-adooho udomo kubid ikie ition (500)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 875 me mita 265</char></note> ke naña mbañ inaañ anie adina nnọọ adisana itie, ndin udomo kubid aba mme duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 88 me ñkpọ nte mita 27.</char></note> ke ñkanna amọ ana anọ ñkaña isọñ. <verse eid="EZK 45:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 45:3" />Ndin domo udomo kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid tọsịn duob (10,000)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 3 1/3 me ñkpọ nte kilomita 5.3; se ñko ke Esi 45:5</char></note> ke ukpa sio ke adisana itie ami. Do ke adisana itie adiiba, Ataa Nsasana Itie. <verse eid="EZK 45:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 45:4" />Anye adiido adisana ubaak isọñ anọ mme aku, e-enamma ñkpọ ke adisana itie e-enyʌññọ esaña ekpere adinam ñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Anye adiido itie ufọk ammọ anyʌñ ado nsasana itie e-esiooho enịm enọ adisana itie. <verse eid="EZK 45:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 45:5" />Ubaak isọñ a-adooho udomo kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ ye kubid tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ubara adiinie mme Lifai, e-enamma utom ke tembịd, nte udeeme ammọ adibọp mme abio se edʌñọ ke esịd.<verse eid="EZK 45:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 45:6" />“ ‘Ana ndufo enọ abio isọñ a-akponno ke ukpa kubid tọsịn ition (5,000)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 1 2/3 me ñkpọ nte kilomita 2.7</char></note> ye kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ, e-ebenne ekedian ye adisana isọñ; anye ado adiinie afịd Isrel.<verse eid="EZK 45:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 45:7" />“ ‘Akpanabọọñ adiinie isọñ adiaññake adaña ye ñkañ a-anaaha anọ adisana isọñ ye anye a-anieghe abio. Anye ayaatara ke ukañ usobutịn anyʌñ atara ke usakkautịn akaa ñkañ usakkautịn, asaña ke unyọọñ tọọñọ ke adaña usobutịn tutu akewuọ usakkautịn asak iso ase keed ke atu mme udeeme ekpək. <verse eid="EZK 45:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 45:8" />Isọñ ami adiido udeeme amọ ke Isrel. Ñko nditọ ideen abọọñ mmi idiifiighe mbon mmi aba ado eyaeyaak mbon Isrel edat isọñ enie akeene mme esiin ammọ.<verse eid="EZK 45:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 45:9" />“ ‘Ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Ndufo nditọ ideen abọọñ Isrel, emenam ebọhọ adaña; a-akem ndin! Isịññe idem ikpọñ ntịme ye adifiik awo inyʌñ inam se ifọn ye se inyʌñ idot. Itre adibịn mbon mmi nsịññe ke abio, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ. <verse eid="EZK 45:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 45:10" />Ndufo ana ekama nnen-nnen udomoñkpọ, nnen-nnen udomo efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Efa akedo udomo nsaad ñkpọ a-adooho ñkpọ nte lita 22.</char></note> ye nnen-nnen udomo baad<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Baad akedo udomo mmọọñ-mmọọñ ñkpọ a-adooho ñkpọ nte lita 22.</char></note>. <verse eid="EZK 45:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 45:11" />Ana efa ye baad edo ukem ke ndaha, yak baad adọñọ mbakka udomo họma keed ke itie duob ñko efa adọñọ mbakka udomo họma keed ke itie duob; ana họma ado nsọọñọnda udomo anọ naña iba. <verse eid="EZK 45:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 45:12" />Yak sekel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Sekel akedoppo ñkpọ nte kram 12.</char></note> akem ye kera edịb. Sekel edịb dian sekel edịb mme ition dian sekel duob mme ition anọ mina keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho sekel 60; ñkaña mina akedo sekel 50. Sekel 60 akedo ñkpọ nte kram 690</char></note>.<verse eid="EZK 45:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 45:13" />“ ‘Ami ado asaña-asaña enọ a-afo anieghe adinọ: mbakka efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 2.7.</char></note> keed ke itie itiokeed a-atooho homa wiid keedekeed ye mbakka efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 2.3.</char></note> keed ke itie itiokeed a-atooho homa baali keedekeed. <verse eid="EZK 45:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 45:14" />Nnen-nnen udomo adan ọlif, e-ekamake baad edomo, ado mbakka keed ke itie duob ke udomoñkpọ baad<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte lita 2.2.</char></note> e-edomoke eto kọọ keedekeed (a-asịneke baad duob me họma keed, sia baad duob ado ukem ye họma keed). <verse eid="EZK 45:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 45:15" />Ñko ana esio edọñ keed ke atu afịd udịmedọñ a-ayọhọke ikie iba se ito idịm Isrel se enekke eduọk mmọọñ enọ. Mme ñkpọ ami ke ediikama inam mme uwa abakpa, ufọfọb uwa ye uwa adidiana keed se ekama enam ñkpeubọk enọ mbon awo, ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ. <verse eid="EZK 45:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 45:16" />Afịd awo ke idʌñ eyaenọ akpanabọọñ Isrel asaña-asaña enọ ami. <verse eid="EZK 45:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 45:17" />Adiido utom akpanabọọñ adinọ mme ufọfọb uwa, uwa mfịd ye adinwọñ uwa ke ini usọrọ ado, ke mme Ufa Afiọñ ye ke mme Sabad, ke afịd ndimek usọrọ ke Isrel. Anye adiinọ uwa idiọọkñkpọ, uwa mfịd, ufọfọb uwa ye uwa adidiana keed adinam ñkpeubọk nnọọ ufọk Isrel.<verse eid="EZK 45:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 45:18" />“ ‘Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: Ke akpa usen ke akpa afiọñ ndufo enie adidat ñyịn ayaaraenañ ammiinieghe ndo nnam adisana itie asana. <verse eid="EZK 45:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 45:19" />Aku anie adidat ubaak iyiib uwa idiọọkñkpọ afiọññọ ke abọbọọk anyenusʌñ tembịd ye ke naña mbañ anyọñ akpokoro uwa inaañ ye ke mme inuaatob esịd esa abọọñ. <verse eid="EZK 45:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 45:20" />Ana ndufo enam ukem ado ke ayọhọ usen itiaba ke afiọñ enọ awo akeedodo i-imiikifiọkkọfiọk inam idiọọkñkpọ me awo a-anamma ke unanaifiọk. Ke ntoro ana ndufo enam ñkpeubọk enọ tembịd.<verse eid="EZK 45:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 45:21" />“ ‘Ke ayọhọ usen duob mme inaañ ke akpa afiọñ ana ndufo enam Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo, usọrọ a-adiikpeene ke usen itiaba; ke idak ini ami ndufo ediita uyo se yiis imiisịneke. <verse eid="EZK 45:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 45:22" />Ke usen ado akpanabọọñ anie adinọ ayaaraenañ nte uwa idiọọkñkpọ anọ idem amọ ye afịd awo ke idʌñ. <verse eid="EZK 45:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 45:23" />Afịd usen ke atu usen itiaba ini usọrọ ado, anye anie adinọ ñyaaraenañ itiaba ye akukịmedọñ itiaba i-imiinieghe ndo nte ufọfọb uwa anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye akpoebod nte uwa idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="EZK 45:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 45:24" />Ana anye anọ efa keed a-adaaha anọ ayaaraenañ keedekeed ye efa keed a-adaaha anọ akukịmedọñ keedekeed asaña ye atu hin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45:24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte lita 3.8.</char></note> adan ọlif keed kwa efa nte uwa ñkpasi.<verse eid="EZK 45:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 45:25" />“ ‘Ke mme usen usọrọ itiaba ami, a-atọọñọke ke ayọhọ usen duob mme ition ke ayọhọ afiọñ itiaba, anye anie adinọ ukem enọ ado ke mme uwa idiọọkñkpọ, mme ufọfọb uwa, mme uwa ñkpasi ye adan.<verse eid="EZK 45:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 45" />
  <chapter number="46" style="c" sid="EZK 46" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 46:1" />“ ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Inuaatob esịd esa abọọñ a-awọttọ usakkautịn ana abebere ke mme usen unam utom itiokeed ado, ado amaado ke usen Sabad ye ke usen Ufa Afiọñ ana ebeere anye. <verse eid="EZK 46:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 46:2" />Akpanabọọñ ana ato esiin asaña esa usʌñ inuaatob anyʌñ akeda ke mben inuaatob. Mme aku enie ediwa ufọfọb uwa ye uwa ewuana amọ. Anye anie adisuuk iwuod ke ukpono ke itie ukọk abakpa ake inuaatob ndin anye asaña awuọ, ado inaaha ebet inuaatob tutu ndubiayio. <verse eid="EZK 46:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 46:3" />Ke mme usen Sabad ye mme Ufa Afiọñ mme awo ana nte ewọt ukpono ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ntondʌk inuaatob. <verse eid="EZK 46:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 46:4" />Adifọb uwa a-akpanabọọñ abenne asọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke usen Sabad adiido ñyịn akukịmedọñ itiokeed ye akukịmedọñ keed, afịd inaaha enie ndo. <verse eid="EZK 46:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 46:5" />Uwa ñkpasi e-ediinọ ye akukịmedọñ adiido udomo efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 16; se ñko ke Esi 46:7 ye 11.</char></note>, ñko uwa ñkpasi ye mme ñyịn edọñ adiiwak kpa naña anye ama, asaña ye atu hin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte lita 3.8; se ñko ke Esi 46:7 ye 11.</char></note> adan ọlif kwa efa. <verse eid="EZK 46:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 46:6" />Ke usen Ufa Afiọñ anye ana awa ñyịn ayaaraenañ, akukịmedọñ itiokeed ye ñyịn edọñ keed, ana afịd enana ndo. <verse eid="EZK 46:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 46:7" />Anye anie adinọ nte uwa ñkpasi efa keed adian ye ayaaraenañ ado, efa keed adian ye akukịmedọñ ado, dian ye uwak ñyịn edọñ naña anye ayem inọ, esaña ye atu adan ọlif ke efa keedekeed. <verse eid="EZK 46:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 46:8" />Ke ini akpanabọọñ ado adʌkkọ, anye anie adisaña esa usʌñ inuaatob, ñko anye anie adisaña ukem usʌñ ado ñwuọ.<verse eid="EZK 46:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 46:9" />“ ‘Ke ini nditọ isọñ edʌkkọ ebịne <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ini usọrọ akemme, awo akeedodo a-atooho inuaatob adoro adʌk ana asaña inuaatob usuuk awuọ; ñko awo akeedodo a-atooho inuaatob usuuk adʌk ana asaña inuaatob adoro awuọ. Inaaha awo ndomokeed ato inuaatob a-anye akesañake adʌk awuọ, ado awo keedekeed ana asaña nsakiso inuaatob a-anye aketooho adʌk awuọ. <verse eid="EZK 46:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 46:10" />Akpanabọọñ ana aba ye ammọ, adʌk idaha ammọ edʌkkọ anyʌñ awuọ idaha ammọ ewuọhọ. <verse eid="EZK 46:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 46:11" />Ndin ke ini mme usọrọ ye ke ini ndia, uwa ñkpasi ana ado efa keed ye ayaaraenañ, efa keed ye akukịmedọñ, dian ye mme ñyịn edọñ naña anem anye esịd, ñkọrọ atu adan ọlif kwa efa.<verse eid="EZK 46:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 46:12" />“ ‘Ke ini akpanabọọñ anọọhọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enọ imaesịd, me ufọfọb uwa me uwa ewuana ana ebeere inuaatob a-awọttọ usakkautịn enọ anye. Anye ayaawa ufọfọb uwa me uwa adidiana keed amọ nte naña anye asinam ke usen Sabad. Ndin anye ayaawuọ; ñko anye amaawuọ, ana ebet inuaatob ado.<verse eid="EZK 46:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 46:13" />“ ‘Afịd usen afo anie adinọ edọñ isua keed ammiinieghe ndo nọ ekama enam ufọfọb uwa enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; afo adiinọ anye kwa ubakusen. <verse eid="EZK 46:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 46:14" />Kwa ubakusen afo ñko anie adidian uwa ñkpasi, e-edọñọke mbakka keed ke itie itiokeed efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 2.7.</char></note> ye ayọhọ atu hin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte lita 1.3.</char></note> adan ita e-ewuahake ye ndomuyo. Afo anie adinọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> uwa ñkpasi ami a-adooho nsi-nsi ewʌhọ. <verse eid="EZK 46:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 46:15" />Ke ntoro edọñ ado ye uwa ñkpasi ado ye adan ado ediisinọ kwa ubakusen se ekama enam nsi-nsi ufọfọb uwa.<verse eid="EZK 46:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 46:16" />“ ‘Ntom ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ: Adieke akpanabọọñ anọọhọ ayịn amọ awodeen enọ ato udeeme ñkpọ amọ, ado ñko adiido inie mme ubon amọ, ammọ ediidat ado inie nte udeeme ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 46:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 46:17" />Adieke anye anọọhọ keed ke atu nditọufọk amọ enọ ato udeeme ñkpọ amọ, ayịnufọk ado ana akama enọ ado tutu isua ubọkkọ amọ akem; ndin eyaemaana eyaak enọ ado enọ akpanabọọñ ado. Udeeme amọ ana anọ nditọ ideen amọ ikpọọñ; ado ake ammọ. <verse eid="EZK 46:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 46:18" />Inaaha abọọñ aben udeeme mbon abio ndomokeed, inaaha abịne ammọ asio akpọñ udeeme ammọ. Anye anie adisio udeeme ñkpọ amọ nnọọ nditọ ideen amọ, mbaak edidiañña mbon mmi ndomokeed ekpọñ inie ammọ.’ ”<verse eid="EZK 46:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 46:19" />Ndin awo ado amamben miin asaña ato usʌñ mben inuaatob e-esañake edʌk ndisana ubeed a-awọttọ usuuk, a-akenieghe mme aku, anyʌñ akeñwọt miin itie ke utịd usobutịn. <verse eid="EZK 46:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 46:20" />Anye amambo miin, “Itie ami ke ana mme aku eba etem uwa ndudue ye uwa idiọọkñkpọ enyʌñ esañ abakpa uwa, nọ etre adiben ammọ ndʌk esiin esa abọọñ ye adikinam mme awo esana.”<verse eid="EZK 46:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 46:21" />Anye ndin amamben miin akaa esiin esa abọọñ anyʌñ andat miin usʌñ akanna inuuk inaañ amọ, ndin kwa inuuk ami mmaakịt esa abọọñ mfen. <verse eid="EZK 46:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 46:22" />Ke inuuk inaañ esa abọọñ esiin ado esa abọọñ mfen emaedọñọ, udomo kubid aba ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid edịb mme duob ke ukpa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46:22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 70 ke unyọọñ ye ikpad 53 ke ukpa me ñkpọ nte mita 21 ke unyọọñ ye mita 16 ke ukpa.</char></note>; afịd ntək esa abọọñ esịd ado ekenie udomo keed. <verse eid="EZK 46:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 46:23" />Udịm ufọk utem ñkpọ e-enamma ke itiad amaaba akanna esa abọọñ inaañ ado, afịd emaenie itie usịññe nsʌñikañ e-ekebọppọ ekanna ufọk utem ñkpọ ado. <verse eid="EZK 46:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 46:24" />Anye amambo miin, “Itie utem ñkpọ mbon e-enamma utom ke tembịd mmi ediitem mme uwa mbon awo ado ami.”<verse eid="EZK 46:24" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 46" />
  <chapter number="47" style="c" sid="EZK 47" />
  <para style="s1">Inyañ Atọọñọke ke Tembịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 47:1" />Awo ado amamben miin atịmme adi inuaatob tembịd, do ke ami ñkekịt naña mmọọñ ato ke idakisọñ asaña usʌñ tembịd awọññọ aka ñkañ usakkautịn (sia tembịd akesak iso ase usakkautịn). Mmọọñ aketo idakisọñ usuuk tembịd, usuuk akpokoro uwa. <verse eid="EZK 47:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 47:2" />Anye ndin amamben miin awuọ ato inuaatob adoro anyʌñ amben asaña akanna esiin a-adatta akewuọ inuaatob esiin a-awọttọ usakkautịn, ñko mmọọñ akesʌk afeghe ato usuuk.<verse eid="EZK 47:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 47:3" />Ke ete ado amaakedakka adʌk usakkautịn ye udomo ñkpọ ke ubọk amọ, anye amaadomo udomo kubid tọsịn keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47:3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 1,700 me mita 530.</char></note> anyʌñ amben miin asaña ke mmọọñ a-aketreke awo ke itọñ ukod. <verse eid="EZK 47:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 47:4" />Anye amaamaana adomo kubid tọsịn keed mfen ndin anye amamben miin asaña ke mmọọñ a-akedọọhọ akesịm edọñ. Anye amaamaana adomo kubid tọsịn keed mfen ndin anye amamben miin asaña ke mmọọñ a-akedọọhọ adiñwuọ isịn. <verse eid="EZK 47:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 47:5" />Anye amaamaana adomo tọsịn keed mfen asio, ado idahami mmọọñ amaakappa inyañ a-ami ndiikikanna ñkaaña, sia adooho mmọọñ amaadọọk anyʌñ atəño akem se ewọk ewọk, inyañ a-awo ndomokeed imiikikanna ikaaña. <verse eid="EZK 47:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 47:6" />Anye amambịp miin abo, “Ayịn awo, afo amekịt ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 47:6">Ndin anye amaatịmme amben miin akaa mben inyañ ado. <verse eid="EZK 47:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 47:7" />Ke ini ami ñkewuọhọ do, ami mmaakịt uwak ibad eto ke mben inyañ naña mbeñ iba. <verse eid="EZK 47:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 47:8" />Anye amambo miin, “Mmọọñ ami afeghe aka ñkañ usakkautịn anyʌñ asọiyọ adʌk Araba, ke itie a-anye atooho adʌk Ikpaikpa Akpainyañ. Ke ini anye anwaññake idem adọñ ke akpainyañ ado, mmọọñ inʌñ akappa afọn. <verse eid="EZK 47:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 47:9" />Udịm mme aduuwem ñkpọ eyaedʌñ ke itie akeedodo a-mmọọñ ami afegheke. Mme uwak ibad iyak eyaeba, sia adooho mmọọñ ami afefeghe do anyʌñ anam mmọọñ inʌñ afọn; ke ntoro itie nte mmọọñ afeghe aka afịd ñkpọ eyaedʌñ. <verse eid="EZK 47:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 47:10" />Mme akọiyak eyaeda ke mben akpa ado; tọọñọ ke En Kedi tutu asịm En Eklaim itie ayaaba se esịn iyịre. Mme iyak ado ediido ke utọ ke utọ nte mme iyak e-ebaaha ke Inyañ Mediterenia. <verse eid="EZK 47:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 47:11" />Ado mme adeb ye mme akpʌk-akpʌk itie idiikappake ifọn; eyaeyaak ammọ enịm enọ inʌñ. <verse eid="EZK 47:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 47:12" />Mme eto mfịd ke utọ ke utọ eyaetịppe ke mben inyañ ado naña edem iba. Mfañ ammọ idiiyeemeke, ñko mfịd ammọ idiiduọhọ. Ammọ eyaenwịm mfịd kwa afiọñ sia adooho mmọọñ a-afegheke abịne ammọ ato adisana itie. Mfịd ammọ adiido ndidia, ñko mfañ ammọ adiido ibọk usọbọ.”<verse eid="EZK 47:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Adaña Isọñ ado</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 47:13" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ ado ami: “Mme adaña ikọd se afo uduudeeme unọ mme esiin Isrel duob mme iba nte udeeme ñkpọ ammọ edo ami, yak Yosef adat itie iba. <verse eid="EZK 47:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 47:14" />Afo anie adibakka ammọ ukem-ukem nnọọ ammọ. Sia ami mmaadịppe ubọk ñnwọñọ ke ñyaanọ mme eteete ndufo; isọñ ami adiido udeeme ndufo.”<verse eid="EZK 47:14" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="li4">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 47:15" />Adaña isọñ ado ado ami:</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 47:15" />
  <para style="li1" vid="EZK 47:15">Ke ubeñ adoro anye adiitọọñọ ke Akpainyañ Mediterenia ke mben usʌñ Hetlọn aboiyo Debo Hamad tutu ke Sedad, <verse eid="EZK 47:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 47:16" />Berota ye Sibraim (a-adaaha ke ufọọd adaña Damaskọs ye Hamad), anyọọñ akesịm Hasa Hatikon, a-abaaha ke ufọọd adaña Hauran. <verse eid="EZK 47:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 47:17" />Adaña ado ayaatara atọọñọ ke inyañ ado akesịm Hasa Enan, tutu ke edem adoro ufọọd adaña Damaskọs, ye ufọọd adaña Hamad ke adoro. Adaña adoro adiido ami.<verse eid="EZK 47:17" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 47:18" />Ke ñkañ usakkautịn adaña adiitọọñọ ke Hauran ye Damaskọs, asaña Yọdan ke ufọọd Kilied ye isọñ Isrel, tutu akesịm Ikpaikpa Akpainyañ ndin anye anyọọñ akewuọ Tama. Ami adiido adaña ñkañ usakkautịn.<verse eid="EZK 47:18" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 47:19" />Ke ukañ usuuk adaña adiitọọñọ ke Tama tutu akesịm mme mmọọñ Meriba Kades, afrọ ke Wadi ke Iyib tutu asịm Akpainyañ Mediterenia. Ami adiido adaña usuuk.<verse eid="EZK 47:19" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 47:20" />Ke ukañ usobutịn, Akpainyañ Mediterenia adiido adaña tutu ke itie a-asakkaiso ase Lebo Hamad. Ami adiido adaña ñkañ usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 47:20" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 47:21" />“Ndufo enie edideeme isọñ ami ke atu ndufo ekeene mme esiin Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 47:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 47:22" />Ndufo enie edideeme isọñ ami nnọọ idem ndufo ye mme isenawo e-edʌññọ ke atu ndufo e-enyʌññọ enie nditọ. Ndufo enie edidat ammọ nte mme amanaisọñ ke Isrel; enie edideeme isọñ nnọọ ammọ nte udeeme ke atu mme esiin Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 47:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 47:23" />Ke esiin akeedodo a-asenawo adʌññọ, ndufo enie adinọ ammọ udeeme ammọ,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 47:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 47" />
  <chapter number="48" style="c" sid="EZK 48" />
  <para style="s1">Udeeme Isọñ</para>
  <para style="li4">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 48:1" />Mbon ami edo mme esiin Isrel, e-esiaha ke anyịñ:</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 48:1" />
  <para style="li1" vid="EZK 48:1">“Ke ukañ adoro, Daan adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiikeene usʌñ Hetlọn akesịm Lebo Hamad; Hasa Enan ye adaña adoro Damaskọs a-adianake Hamad adiisịne ke atu adaña amọ tọọñọ ke ukañ usakkautịn tutu ke ukañ usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:1" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 48:2" />Asaa adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke ñkañ Daan tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:2" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 48:3" />Naftali adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke ñkañ Asaa tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:3" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 48:4" />Manase adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke ñkañ Naftali tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:4" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 48:5" />Ifrem adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke ñkañ Manase tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:5" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 48:6" />Rubịn adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke ñkañ Ifrem tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:6" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 48:7" />Yuda adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke ñkañ Rubịn tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:7" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 48:8" />“Adaña ñkañ Yuda tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn adiido mbakka a-afo anieghe adinọ nte asaña-asaña enọ. Anye adiido kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48:8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 8 me kilomita 13; se ñko ke Esi 48:9, 10, 13, 15, 20 ye 21.</char></note> ke ukpa, ñko unyọọñ amọ tọọñọ ke usakkautịn kesịm usobutịn adiido ukem ye mbakka keed ake esiin Isrel; adisana itie adiiba ke ufọọd amọ.<verse eid="EZK 48:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 48:9" />“Asaña-asaña mbakka a-anaaha nte afo anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adiido udomo kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ ye udomo kubid tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ukpa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48:9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 3 1/3 me ñkpọ nte kilomita 5.3; se ñko ke Esi 48:10, 13 ye 18.</char></note>. <verse eid="EZK 48:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 48:10" />Anyem adiido adisana mbakka enọ mme aku. Anye adiido udomo kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ ke adoro, udomo kubid tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ukpa ke edem usobutịn, udomo tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ukpa ke usakkautịn ye udomo tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ ke usuuk. Ke ufọọd amọ adisana itie <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adiiba. <verse eid="EZK 48:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 48:11" />Ami adiina inọ mme aku e-eyette adan, mbon Sadọk, e-ekenamma akpanikọ ke edinam ñkpọ innọọ miin, i-imiikinyʌññọ iwuọ ikpọñ usʌñ nte mbon Lifai ekenamma ke ini nditọ Isrel ekewuọhọ ekpọñ usʌñ. <verse eid="EZK 48:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 48:12" />Anye adiido asaña-asaña enọ e-enọọhọ ammọ eto mbakka adisana isọñ, ataa adisana mbakka, a-adiaññake adaña ye ñkañ mme Lifai.<verse eid="EZK 48:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 48:13" />“Ke mbeñ ñkañ mme aku, mme Lifai ediinie udeeme udomo kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ ye kubid tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ukpa. Afịd unyọọñ amọ adiido kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ ye kubid tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ukpa. <verse eid="EZK 48:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 48:14" />Ammọ inaaha enyam me ekpəho mbakka ammọ ndomokeed. Anyem ado isọñ a-afọnnọ akan ndin inaaha enyam nọ awuọ adʌk mbon mfen ubọk, sia anye ado adisana anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>”<verse eid="EZK 48:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 48:15" />Ñyọhọnsʌhọ isọñ ado, a-adooho kubid tọsịn ition (5,000)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48:15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 1 2/3 me ñkpọ nte kilomita 2.7.</char></note> ke ukpa ye kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke unyọọñ, adiina inọ se afịd abio ekama, se ebọp ufọk ye se ekama etọ mbid enọ ufene. Abio adiisịne ke ufọọd amọ <verse eid="EZK 48:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 48:16" />ndin anye adiinie udomo ami: ke adoro udomo kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition (4,500)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 1 1/2 me kilomita 2.4; se ñko ke Esi 48:30, 32, 33 ye 34.</char></note>, ke usuuk kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition, ke usakkautịn kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition (4,500), ke usobutịn kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition (4,500). <verse eid="EZK 48:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 48:17" />Ndin anwa mbid a-anaaha anọ abio adiido kubid ikie iba mme aba mme duob (250)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48:17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 440 me mita 135.</char></note> ke ñkañ adoro, kubid ikie iba mme aba mme duob (250) ke ñkañ usuuk, kubid ikie iba mme aba mme duob (250) ke ñkañ usakkautịn ye kubid ikie iba mme aba mme duob (250) ke ñkañ usobutịn. <verse eid="EZK 48:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 48:18" />Se idiiyọhọ isʌhọ ke ukpa ado, a-adiaññake adaña ye adisana mbakka anyʌññọ asaña ke unyọọñ amọ, adiido udomo kubid tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ñkañ usakkautịn ye kubid tọsịn duob (10,000) ke ñkañ usobutịn. Eyaekama mbunwịm amọ enọ mme anam utom ke abio ndidia. <verse eid="EZK 48:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 48:19" />Mme anamutom e-etooho esịd abio etọ inwañ do ediito afịd esiin Isrel. <verse eid="EZK 48:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 48:20" />Afịd mbakka ado adiido ukem ke naña mbeñ inaañ, adiido udomo kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke afịd mbeñ. Nte asaña-asaña enọ, afo anie adisio adisana udeeme ado, adian ye inie mbon abio. <verse eid="EZK 48:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 48:21" />“Se iyọhọ isʌhọ ke naña ñkañ iba a-atooho adisana ubaak itie ye inie abio adiinie akpanabọọñ. Anye ayaatọñọ ke adisana itie mbakka kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ke ñkañ usakkautịn akaa adaña ñkañ usakkautịn, anyʌñ ato ke mbakka kubid tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) akaa ke adaña ñkañ usobutịn. Naña ubeñ iba ñkañ a-anyọọñọ aka ñkañ idịd adiido udeeme akpanabọọñ, ndin ufọọd ammọ adiido adisana itie tembịd.” <verse eid="EZK 48:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 48:22" />Ke ntoro udeeme mme Lifai ye udeeme abio adiisịne ke ufọọd ikpeghe a-anieghe akpanabọọñ. Ukañ a-anieghe akpanabọọñ adiiba ke ufọọd adaña Yuda ye adaña Benyamin.<verse eid="EZK 48:22" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="li4">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 48:23" />“Amaado mme esiin mfen esʌhọke:</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 48:23" />
  <para style="li1" vid="EZK 48:23">“Benyamin adiinie mbakka keed; anye ayaatara tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:23" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 48:24" />Simiọn adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ye mbeñ Benyamin tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:24" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 48:25" />Isaka adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke mbeñ Simiọn tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:25" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 48:26" />Sebulọn adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña ye mbeñ Isaka tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:26" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 48:27" />Kad adiinie mbakka keed; anye adiidiañña adaña ke mbeñ Sebulọn tọọñọ ke usakkautịn tutu ke usobutịn.<verse eid="EZK 48:27" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 48:28" />Kad adiinie adaña ñkañ usuuk-usuuk asaña ke ñkañ usuuk tọọñọ ke Tama tutu ke mme mmọọñ Meriba Kades, ndin ke ñkañ Wadi ke Iyib tutu ke Akpainyañ Mediterenia.<verse eid="EZK 48:28" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="li4">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 48:29" />“Isọñ ami ke ana nte afo adeeme nte udeeme inie anọ mme esiin Isrel, ñko se idiido ubakka amọ ado ami,” ami ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara atañ.<verse eid="EZK 48:29" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Inuaatob Ufa Abio</para>
  <para style="li4">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 48:30" />“Mme usʌñ se ediisaña iwuọ ke abio edo ami:</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 48:30" />
  <para style="li1" vid="EZK 48:30">“Tọọñọ ke adoro, a-adooho udomo kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition (4,500), <verse eid="EZK 48:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 48:31" />ediikoot mme inuaatob abio ado idian mme esiin Isrel. Inuaatob ita ke adoro adiido inuaatob Rubịn, inuaatob Yuda ye inuaatob Lifai.<verse eid="EZK 48:31" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 48:32" />Ke ñkañ usakkautịn, a-adooho udomo kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition (4,500) ke unyọọñ adiido inuaatob ita: Inuaatob Yosef, inuaatob Benyamin ye inuaatob Daan.<verse eid="EZK 48:32" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 48:33" />Inuaatob ita adiiba ke ñkañ usuuk, a-adooho udomo kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition (4,500): Inuaatob Simiọn, inuaatob Isaka ye inuaatob Sebulọn.<verse eid="EZK 48:33" /></para>
  <para style="li1">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 48:34" />Inuaatob ita ediiba ke ñkañ usobutịn, a-adooho udomo kubid tọsịn inaañ mme ikie ition (4,500): Ammọ edo inuaatob Kad, inuaatob Asaa ye inuaatob Naftali.<verse eid="EZK 48:34" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="li4">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 48:35" />“Unyọọñ afịd ñkanñkʌk amọ adiido udomo kubid tọsịn duob mme itiaita (18,000)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48:35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte itiad 6 me ñkpọ nte kilomita 9.5.</char></note>.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="EZK 48:35" />
  <para style="p" vid="EZK 48:35">“Ndin anyịñ abio ado tọọñọ ke usen ado kaa iso adiido, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmọaba do,”<verse eid="EZK 48:35" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EZK 48" />
</usx>